    doc /* The compiler platform shall function strictly as an abstract Model-Based Systems Engineering (MBSE) compiler, deriving all synthesized intermediate representations, verification models, downstream specification projections, and interface definitions deterministically from user-provided schema inputs. The compiler must operate exclusively on generic systems engineering metamodel primitives: Classifiers, Feature Usages, Abstract Ports, Directional Connectors, Mathematical Constraints, Discrete State Transitions, and Occurrence Lifecycles. Compilation passes, lowering pipelines, code generators, and autonomous tooling agents are strictly prohibited from hardcoding, injecting, or assuming domain-specific concepts, domain vocabularies, or heuristic domain assumptions into pipeline logic, templates, intermediate representations, or emitted artifacts. All illustrative examples, test fixtures, and internal representations shall utilize purely synthetic abstract placeholders (e.g., `Package_0`, `Classifier_Alpha`, `Port_1`, `Flow_A`, `param_x : Real`). When synthetic structural identifiers or topological anchors are generated for intermediate representations or scaffolding nodes, they shall be deterministically derived via RFC 4122 UUIDv5 namespace hashing rooted in a fixed compiler namespace UUID constant ($``\text{NS}_{\text{DEAP}}``$) and the fully qualified topological path of the element within the abstract syntax tree containment hierarchy. If any compilation stage detects an ungrounded domain term or non-schema symbol outside the formal grammar vocabulary and synthetic anchor set, the compiler shall halt execution immediately and emit diagnostic error code `E0100`. ---
                      The compiler platform shall enforce a strict, surjective lexical provenance gate across all synthesized abstract syntax tree (AST) elements. Every generated classifier, feature usage, port, connector, attribute, constraint, behavior, action, and state identifier shall establish a verifiable derivation link back to either a corresponding AST node within parsed schema source files or a deterministic synthetic topological parent anchor. Generation of ungrounded, fabricated, or hallucinated structural entities is strictly prohibited across all lowering, transformation, optimization, and code generation passes. Each synthesized AST node must maintain an immutable provenance descriptor recording: 1. Originating source file identifier, 2. Physical source byte span ($`\text{ByteStart}`$ and $`\text{ByteEnd}`$ offsets), 3. Line and column coordinates, and 4. Parent AST node handle. When intermediate scaffolding nodes (such as implicit root namespaces or structural containment boundaries) are synthetically generated, the compiler shall derive their provenance anchors deterministically via RFC 4122 UUIDv5 hashing seeded by a fixed namespace OID and the node fully qualified topological path. The compiler shall verify surjective range completeness across all parsed schema source nodes, ensuring that zero user-defined structural entities are omitted during lowering. The provenance gate must execute as a mandatory verification pass immediately following schema ingestion and AST construction, failing closed upon any provenance violation. ---
                      The compiler pipeline shall guarantee bitwise deterministic artifact emission across repeated invocations on identical input schemas, producing bit-for-bit identical outputs. The pipeline must eliminate all sources of entropy and platform variance: hash iteration orders, thread scheduling interleavings, host-specific absolute paths, system timestamps, and pseudorandom seeds. All symbol tables, maps, and registries shall enforce deterministic iteration orders via canonical key sorting prior to serialization. Emission pipelines shall normalize line endings to Unix LF (`0x0A`), prohibit timestamp injection, and generate synthetic identifiers exclusively via deterministic RFC 4122 UUIDv5 hashing. Bounded work-stealing worker threads ($``N_{\text{max\_workers}}``$) shall preserve identical output ordering. When emitting artifacts, the compiler shall verify in-memory byte streams against existing on-disk files; unchanged files shall bypass filesystem writes, preserving timestamps and eliminating diff churn. Any non-deterministic output divergence on identical inputs shall fail compilation and emit diagnostic error code `E0100`. ---
                      The compiler platform shall operate in a self-contained, sovereign repository architecture wherein all filesystem operations, cross-module schema imports, configuration lookups, and generated artifact paths resolve dynamically using canonical workspace-relative paths derived from an authenticated repository root. The compiler must discover workspace root $`\mathcal{R}`$ dynamically at runtime by searching parent directories upward from the current working directory for the nearest sovereign repository marker, or by accepting an explicit root path supplied via command-line arguments. All path resolution operations shall strictly enforce boundary containment: every resolved path must reside within the directory subtree rooted at $`\mathcal{R}`$. The compiler shall strictly reject any path reference attempting directory traversal outside $`\mathcal{R}`$ (including parent traversal sequences `..`, absolute filesystem paths, drive letter prefixes, user home expansions, external symbolic links, and network URIs). Upon detecting an out-of-bounds or invalid path, the compiler shall halt execution and emit diagnostic error code `E0100`. The compiler shall guarantee bitwise determinism and zero environment leakage: all synthesized intermediate representations, ASTs, and output artifacts must be bit-for-bit identical regardless of the absolute mount path of $`\mathcal{R}`$ on disk. Absolute machine paths, usernames, hostnames, or build-environment paths are strictly forbidden from appearing in generated outputs. ---
                      The compiler platform shall execute as an autonomous, self-contained compiler binary that operates independently of host environment configuration, external service daemons, network connectivity, or implicit ambient filesystem state. The compiler must not require external language runtimes, dynamic linkers to non-standard host libraries, container runtime daemons, or background helper processes during any compilation phase. The compiler shall isolate its execution from ambient host environment variables, user identity (UID/GID and username), host locale, timezone, hostname, and global filesystem paths situated outside the designated sovereign workspace root. All core metamodels, standard libraries (such as `Base`, `Collections`, and primitive scalar definitions), and diagnostic templates necessary for bootstrapping must be embedded directly into the compiler binary image or resolved exclusively via workspace-relative paths. The compiler shall enforce absolute network isolation. Compilation passes shall never initiate outbound network connections, bind or listen on inbound network sockets, execute remote procedure calls, or issue DNS queries. Any attempt by a compilation pass or lowering step to access network sockets, read unwhitelisted environment variables, or read/write filesystem paths outside the sovereign workspace boundary shall be rejected as an invariant violation, causing the compiler to halt execution immediately and emit diagnostic error code `E0100`. ---
                      The compiler platform shall maintain fine-grained dependency tracking across all modular compilation units within an explicit compilation unit dependency directed acyclic graph (DAG). The incremental compilation subsystem must compute deterministic cryptographic content digests for each input compilation unit upon ingestion. When input schema compilation units are modified, added, or removed, the compiler shall identify the mutated seed set $`M`$ and compute the exact forward reachability closure across the dependency DAG. The compiler must invalidate and recompute strictly the AST subgraphs, symbol tables, and lowering artifacts belonging to this transitively affected closure. All unaffected compilation units outside the transitive invalidation set shall be reused directly from the compiler AST cache without disk re-reads, re-lexing, or re-parsing. The synthesized composite AST resulting from incremental recomputation shall be bitwise and structurally equivalent to the AST produced by clean compilation from scratch, exhibiting zero diff churn in emitted Merkle roots. If an unresolvable dependency cycle, invalidation fault, or corrupted cache record occurs, the compiler shall reject the invalid state, invalidate the affected cache partition, and emit diagnostic error code `E0100` detailing the affected unit identifier, dependency coordinates, and source byte spans. ---
                      The compiler architecture shall resolve multi-file compilation units and enforce hierarchical package scoping across modular schema libraries without cross-module symbol collision or namespace pollution. Each compilation unit ingested from the workspace shall bind to a hierarchical package namespace matching its declared package path. The compiler must construct a global package forest where each package possesses a unique fully qualified name (FQN) joined by `::`. Symbol visibility and lexical scoping rules shall govern identifier resolution: 1. **Local Precedence**: Local declarations in a package scope shadow imported symbols and outer ancestor declarations. 2. **Ancestor Traversal**: Unqualified symbols not declared locally resolve along ascending parent lexical scopes up to the package root. 3. **Explicit Imports**: External symbols require explicit qualified paths (e.g., `Package_0::Package_1::Classifier_Alpha`) or unambiguous import bindings. 4. **Disjoint Namespaces**: Distinct packages maintain disjoint qualified namespaces; identical local identifiers in distinct packages remain isolated without collision. 5. **Ambiguity Rejection**: Unqualified references matching multiple imported candidates must be rejected as ambiguous. 6. **Nesting Depth Bound**: Package hierarchy nesting depth is strictly bounded by $``D_{\max} = 16``$. Failure modes--conflicting declarations within a scope, unresolvable package paths, cyclic imports, depth violations ($`D \gt 16`$), and ambiguous references--shall halt compilation and emit diagnostic error code `E0100` with unit coordinates and source byte spans. ---
                      The compiler platform shall establish and maintain the unified, multi-file SysML v2 / KerML Abstract Syntax Tree (AST) synthesized from modular schemas in the `schema/` directory as the sovereign Single Source of Truth (SSOT) for all architectural structures, interfaces, and constraints across the compilation lifecycle. Downstream representations--including Epics, Features, Interface Control Documents (ICDs), simulation models, and target source code--shall function strictly as deterministic, pure mathematical projections of this authoritative AST. Downstream artifacts are prohibited from acting as independent sources of truth or introducing unauthorized architectural mutations. Every entity within the central AST model shall be deterministically anchored by an RFC 4122 UUIDv5 identifier computed from fixed compiler namespace OID $``\text{NS}_{\text{DEAP}}``$ and the entity's fully qualified topological path. When downstream artifacts are parsed or evaluated during compilation or synchronization passes, automated bidirectional reconciliation gates shall compare on-disk artifacts against authoritative AST projections. If structural discrepancy or uncoordinated modification is detected, the central AST model unconditionally governs. If irreconcilable structural divergence or downstream entity invention occurs without corresponding upstream schema modification, the compiler shall halt execution and emit diagnostic error code `E0100` detailing the offending artifact path, diverging node identifier, expected AST projection digest, and observed downstream content. ---
                      The compiler front-end, lexical analyzer, parser, and core abstract syntax tree (AST) engine shall utilize zero-copy memory management via contiguous bump allocation arenas for all parsed AST nodes, token streams, syntax trees, and intermediate representation graphs. Lexical tokens and string identifiers representing slices of source text shall directly borrow contiguous byte slice references from read-only memory-mapped source file buffers without intermediate heap string allocations or dynamic buffer cloning. Bump arenas must allocate AST nodes sequentially along contiguous memory segments, advancing a monotonic bump pointer with strict 64-bit data alignment boundaries (8-byte alignment). Arena lifecycle management must reset or deallocate entire arena chunks in a single bulk operation upon completion of compilation units or compilation phases, eliminating individual node deallocation overhead, per-node allocator metadata headers, and heap fragmentation. Memory allocation during lexical and parsing passes shall strictly enforce zero individual heap allocations for AST nodes and token strings. Copying string bytes from the source buffer into the deduplicated global symbol interner pool for scalar symbol identifier tokens during the initial lexical pass constitutes the sole permitted exception to the zero-copy invariant, as specified in REQ-0036. If an arena segment exhausts pre-allocated capacity, the arena manager shall allocate a new contiguous chunk without moving, reallocating, or invalidating previously allocated node references. If an allocation exceeds segment capacity without memory availability, or an out-of-bounds slice is accessed, or an unauthorized heap allocation occurs during parsing, the compiler shall halt execution immediately and emit diagnostic error code `E0100`. ---
                      The compiler platform shall generate all synthetic entity identifiers, specification document anchors (Epics, Features, User Stories, Use Cases), intermediate representation node handles, and downstream artifact keys exclusively via deterministic RFC 4122 UUIDv5 namespace hashing. In accordance with Architectural Directive 1, time-based UUIDs (UUIDv1, UUIDv6, UUIDv7) and pseudo-random UUIDs (UUIDv4) are strictly prohibited across all passes to eliminate entropy injection and preserve bitwise reproducibility and Merkle root digests. The hashing engine shall accept a fixed compiler namespace UUID constant ($``\text{NS}_{\text{DEAP}}``$) and the canonical fully qualified topological path string ($``\mathcal{N}_{\text{topological}}``$) of the target AST entity (e.g., `Package_0::Subsystem_Alpha::Classifier_Beta`). Canonical topological paths must strictly use uniform scope delimiters (`::`), case-sensitive ASCII representation, and abstract entity naming without host-dependent filesystem path prefixes, mount roots, or process descriptors. The UUIDv5 engine shall compute the SHA-1 digest over the big-endian concatenation of the 16 namespace octets and the UTF-8 encoded canonical path string. The resulting 160-bit digest shall be truncated to 16 octets, setting version bits to $``0101_2``$ (Version 5, octet 6) and variant bits to $``10_2``$ (RFC 4122 variant, octet 8). Emitted strings shall conform to the canonical 36-character hyphenated lowercase hexadecimal format (`8-4-4-4-12`). Identifiers must remain strictly invariant across execution environments, CPU architectures, endianness, host operating systems, filesystem mount points, thread allocations in the bounded work-stealing pool, and physical build timestamps. On detection of an invalid path, host path prefix, hash collision, or non-deterministic UUID, the compiler shall halt execution immediately and emit diagnostic error code `E0100`. ---
                      Production compiler library code and release executable binaries shall strictly enforce a deterministic, non-panicking execution contract with guaranteed total-function termination on all valid, invalid, truncated, malformed, and adversarial schema inputs. The compiler platform must strictly eliminate all unhandled runtime panics, stack overflow conditions, unhandled exceptions, abnormal aborts, unchecked arithmetic faults, and fatal signal terminations (including `SIGABRT`, `SIGSEGV`, and `SIGILL`). All internal failure states--including lexical errors, syntactic malformations, unresolved symbol references, cyclic dependencies, physical unit inconsistencies, and metamodel invariant violations--shall be captured deterministically and propagated through structured diagnostic error collections adhering to standardized diagnostic codes (`E01xx` through `E05xx`, with baseline invariant violations bound to `E0100`). The compiler pipeline shall bound total execution latency in optimized release configurations for baseline models containing up to $``N_{\max} = 10{,}000``$ abstract syntax tree (AST) nodes to strictly under 25 milliseconds ($``\Delta t \le T_{\max} = 25\text{ ms}``$). In accordance with Architectural Directive 5, execution latency bounds ($``T_{\max} = 25\text{ ms}``$) and memory consumption thresholds shall be evaluated exclusively in compiled Release mode (`--release`) via dedicated benchmark harnesses, completely isolated from standard continuous integration (CI) functional logic tests. Any unhandled panic, abnormal process termination, or release latency threshold breach shall halt the pipeline or benchmark harness and emit diagnostic error code `E0100`. ---
                      All concurrent compilation operations--including parallel schema ingestion, multi-file AST parsing, graph traversals, STPA Cartesian product hazard tensor expansions, temporal reachability evaluations, and downstream artifact code generation--shall execute exclusively through a bounded work-stealing thread pool. Parallel task execution must be strictly bounded by an upper worker limit $``N_{\text{workers}} = \min(C_{\text{logical}}, N_{\text{max\_workers}})``$, where $``C_{\text{logical}} \in \mathbb{N}_{\ge 1}``$ is the detected host logical CPU core count and $``N_{\text{max\_workers}} \in \mathbb{N}_{\ge 1}``$ is a configurable runtime worker ceiling. The compiler runtime shall strictly prohibit unbounded, ad-hoc, or manual operating system thread creation. Worker threads must operate in complete memory isolation without shared mutable state across thread boundaries. Concurrent worker tasks shall access shared compiler structures exclusively via immutable references or frozen AST views. All task-local mutations and intermediate state synthesis must remain confined to thread-local memory regions or task-private accumulators. Parallel reductions and multi-threaded aggregations must enforce deterministic combination ordering such that thread scheduling interleavings never induce non-deterministic AST mutations or artifact diff churn. If any compiler component attempts to spawn an unmanaged thread, if worker thread allocation exceeds $``N_{\text{max\_workers}}``$, or if concurrent data race or shared mutable state violations are detected, the compiler shall halt execution immediately and emit diagnostic error code `E0100`. ---
                      All front-end schema and language parsers--including CommonMark tabular schema parsers, KerML and SysML v2 grammar parsers, Protocol Buffer parsers, IDL parsers, and structural ADL parsers--shall implement Synchronization Token Error Recovery in accordance with Directive 4. Front-end parsers must never abort compilation on the first encountered syntax error, lexical fault, or delimiter mismatch. Instead, upon detecting a syntax fault, the parser shall construct a structured diagnostic, discard invalid tokens up to the nearest synchronization boundary $``\mathcal{T}_{\text{sync}}``$, unwind the parser stack to an enclosing synchronizing production, and resume parsing to accumulate multiple localized diagnostics in a single pass. Recovery operations must execute under a deterministic, non-panicking contract with zero unhandled exceptions. The engine shall enforce strictly monotonic forward stream progress ($``\text{StreamPosition}_{t+1} \gt \text{StreamPosition}_t``$) on every recovery transition to eliminate livelocks and infinite loops. To eliminate realignment noise, the parser shall enforce cascading error suppression, suppressing secondary diagnostics detected within proximity window $`\delta \le 3`$ tokens following a synchronization event. Diagnostic accumulation shall enforce a configurable bounded capacity ceiling $``C_{\text{max\_errors}}``$ per compilation unit; upon reaching $``C_{\text{max\_errors}}``$, the parser shall gracefully conclude the pass and emit diagnostic code `E0199`. All syntax diagnostics shall bind 1-indexed source span coordinates within range `E0100`--`E0199` per REQ-0191. ---
                      The compiler ingestion engine shall classify input schema files into target schema formats using file extensions and deterministic content prefix signatures across 5 supported formats: CommonMark Markdown tables (`.md`, `.markdown`), Protocol Buffers (`.proto`), OMG IDL (`.idl`), OpenAPI schemas (`.json`, `.yaml`, `.yml`), and XML Schema Definitions (`.xml`, `.xsd`). Detection shall evaluate canonical lowercase file extensions followed by an initial bounded prefix window $`\text{head}(F, K)`$ of at most $`K = 512`$ bytes using deterministic scalar byte matching. Classification must execute strictly without regular expressions ($`\text{RegexEvaluations} = 0`$) or exploratory backtracking ($`\text{BacktrackCount} = 0`$). If a file cannot be classified or exhibits an unrecognized, corrupt, or contradictory signature, the engine shall classify it as `Unknown` and emit structured diagnostic `E0100`., the engine shall implement synchronization recovery, recording the diagnostic and proceeding to subsequent compilation units to accumulate all diagnostics without aborting prematurely. ---
                      The ingestion engine shall parse CommonMark Markdown tables containing component declarations, interfaces, attributes, and constraints using an explicit deterministic pushdown automaton (DPDA) that emits an event stream of structural tokens. Lexing and tokenization must strictly prohibit regular expressions and catastrophic backtracking. Front-end table ingestion passes shall operate directly on contiguous UTF-8 byte streams, executing scalar byte-matching transitions to classify cell boundaries, row terminators, header delimiters, and escaped literal sequences. Token emissions must occur on-the-fly via a streaming event sink interface, delivering structured token events without materializing intermediate syntax trees or buffering unneeded file contents in memory. Every emitted token event shall capture exact source provenance, including 0-indexed byte offset intervals and 1-indexed line and column coordinates. The lexer shall enforce an explicit bounded frame stack with maximum nesting depth $`D \le 4`$, rejecting deeper nesting or unclosed frames deterministically with diagnostic code `E0100` or `E0102`. Lexer execution shall follow a total, non-panicking execution contract with deterministic error emission upon encountering invalid byte encodings or structural anomalies. In accordance with synchronization token error recovery on table delimiter boundaries, when encountering unexpected tokens or malformed cells, the lexer shall emit diagnostic `E0102`, resynchronize to the next column delimiter pipe or newline boundary, and continue processing subsequent cells and rows without crashing or abandoning the compilation unit. ---
                      The CommonMark table parser within the Universal Schema Ingestion Engine shall implement Synchronization Token Error Recovery on table delimiter boundaries per Architectural Directive 4. When encountering unexpected formatting, unescaped pipe characters, malformed scalar literals, or delimiter mismatches within cell $``C_{i, j}``$ of row $``R_i``$, the parser must record a localized diagnostic and resynchronize at the nearest synchronization token boundary without aborting compilation or discarding unaffected cells and rows. The table synchronization token set comprises column delimiter pipes (`|`, $``\text{SYM}_{\text{PIPE}}``$), record line breaks ($``\text{SYM}_{\text{LF}}``$), and end-of-file ($``t_{\text{EOF}}``$). Upon detecting a cell fault, the parser shall construct a structured diagnostic binding error code `E0102` per REQ-0191 with 1-indexed line and column coordinates, byte span $``[p_{\text{start}}, p_{\text{end}})``$, the offending token slice, and expected grammar production. The parser shall advance the stream pointer monotonically forward to the nearest synchronization token, discard invalid tokens, substitute a typed error sentinel $``\bot_{\text{cell}}``$ into row $``R_i``$, preserve valid preceding cells $``C_{i, 1}, \dots, C_{i, j-1}``$, and resume parsing at cell $``C_{i, j+1}``$ (on pipe) or row $``R_{i+1}``$ (on line break). The parser shall enforce a total, deterministic, non-panicking execution contract across all inputs. Monotonic forward stream progress ($``\text{ByteOffset}_{t+1} \gt \text{ByteOffset}_t``$) must hold on every recovery transition to eliminate livelocks. The parser shall apply cascading error suppression, suppressing secondary diagnostics detected within proximity window $`\delta \le 3`$ tokens following a synchronization event. Diagnostic accumulation shall enforce a configurable bounded capacity ceiling $``C_{\text{max\_errors}}``$ per compilation unit; upon saturation, the parser shall terminate table ingestion and emit diagnostic code `E0199`. ---
                      The CommonMark tabular schema parser within the Universal Schema Ingestion Engine shall implement dynamic semantic header key normalization and order-independent column binding for all tabular model specifications. The parser shall accept column headers in arbitrary horizontal order and normalize each raw header string $`H`$ into a canonical attribute key $``k \in \mathcal{K}_{\text{canonical}}``$ via a deterministic four-stage pipeline: (1) ASCII whitespace trimming, (2) ASCII case folding, (3) punctuation stripping and whitespace collapse, and (4) alias lookup against immutable catalog $``\mathcal{K}_{\text{canonical}}``$. The engine shall construct binding vector $``\vec{\beta} \in (\mathcal{K}_{\text{canonical}} \cup \{ \bot \})^C``$ for column count $``C \le C_{\text{max\_cols}} = 32``$. Data rows shall be projected positionally through $`\vec{\beta}`$, ensuring any column permutation $``\pi \in \mathfrak{S}_C``$ synthesizes an AST entity identical to the unpermuted schema. Execution shall be deterministic and non-panicking. Header resolution must enforce injective column assignment: duplicate collisions or ambiguous bindings shall emit diagnostic `E0102` and engage synchronization token recovery per REQ-0016. If mandatory attribute set $``\mathcal{M} \subseteq \mathcal{K}_{\text{canonical}}``$ is not fully covered by $`\vec{\beta}`$, or if strict validation encounters an unrecognized header ($`\beta(H) = \bot`$), the parser shall emit diagnostic `E0102`. Tables exceeding column ceiling $``C \gt C_{\text{max\_cols}} = 32``$ shall be rejected with diagnostic `E0102`. ---
                      The CommonMark table parser within the Universal Schema Ingestion Engine shall preserve multi-line cell content, nested bullet points, list items, and inline code spans within table cells without dropping formatting, truncating text, or losing structural hierarchy. The engine must normalize embedded HTML line break variants (`<br>`, `<br/>`, `<br />`, `<BR>`, `<BR/>`, `<BR />`) and escaped linefeeds (`\n`, `\r\n`) into canonical newline block tokens ($``\text{SYM}_{\text{LF}}``$) via deterministic byte prefix scanning strictly without regular expressions and backtracking. Inline code spans delimited by backticks shall be preserved verbatim without break normalization, delimiter splitting, or escape expansion. Nested list items within cells shall parse into structured sub-item tokens, mapping indentation to bullet depths bounded by $``D_{\text{max\_bullet}} \le 8``$ and preserving list marker types (hyphens, asterisks, plus signs, numeric sequences). The normalizer shall operate with zero dynamic buffer reallocations, projecting token spans directly from input buffers. On malformed cells--including unclosed code spans at delimiter pipes (`|`), illegal ASCII control bytes ($`b \lt 32, b \notin \{9, 10, 13\}`$), or bullet depths exceeding $``D_{\text{max\_bullet}}``$--the engine shall emit diagnostic `E0100` or `E0102` per REQ-0191 with coordinates $``[p_{\text{start}}, p_{\text{end}}]``$., the engine shall insert error sentinel $``\bot_{\text{block}}``$, retain preceding valid tokens, and resynchronize at the nearest pipe (`|`) or record break without aborting. The normalizer shall enforce a total, non-panicking execution contract. Latency and memory gates shall be verified. ---
                      The CommonMark table parser within the Universal Schema Ingestion Engine shall map each valid table row to a corresponding intermediate representation (IR) entity in contiguous memory storage while sanitizing raw entity names into valid OMG SysML v2 and KerML basic identifiers using deterministic replacement, contiguous delimiter collapse, prefixing, and scope collision avoidance. For each table row $``\mathbf{r}_i = \langle c_{i, 0}, \dots, c_{i, C-1} \rangle``$, the engine shall extract cell values positionally via column-to-attribute binding vector $`\vec{\beta}`$ and instantiate an IR entity. The raw name string $``S_{\text{raw}}``$ is extracted from the cell bound to $``k_{\text{name}}``$. If a row omits the name cell or contains only whitespace under mandatory naming, the engine shall record diagnostic error code `E0102` with 1-indexed coordinates and synthesize deterministic fallback identifier $``\text{"id\_anonymous\_"} \mathbin{\Vert} \text{Str}(i)``$. The engine shall transform $``S_{\text{raw}}``$ into a valid basic identifier satisfying grammar $``[a\text{-}zA\text{-}Z\_][a\text{-}zA\text{-}Z0\text{-}9\_]^*``$ via a four-stage pipeline: 1. Strip leading and trailing ASCII whitespace. 2. Map non-alphanumeric bytes outside ASCII alphanumerics and underscore to an underscore (`_`). 3. Collapse contiguous runs of underscores into a single underscore (`_`). 4. Prepend prefix `id_` if the initial character is an ASCII digit or matches a reserved keyword. The engine shall track active namespace scope. If a sanitized identifier collides with an existing sibling, the engine shall append an underscore and the monotonic occurrence count $`k \ge 2`$ (`_2`, `_3`) until unique. Per REQ-0002, synthesized entities must retain both the sanitized identifier and original $``S_{\text{raw}}``$ with source byte span coordinates. The pipeline shall enforce a total, non-panicking contract bounding raw identifiers to $``L_{\text{max}} = 256``$ bytes; exceeding $``L_{\text{max}}``$ triggers diagnostic `E0102`. ---
                      The CommonMark table parser within the Universal Schema Ingestion Engine shall implement deterministic lexical disambiguation of array indexing syntax across tabular MBSE schemas. When ingesting cell tokens for structural identifiers, component references, port bindings, or interconnect endpoints, the engine shall decompose bracketed identifiers into a base symbol identifier and integer index qualifiers without lexical backtracking or confusion with type multiplicity brackets (`Type[1..*]`). The engine shall support four syntactic forms: 1. **Scalar Identifiers**: Unindexed strings (`base`, e.g., `Classifier_Alpha`), lowered to $`\langle \text{base}, \bot \rangle`$. 2. **Single-Dimensional Indexed Identifiers**: Bracketed strings (`base[index]`, e.g., `Part_Alpha[0]`), decomposed to base symbol and integer qualifier $``k \in \mathbb{N}_0``$. 3. **Multi-Dimensional Indexed Identifiers**: Chained bracketed indices (`base[i_1]...[i_K]`, e.g., `Matrix_Node[2][3]`), bounded by rank $`K \le 8`$, decomposed to base symbol and index tuple $``\langle i_1, \dots, i_K \rangle``$. 4. **Type Multiplicity Brackets**: Range-bounded types (`Type[lower..upper]`, e.g., `Classifier_Alpha[1..*]`), decomposed to type symbol and multiplicity bounds $`\langle L, U \rangle`$. Bracket contents with `..` or `*` designate type multiplicity $``\theta_{\text{multiplicity}}``$ and are rejected with diagnostic `E0102` if present in an instance column; bracket contents containing strictly decimal digits designate array indexing $``\theta_{\text{array}}``$. ---
                      The Universal Schema Ingestion Engine shall parse CommonMark tabular schemas specifying structural parts and component assemblies into `IngestedPart` intermediate entities. For each data row, the parser shall extract the part definition or usage name, the classifier type reference, the multiplicity interval $`\langle l, u \rangle`$, the structural containment hierarchy, and owned property sets. Part identifiers shall be sanitized according to REQ-0019. The parser shall evaluate multiplicity interval strings into integer pairs $``\langle l, u \rangle \in \mathbb{N}_0 \times (\mathbb{N}_0 \cup \{ \infty \})``$ with $`0 \le l \le u`$ and $`u \ge 1`$. Empty cells ($`M = \bot`$) shall default to $`\langle 1, 1 \rangle`$. Malformed syntax or inverted ranges ($`l \gt u`$) shall emit diagnostic `E0103` (per REQ-0191), substitute sentinel $``\bot_{\text{mult}}``$, and trigger delimiter synchronization per REQ-0016. Structural containment shall form an acyclic directed forest across part entities. A part shall not directly or transitively contain its ancestor. Containment cycles or multiple-parent assignments shall emit diagnostic `E0102`. Missing mandatory part name or classifier type columns shall emit diagnostic `E0102`. ---
                      The CommonMark table parser within the Universal Schema Ingestion Engine shall parse tabular schemas specifying directed ports into intermediate `IngestedPort` AST entities. For each data row, the parser shall extract the port identifier, owning component handle, declared direction (`in`, `out`, `inout`), interface payload data type handle, multiplicity bounds, and optional conjugated marker (`~`). Header columns shall normalize into canonical attributes order-independently. The engine shall compute effective port direction via algebraic involution $``\tau_{\text{conj}}``$ when a conjugated marker is present. Conjugation shall invert directional polarity (`in` to `out`, `out` to `in`, `inout` to `inout`) while strictly preserving payload data type handles, multiplicity bounds, and contractual invariants. Within each parent component classifier, port identifiers must be pairwise distinct. ---
                      The Universal Schema Ingestion Engine shall parse CommonMark tabular schemas specifying classifier attributes, scalar types, default values, engineering units, and numerical bounds into `IngestedAttr` AST entities. The parser shall map columns via an order-independent binding vector into canonical properties: identifier (`id`), owner classifier reference (`owner`), scalar data type ($`\tau`$), default value ($``v_{\text{default}}``$), envelope interval ($``\mathcal{I} = \langle L, U, o_L, o_U \rangle``$), and unit exponent vector ($`\mathbf{u} \in \mathbb{Q}^7`$). Scalar types shall be restricted to `Real`, `Integer`, `Boolean`, `String`, or `ClassifierRef`. The parser shall extract numerical envelopes as closed, open, half-open, or unbounded intervals over real or integer values, enforcing $`L \le U`$. Degenerate intervals ($`L = U`$) are valid iff boundaries are closed ($``\neg o_L \wedge \neg o_U``$). Any specified default value must satisfy $``v_{\text{default}} \in \mathcal{I}``$ and type rules. Non-numeric types (`Boolean`, `String`) shall not declare restrictive envelopes or non-zero unit vectors. Engineering units shall map to rational exponent vectors $`\mathbf{u} \in \mathbb{Q}^7`$ or dimensionless vector $``\mathbf{0}_{\mathbb{Q}^7}``$. Copying string bytes into the symbol interner pool during this pass is the sole permitted exception to zero-copy memory management. ---
                      The Universal Schema Ingestion Engine shall parse CommonMark tabular schemas defining formal constraints, safety conditions, and operational envelopes into strongly typed `IngestedConstraint` AST entities. For each row, the parser shall extract the constraint identifier (`id`), owning classifier (`owner`), verbatim raw constraint expression (`expr`), formal invariant kind (`kind` $`\in \{ \text{Assert}, \text{Assume} \}`$, default `Assert`), severity tier (`severity` $`\in \{ \text{Critical}, \text{Degraded}, \text{Advisory} \}`$, default `Critical`), and optional operational envelope interval ($``\mathcal{I} = \langle L, U, o_L, o_U \rangle``$). Ingestion operates directly on tokenized table rows resolved via dynamic column binding vectors ($`\vec{\beta}`$). Per the Verbatim Expression Preservation Invariant, raw constraint expressions shall be captured without character mutation, re-encoding, or evaluation, preserving bitwise-identical lexical byte sequences for downstream Boolean AST parsing (REQ-0138) and SMT encoding (REQ-0188). Constraint identifiers shall be unique within the owning classifier scope. When present, operational envelopes must satisfy $`L \le U`$, with degenerate intervals ($`L = U`$) requiring closed bounds. Inverted bounds ($`L \gt U`$) or malformed numerical syntax shall emit diagnostic `E0103`. Missing mandatory columns (`id`, `owner`, `expr`), unrecognized kind or severity tokens, or duplicate scoped identifiers shall emit diagnostic `E0102`. ---
                      The CommonMark table parser within the Universal Schema Ingestion Engine shall parse tabular schemas specifying topological connections into `IngestedConnection` intermediate AST entities. For each data row, the parser must extract the connection identifier, source port endpoint path ($``P_{\text{src}}``$), target port endpoint path ($``P_{\text{tgt}}``$), protocol handle ($`\pi`$), optional latency upper bound ($``\tau_{\text{lat}}``$), and explicit delay model flag ($`\delta`$). Column headers shall be dynamically normalized into canonical connection attributes in an order-independent manner. All identifiers must conform to lexical sanitization grammar rules. Endpoint paths must comprise at least two segments delimited by canonical scope delimiters (`::`), decomposing into an owning component hierarchy path and a terminal port identifier ($`P = \text{OwnerPath} \mathbin{\Vert} \text{"::"} \mathbin{\Vert} \text{PortIdentifier}`$). In the topological multigraph, each connection establishes directed edge $``E = (P_{\text{src}}, P_{\text{tgt}})``$. Direct self-loops ($``P_{\text{src}} = P_{\text{tgt}}``$) lacking an explicit delay model ($`\delta = \text{false}`$) are invalid and shall deterministically trigger diagnostic error code `E0104`. ---
                      The Universal Schema Ingestion Engine shall parse CommonMark tables specifying behavioral actions, activities, and discrete state transitions into intermediate `IngestedAction` and `IngestedTransition` AST entities. For action rows, the parser must extract action identifier `id`, owning classifier handle, kind (`Action`, `Activity`, `OpaqueAction`), typed inputs $`\mathcal{I}`$, typed outputs $`\mathcal{O}`$, optional trigger $``e_{\text{trigger}}``$, guard $``g_{\text{guard}}``$, preconditions $``\mathcal{P}_{\text{pre}}``$, and postconditions $``\mathcal{P}_{\text{post}}``$. For state transition rows, the parser shall extract source state $``s_{\text{source}}``$, target state $``s_{\text{target}}``$, trigger $``e_{\text{trigger}}``$, guard $``g_{\text{guard}}``$, and effect handle $``A_{\text{effect}}``$, validating that $``s_{\text{source}}``$ and $``s_{\text{target}}``$ resolve within the owning classifier state scope. On syntax faults, malformed parameter signatures, duplicate names, or unresolvable states, the engine shall emit diagnostic `E0102` per REQ-0191., REQ-0013, and REQ-0016, the engine shall execute synchronization token error recovery on row line breaks ($``\text{SYM}_{\text{LF}}``$), substitute typed error sentinel $``\bot_{\text{action}}``$ or $``\bot_{\text{trans}}``$, and resume ingestion. If diagnostics reach capacity limit $``C_{\text{max\_errors}}``$, the parser shall emit `E0199` and terminate table processing. The parser shall enforce a deterministic, non-panicking execution contract. Test fixtures shall strictly use abstract MBSE placeholders (e.g., `Package_0`, `Classifier_Alpha`, `StateMachine_0`, `State_Idle`, `State_Active`, `Action_0`, `Event_0`, `param_x : Real`). ---
                      The compiler ingestion engine shall provide a native Protocol Buffer version 3 (Proto3) parser that ingests `.proto` schemas into intermediate schema representation (IR) without external toolchain dependencies. The engine shall lower Protobuf messages to `IngestedPart` definitions, fields to typed `IngestedAttr` properties, service RPCs to `IngestedAction` operations, and enums to `IngestedClassifierDef` data types. Field declarations shall preserve names, types, tags $`i`$, and multiplicity intervals $``\langle l, u \rangle \in \mathbb{N}_0 \times (\mathbb{N}_0 \cup \{\infty\})``$, mapping \texttt{repeated} to $`\langle 0, \infty \rangle`$, \texttt{optional} to $`\langle 0, 1 \rangle`$, and singular fields to $`\langle 1, 1 \rangle`$. Declared field tags must satisfy validity invariant $`i \in [1, 2^{29}-1] \setminus [19000, 19999]`$ ($`2^{29}-1 = 536{,}870{,}911`$); tags $`i \le 0`$, $`i \gt 2^{29}-1`$, or $`i \in [19000, 19999]`$ shall emit diagnostic `E0103`. Duplicate field tags within a message shall trigger diagnostic `E0102`. Proto3 enums must bind tag 0 to the first enumerator; missing tag 0 shall emit diagnostic `E0103`. Nested messages shall recursively lower to child classifiers scoped under the parent message package. Service RPCs shall synthesize `IngestedAction` operations with ordered input and output parameters, mapping \texttt{stream} qualifiers to multiplicity $`\langle 0, \infty \rangle`$ and unary parameters to $`\langle 1, 1 \rangle`$. ---
                      The compiler ingestion engine shall parse OMG IDL (`.idl`) specifications into intermediate schema representation (IR) without external preprocessors. The engine shall lower IDL `module` namespaces to nested `IngestedPackage` scopes, `struct` definitions to `IngestedClassifierDef` data types with sequential `IngestedAttr` members, discriminated `union` declarations to variant `IngestedClassifierDef` types with explicit discriminant expressions, `enum` declarations to enumerated `IngestedClassifierDef` types, `typedef` declarations to `IngestedTypeDef` aliases, and `interface` declarations to `IngestedPart` definitions annotated with `is_interface: true`. Every operation parameter must specify an explicit direction (`in`, `out`, or `inout`); omitted or invalid directions shall emit diagnostic `E0102`. The parser shall partition parameters into action inputs (`in`, `inout`) and outputs (`out`, `inout`). Non-void returns shall synthesize output parameter `result`; void returns synthesize no parameter. Bounded sequences `sequence<T, K>`, unbounded sequences `sequence<T>`, and fixed arrays `T[K]` shall lower to multiplicity intervals $`\langle 0, K \rangle`$, $`\langle 0, \infty \rangle`$, and $`\langle K, K \rangle`$ respectively. ---
                      The Universal Schema Ingestion Engine shall parse OpenAPI 3.0 and 3.1 specifications in JSON and YAML formats into intermediate schema IR without external dependencies. The root document lowers to an `IngestedPackage` (e.g., `Package_0::Spec_Alpha`). Schema objects under `components/schemas` lower to `IngestedClassifierDef` (`ClassifierKind::Struct` or `ClassifierKind::Enum`) with `IngestedAttr` fields binding identifiers, types, and multiplicity $``\langle l, u \rangle \in \mathbb{N}_0 \times (\mathbb{N}_0 \cup \{\infty\})``$. Scalar types map deterministically: `string` to `String`, `integer` to `Int32`/`Int64`, `number` to `Real32`/`Real64`, `boolean` to `Boolean`, and `array` to item types with multiplicity. API paths under `paths` (e.g., `/endpoint_alpha/{param_id}`) lower to interface endpoints. HTTP operations (`get`, `post`, `put`, `delete`, `patch`) lower to `IngestedAction` entities. Primary action identifiers derive from explicit `operationId` or deterministic concatenation (`verb_path`); duplicate action identifiers within scope trigger diagnostic `E0102`. Declared path parameters (`in: path`) require `required: true`, multiplicity $`\langle 1, 1 \rangle`$, and bijective equivalence to route template variables; mismatched path parameters trigger `E0102`. Query, header, and cookie parameters lower to input parameters with multiplicity $`\langle 1, 1 \rangle`$ (required), $`\langle 0, 1 \rangle`$ (optional), or array intervals $``\langle \kappa_{\min}, \kappa_{\max} \rangle``$. Declared `requestBody` objects lower to an input parameter named `payload` with multiplicity $`\langle 1, 1 \rangle`$ (required) or $`\langle 0, 1 \rangle`$ (optional). Success responses ($`2xx`$) synthesize output parameter `result` with multiplicity $`\langle 1, 1 \rangle`$ (or $`\langle 0, 0 \rangle`$ for status 204); non-$`2xx`$ responses map to typed error variants. JSON Pointer references (`#/components/schemas/...`) dereference in the symbol table; cyclic references resolve via handle indirection; unresolvable references trigger `E0102`. ---
                      The Universal Schema Ingestion Engine shall provide a native XML Schema Definition (W3C XSD) and Architecture Description Language (ADL) parser that ingests structural schemas and component topologies into intermediate schema IR without external toolchains. The parser must execute via a deterministic, single-pass event-driven pushdown automaton without regular expressions, enforcing the Zero Regex XML Processing Invariant across all input streams. The lowering transformation shall map XML constructs into schema IR: 1. Complex Types and Components: `xs:complexType` definitions and `adl:component` prototypes lower to `IngestedPart` entities within an `IngestedPackage` namespace, establishing hierarchical scoping (e.g., `Package_0::Component_Alpha`). 2. Attributes and Elements: `xs:element` and `xs:attribute` declarations lower to `IngestedAttr` properties with multiplicity $``\langle \text{minOccurs}, \text{maxOccurs} \rangle \in \mathbb{N}_0 \times (\mathbb{N}_0 \cup \{\infty\})``$, mapping `unbounded` to $`\infty`$. Declarations with $`\text{minOccurs} \gt \text{maxOccurs}`$ are invalid and emit `E0103`. 3. Ports: `adl:port` definitions lower to `IngestedPort` entities with explicit directions: provided ports (P-Ports) map to `Out`, required ports (R-Ports) map to `In`, and bidirectional ports map to `InOut`. Missing or invalid directions emit `E0102`. 4. Connectors: `adl:connector` links lower to `IngestedConnection` entities binding source endpoint $``P_{\text{src}}``$ and target endpoint $``P_{\text{tgt}}``$. Unresolved endpoints or directional mismatches (connecting `In` to `Out` in reverse flow) emit `E0102`. ---
                      The compiler ingestion engine shall provide a canonical SysML v2 textual concrete syntax emitter ($``\mathcal{E}_{\text{sysml}}``$) that serializes parsed intermediate schema IR entities into standard-compliant OMG SysML v2 textual notation, writing the unified model atomically to `schema/model.sysml`. The emitter shall lower intermediate schema IR entities to normative SysML v2 syntax: packages to `package <name> {... }`, part definitions to `part def <name> {... }`, usages to `part <name> : <Type>;`, ports to directional declarations (`in port`, `out port`, `inout port`, `port`), attributes to `attribute <name> : <Type>;` with optional multiplicity intervals (`[l..u]`) and default values, connections to `connect <src> to <tgt>;`, constraints to `assert constraint <name> { <expr> };`, actions to `action def <name> {... }`, and item flows to `flow of <Type> from <src> to <tgt>;`. Formatting shall enforce 4 ASCII spaces per indentation level (tabs prohibited) and single line feed terminations ($``\text{SYM}_{\text{LF}}``$, `0x0A`; carriage returns prohibited). Reserved keywords and non-standard identifiers shall be escaped in single backticks. Emitted files shall commence with a fixed timestamp-free header comment ensuring bitwise determinism (REQ-0003). Scoped child entities shall be sequenced in ascending lexicographical order by fully qualified name (REQ-0032). ---
                      The textual emission and model serialization engine shall sort all model declarations--packages, classifiers, ports, attributes, connections, constraints, and behaviors--strictly by canonical fully qualified name prior to canonical model emission (`schema/model.sysml`, REQ-0031) and serialized artifact generation (REQ-0044, REQ-0145, REQ-0178). The canonical fully qualified name $`\text{QName}(d)`$ shall concatenate ancestor namespace identifiers separated by `::`, rooted at the top-level compilation unit (e.g., `Package_0::Classifier_Alpha::Port_1`), using sanitized ASCII identifiers (REQ-0019). Sibling declarations in each scope shall be sorted by lexicographical ASCII byte ordering ($``\prec_{\text{lex}}``$). If declarations share an identical qualified name but distinct metaclasses, sorting shall order them deterministically by metaclass ordinal $`\text{KindOrdinal}(\tau(d))`$. Duplicate declarations possessing identical qualified names and metaclasses within the same scope shall trigger diagnostic `E0102`. Under Synchronization Token Error Recovery, the engine shall log `E0102`, substitute sentinel $``\bot_{\text{sym}}``$, and resume sorting remaining symbols. If accumulated diagnostics reach capacity $``C_{\text{max\_errors}}``$, the engine shall emit `E0199` and terminate. ---
                      The compiler ingestion engine shall compute, record, verify, and persist a multi-file cryptographic manifest recording SHA-256 content hashes, byte sizes, line counts, and AST entity counts for all workspace schema input files and the emitted canonical model (`schema/model.sysml`). The manifest shall be serialized as a canonical JSON document and written atomically to `.pipeline/schema-digest.json`. For each schema input file ($``F_{i} \in \mathcal{F}_{\text{inputs}}``$) and `schema/model.sysml`, the engine shall compute a 5-tuple digest record: normalized workspace-relative path ($``P_{i}``$), 64-character lowercase hexadecimal SHA-256 hash ($``H_{i}``$), exact 64-bit byte size ($``S_{i}``$), line break count ($``L_{i}``$), and synthesized AST entity count ($``N_{i}``$). The manifest shall be written to `.pipeline/schema-digest.json.tmp.<pid>`, flushed via `fsync`, and atomically renamed to `.pipeline/schema-digest.json`. On subsequent compilation, if all live input file digests match `.pipeline/schema-digest.json`, the engine shall register a cache hit, skip parsing and lowering, reuse the cached model, and bypass re-emission of `schema/model.sysml`. Any modified, added, or deleted input file, or corrupted manifest, triggers a cache miss and complete manifest regeneration. ---
                      The compiler core metamodel lowering engine shall lower all ingested schema abstract syntax tree (AST) entities (packages, part definitions, port definitions, action definitions, constraint definitions) into contiguous virtual memory allocations within a typed node arena. AST entities must be allocated in uniform-sized contiguous slots of size $``S_{\text{slot}} = \text{sizeof}(\text{NodeSlot})``$ with 64-bit alignment ($``A_{\text{align}} = 8\text{ bytes}``$), eliminating per-node heap allocator headers, pointer chasing, and heap fragmentation. All inter-node edges and hierarchies within the lowered AST shall reference target entities exclusively via typed scalar integer handles (`NodeIndex`), guaranteeing a pointer indirection depth of zero ($``\text{PointerIndirectionDepth}(\mathcal{A}_{\text{node}}) = 0``$). Insertion into pre-allocated arena chunks shall execute in amortized $`O(1)`$ time, and complete lowering of an AST with $`N`$ entities shall execute in deterministic linear time $`O(N)`$ with $`O(1)`$ base-plus-offset random slot access. ---
                      The compiler metamodel, node arena storage, and abstract syntax tree (AST) graph engine shall address, reference, and interconnect all AST nodes throughout the compilation pipeline exclusively via deterministic typed integer handles (`NodeHandle<T>`). Raw virtual memory pointers (`*const T`, `*mut T`), dynamic heap references, and unaligned offsets are strictly prohibited across all AST graph edges, symbol tables, and compiler passes. Every node handle shall be encoded as a compact 64-bit unsigned integer scalar combining three disjoint bitfields: 1. A 32-bit arena slot index ($`\text{Index} \in [0, 2^{32}-1]`$). 2. A 16-bit slot generation counter ($`\text{Generation} \in [0, 2^{16}-1]`$). 3. A 16-bit node type discriminator tag ($`\text{TypeTag} \in [0, 2^{16}-1]`$). The handle addressing architecture shall enforce the following normative guarantees: - **Generational Safety**: Every arena slot shall maintain an incarnation generation counter incrementing modulo $`2^{16}`$ upon slot reallocation or mutation. Dereferencing a handle within arena $`\mathcal{A}`$ shall perform constant-time tripartite validation: checking slot index bounds, generation equality, and type tag equality. - **Dangling Reference Elimination**: Dereferencing a stale handle (generation mismatch), out-of-bounds index, or type-mismatched handle shall evaluate to $`\bot`$ and emit diagnostic error code `E0200` per REQ-0191 without panics or memory faults, upholding Architectural Directive 5 and REQ-0011. - **Deterministic Serialization & Concurrency**: Handles shall be deterministic functions of topological ingestion order (REQ-0003, REQ-0010) and serialize directly to CBOR/JSON without pointer rebasing (REQ-0044, REQ-0050). Handles have scalar copy semantics, permitting lock-free distribution across the bounded work-stealing thread pool (Directive 2, REQ-0012). - **Reserved Sentinel**: Handle value `0xFFFF_FFFF_0000_0000` is reserved as the typed null handle (`NodeHandle::NULL`) denoting terminal nodes. - **Interner Exception**: String literals and identifiers shall be addressed via interned scalar `SymbolId` tokens within the deduplicated symbol interner pool, which constitutes the sole permitted exception to zero-copy memory management (Directive 3, REQ-0036). - **Abstract MBSE Modeling**: All diagnostics, tests, and models shall strictly use abstract MBSE placeholders (`Package_0`, `Classifier_Alpha`, `Port_1`, `Flow_A`, `param_x : Real`). ---
                      The compiler core metamodel, lexical analyzer, and abstract syntax tree (AST) graph engine shall intern all identifier strings, type names, docstrings, and qualified paths across compilation units into a thread-safe concurrent string interner pool, mapping each distinct string to a 32-bit scalar symbol handle ($`\sigma \in \text{SymbolId}`$, $`\text{sizeof}(\sigma) \le 4\text{ bytes}`$) supporting $`O(1)`$ constant-time scalar equality comparisons. Slicing and copying string bytes from read-only memory-mapped source file buffers into the deduplicated global symbol interner pool during the initial lexical pass represents the sole permitted architectural exception to the zero-copy memory management invariant, in accordance with Architectural Directive 3 and REQ-0009. All downstream AST nodes, intermediate representations, symbol tables, lexical scope environments, and graph structures shall exclusively store, reference, and pass 32-bit scalar `SymbolId` handles rather than heap-allocated string objects or cloned buffers. The interner shall provide bijective bidirectional mapping: forward interning ($`\text{intern}(s) \to \sigma`$) mapping UTF-8 slices to unique scalar handles, and reverse resolution ($`\text{resolve}(\sigma) \to \text{str}`$) returning borrowed immutable `&str` slices from contiguous backing storage without heap allocation. Multi-threaded access shall be scheduled on a bounded work-stealing pool with worker ceiling $``N_{\text{max\_workers}}``$ (Architectural Directive 2, REQ-0012) ensuring data-race freedom. The interner shall enforce string length limit $``L_{\text{max\_str}} = 65536\text{ bytes}``$ and capacity bound $``S_{\text{max\_count}} = 2^{32} - 2``$. In accordance with Architectural Directive 5, the interface is a total function: invalid UTF-8 sequences, strings exceeding $``L_{\text{max\_str}}``$, or pool exhaustion shall emit diagnostic `E0200` per REQ-0191 and yield typed sentinel $``\bot_{\text{sym}} = 2^{32} - 1``$ without unhandled panics. All illustrative examples shall strictly use synthetic abstract MBSE placeholders (e.g., `Package_0`, `Classifier_Alpha`, `Port_1`, `Flow_A`, `param_x : Real`). ---
                      The core metamodel shall enforce a strict formal duality and architectural partition between classifier definitions (`ClassifierDef`) representing reusable types and feature usages (`FeatureUsage`) representing contextual occurrences within enclosing namespaces. Structural elements in the abstract syntax graph shall belong exclusively to either partition, with empty intersection ($`\mathcal{C} \cap \mathcal{U} = \emptyset`$). Every feature usage shall bind to an authoritative classifier definition via a typed reference relation $`\tau : \mathcal{U} \longrightarrow \mathcal{C}`$. Un-typed feature usages ($`\tau(u) = \bot`$), unresolved classifier references, and cyclic definition-usage instantiation chains are strictly prohibited at compile time. In accordance with the subtyping partial order $`(\mathcal{C}, \le)`$, if a feature usage $`u`$ has resolved type $``\tau(u) = C_1``$ and $``C_1``$ specializes $``C_2``$ ($``C_1 \le C_2``$), then $`u`$ conforms to $``C_2``$. When a feature usage binds to an interface slot, parameter, port, or connector end expecting target classifier $``C_{\text{target}}``$, the type checker shall enforce type conformance $``\tau(u) \le C_{\text{target}}``$. Feature usages may redefine inherited features strictly under monotonic covariance rules: 1. **Type Covariance:** $``\tau(u_{\text{redef}}) \le \tau(u_{\text{base}})``$. 2. **Multiplicity Narrowing:** $``[l_u, u_u] \subseteq [l_{\text{base}}, u_{\text{base}}]``$. 3. **Default Value Containment:** $``v_{\text{default}} \in \text{Domain}(\tau(u_{\text{base}}))``$. 4. **Directional Invariance:** Port directionality ($`\text{in}`$, $`\text{out}`$, $`\text{inout}`$) must be preserved across redefinitions. Contravariant type redefinition, multiplicity widening, or invalid default values shall deterministically emit diagnostic error code `E0200` per REQ-0191. The engine shall bind error sentinel $``\bot_{\text{type}}``$ on violation, guaranteeing total-function panic-free execution. ---
                      The Core Metamodel, Node Arena & AST Graph Engine shall enforce strongly typed port directionality (`in`, `out`, `inout`) on all port definitions and usages, verifying directional compatibility across topological connection bindings. Port definitions shall declare an immutable base direction $``d_{\text{decl}} \in \mathcal{D} = \{ \text{In}, \text{Out}, \text{InOut} \}``$. Port usages shall inherit $``d_{\text{decl}}``$, with optional conjugation (`~`) applying algebraic involution $``\tau_{\text{conj}}``$ to compute effective direction $``d_{\text{eff}} \in \mathcal{D}``$. Connections are partitioned into two structural categories: 1. **Peer-to-Peer (Assembly) Connections:** For sibling component usages, the engine shall enforce anti-parallel directed flow (`Out` to `In`, `In` to `Out`) or bidirectional flow (`InOut` to `InOut`). Unidirectional matching (`In` to `In`, `Out` to `Out`) or mismatched `InOut` pairs without adapters shall emit diagnostic `E0201` per REQ-0191. 2. **Hierarchical Delegation Connections:** For enclosing parent boundary ports connecting to inner child ports, the engine shall enforce parallel flow preservation ($``P_{\text{outer}}.d_{\text{eff}} = P_{\text{inner}}.d_{\text{eff}}``$). Directional inversion across boundaries shall emit diagnostic `E0201`. ---
                      The Core Metamodel, Node Arena & AST Graph Engine shall bind item flow payloads to authoritative classifier definitions and validate stream transmission rate multiplicities across connectors and channels. Every item flow (`ItemFlow` or `FlowUsage`) connecting source port $``P_{\text{src}}``$ and target port $``P_{\text{tgt}}``$ must specify payload classifier $``\tau_F``$ and rate multiplicity interval $``R_{\text{flow}} = [r_{\min}, r_{\max}]``$ in Hertz. The type checking engine shall enforce endpoint payload compatibility. Without an explicit serialization adapter ($``\mathcal{A}_F = \bot``$), payload $``\tau_F``$ must satisfy subtyping covariance: $``\tau_F :> \tau(P_{\text{src}})``$ and $``\tau_F :> \tau(P_{\text{tgt}})``$. With an adapter $``\mathcal{A}_F``$, the engine shall verify signature conformance: $``\tau(P_{\text{src}}) \le \text{InType}(\mathcal{A}_F)``$ and $``\text{OutType}(\mathcal{A}_F) \le \tau(P_{\text{tgt}})``$. Incompatible payloads without adapters shall emit diagnostic error code `E0202`. Rate intervals must satisfy $``0 \le r_{\min} \le r_{\max}``$. Peak throughput $``\Theta(F) = r_{\max} \cdot \text{sizeof}(\tau_F)``$ must not exceed channel capacity $``C_{\text{channel}}``$, where $``\text{sizeof}(\tau_F)``$ is the serialized byte footprint of $``\tau_F``$. Multiplexed channels must satisfy $``\sum \Theta(F) \le C_{\text{channel}}``$. Violations shall emit diagnostic error code `E0202`. ---
                      The core abstract syntax tree (AST) engine shall execute a deterministic two-pass symbol resolution pipeline across workspace compilation units, decoupling declaration order from reference order. Pass 2 (Reference Resolution): The engine traverses the AST and resolves symbol references, cross-references, feature typings, connection endpoints, port bindings, subtyping relationships (`:>`, `:>>`), and constraint variables against $`\Gamma`$. Lookups search outward through ancestor scopes or evaluate double-colon paths (`::`), resolving forward references and mutual recursion across packages invariant to declaration order. ---
                      The Core Metamodel, Node Arena & AST Graph Engine shall implement hierarchical lexical scope lookup and path evaluation using double-colon scoping (`::`) to resolve identifier references across nested lexical scopes, package boundaries, and imported namespaces. The resolver shall evaluate references via two deterministic mechanisms: 1. **Unqualified Lexical Lookup:** Given unqualified identifier $`\sigma`$ in active scope $``S_{\text{active}}``$, the resolver searches outward along the parent chain $`\text{parent}(S)`$ to root namespace $``S_{\text{root}}``$. The first matching visible declaration binds to the reference, establishing lexical shadowing where inner definitions shadow enclosing ones. 2. **Qualified Path Resolution:** Given path $``p_1 \mathbin{::} \dots \mathbin{::} p_k``$, a leading `::` indicates an absolute path evaluated from $``S_{\text{root}}``$. Otherwise, $``p_1``$ resolves via unqualified lookup in $``S_{\text{active}}``$. Subsequent segments $``p_j``$ ($`2 \le j \le k`$) resolve as direct members of predecessor $``p_{j-1}``$. 3. **Visibility & Ambiguity:** `Public` symbols are accessible universally. `Private` symbols are accessible strictly within their declaring package. `Protected` symbols are accessible within declaring and conforming classifiers. Inaccessible accesses or conflicting wildcard imports emit diagnostic `E0200` per REQ-0191. ---
                      The core abstract syntax tree (AST) engine shall implement a deterministic cycle detection engine utilizing Tarjan's strongly connected components (SCC) algorithm to identify, isolate, and reject circular dependencies across metamodel relationship graphs during compile-time semantic analysis. The engine shall enforce acyclicity across three directed relational subgraphs: 1. Specialization Hierarchies ($``G_{\text{inherit}}``$): Specialization relations (`specializes`, `:>`) between classifier definitions (`ClassifierDef`) must be strictly acyclic, prohibiting self-specialization ($`u :> u`$) and mutual circular chains ($``v_1 :> \dots :> v_k :> v_1``$). 2. Composition Hierarchies ($``G_{\text{comp}}``$): Containment relations (`contains`, `owns`) between packages, definitions, and usages must be strictly acyclic, prohibiting direct or transitive self-containment. 3. Feature Redefinition Hierarchies ($``G_{\text{redef}}``$): Feature redefinition and subsetting relations (`redefines`, `:>>`, `subsets`) across feature usages must be strictly acyclic. Upon detecting any cycle, the engine shall reconstruct deterministic directed cycle path $``\mathcal{P}_{\text{cycle}} = \langle v_1, \dots, v_k, v_1 \rangle``$ starting at origin $``v_1 = \min_{v \in C} \text{Handle}(v)``$ and emit diagnostic error code `E0203` with source byte spans, coordinates, cycle category (`InheritanceCycle`, `ContainmentCycle`, or `RedefinitionCycle`), and ordered traceback per REQ-0191. , the engine shall apply synchronization token error recovery: it records `E0203` into sink $``\mathcal{D}_{\text{sink}}``$, prunes closing back-edge $``(v_k, v_1)``$ in overlay $``\mathcal{E}_{\text{overlay}}``$, and binds sentinel $``\bot_{\text{cycle}}``$, enabling independent subgraphs to continue semantic validation. If accumulated diagnostics reach capacity $``C_{\text{max\_errors}}``$, the compiler shall emit `E0199` and terminate gracefully. ---
                      The compiler shall support multi-file models partitioned across hierarchical directories, deterministically mapping relative filesystem paths to nested package namespaces within the abstract syntax tree (AST). For every source file ingested beneath the workspace schema root directory ($``\mathcal{R}_{\text{schema}}``$), the compiler shall decompose the relative path into directory segments and bind the file's top-level declarations to an enclosing leaf package namespace whose fully qualified name matches the PascalCase-normalized directory hierarchy. The ingestion engine shall enforce the following normative rules: 1. **Directory Mapping**: Relative path $``p_1 / p_2 / \dots / p_k / \text{name}.\text{ext}``$ shall deterministically map to package namespace $``\text{PascalCase}(p_1) \mathbin{::} \dots \mathbin{::} \text{PascalCase}(p_k)``$. Files at the schema root ($`k = 0`$) shall bind to canonical root package `RootPackage`. 2. **Intermediate Package Synthesis**: If an intermediate package in the prefix chain does not exist in the AST, the compiler shall synthesize an intermediate package container node in the AST. Sibling files sharing directory prefixes shall resolve to identical synthesized package node handles. 3. **Declaration Containment**: All top-level declarations within an ingested file shall be registered as owned members of the resolved leaf package container node. 4. **Package Declaration Reconciliation**: Explicit top-level package declarations must match the directory-derived leaf namespace or represent an explicit child subpackage. Incompatible declarations shall be rejected with diagnostic `E0200`. 5. **Path Normalization & Collision Detection**: Segments shall be normalized to valid PascalCase identifiers. Distinct sibling directories that normalize to identical identifiers or contain invalid characters shall be rejected with diagnostic `E0200`. 6. **Nesting Depth Bounds**: Directory nesting depth shall satisfy $``k \le D_{\max} = 16``$. Paths exceeding $``D_{\max}``$ shall be rejected with diagnostic `E0200`. ---
                      The Core Metamodel, Node Arena & AST Graph Engine shall provide deterministic, bidirectional, lossless serialization and deserialization of compiled Abstract Syntax Trees (AST) to and from minified JSON (RFC 8259) and binary CBOR (RFC 8949). Codecs must preserve all AST structural entities: packages, part definitions, port definitions, item definitions, connection definitions, action definitions, constraint definitions, attributes, expressions, multiplicity intervals, relational edges, port directions (`in`, `out`, `inout`), conjugation flags, and exact source spans $``\langle \text{file\_id}, p_{\text{start}}, p_{\text{end}}, \text{line}, \text{col} \rangle``$ per REQ-0002. Per Directive 1 and REQ-0010, every serialized AST node must store a deterministic RFC 4122 UUIDv5 identifier derived from compiler namespace constant $``\text{NS}_{\text{DEAP}}``$ and canonical topological path; time-based UUIDs are prohibited. AST nodes shall be reconstructed directly into contiguous bump arena storage per REQ-0009 and REQ-0034 using typed generational node handles per REQ-0035 without pointer swizzling. Centralized string deduplication must be enforced; copying string bytes into the global symbol interner pool during deserialization is the sole permitted exception to zero-copy memory management per Directive 3 and REQ-0036. Serialized binary CBOR payload size must satisfy $`|\text{CBOR}(\mathcal{A})| \le 0.40 \cdot |\text{JSON}(\mathcal{A})|`$ for models where $`|\text{Nodes}(\mathcal{A})| \ge 100`$. Round trips must preserve structural isomorphism ($`\mathcal{D}(\mathcal{S}(\mathcal{A})) \cong \mathcal{A}`$) and bitwise idempotency ($`\mathcal{S}(\mathcal{D}(\mathcal{S}(\mathcal{A}))) = \mathcal{S}(\mathcal{A})`$), enforcing zero diff churn per REQ-0003. Per Directive 4, REQ-0013, and REQ-0016, deserialization shall implement synchronization token recovery on record boundaries: malformed payload bytes or truncated streams record diagnostic error code `E0200` per REQ-0191 and continue parsing, emitting `E0199` if accumulated diagnostics reach $``C_{\text{max\_errors}}``$. Per Directive 5, REQ-0011, and REQ-0196, the engine enforces a non-panicking execution contract; in compiled Release mode (`--release`), CBOR deserialization of a 100,000-node model must complete in under 15 ms with total latency under 25 ms and peak RSS memory under 100 MB. All fixtures, diagnostics, and models shall exclusively use synthetic abstract placeholders (`Package_0`, `Classifier_Alpha`, `Port_1`, `Flow_A`, `param_x : Real`). ---
                      The Core Metamodel, Node Arena & AST Graph Engine shall provide an immutable graph traversal engine that visits vertices and directed edges of the abstract syntax tree (AST) multigraph $``G = (\mathcal{V}_{\text{AST}}, \mathcal{E}_{\text{AST}})``$ in topological, depth-first (pre-order and post-order), or breadth-first (level-order) disciplines with strictly bounded $`O(V + E)`$ linear time complexity. Traversal algorithms must operate strictly over shared immutable references without allocating temporary graph structures or mutating node payloads, headers, or edge relations. ---
                      The abstract syntax tree (AST) engine shall provide a deterministic, mutable transformation pass engine for lowering, syntactic desugaring, optimization rewrites, constant propagation, and semantic enrichments while strictly preserving graph topological integrity and typed reference safety. All AST rewrite passes shall perform node attribute modifications in-place within contiguous node arena storage, preserving immutable slot indices ($``\text{Index}(n, \mathcal{A}_{t+1}) = \text{Index}(n, \mathcal{A}_t)``$) and fixed virtual memory base offsets without disjoint node reallocations. The mutation engine must update each arena slot's monotonic incarnation generation counter ($``g \in \mathbb{U}_{16}``$) modulo $`2^{16}`$ upon in-place modification or replacement. Any external node handle referencing an obsolete generation shall evaluate deterministically to an invalid reference ($`\bot`$), preventing ABA hazards across compiler passes. ---
                      The compiler core shall construct, maintain, and query an in-memory bidirectional directed property multigraph $`G = (V, E)`$ over abstract syntax tree (AST) nodes stored in the AST. The multigraph implementation must remain strictly technology-neutral, clean-room engineered, and decoupled from external graph libraries, operating directly on arena index slabs, scalar node handles (`NodeHandle`), and deterministic adjacency lists. The multigraph architecture shall enforce the following normative guarantees: 1. Representation & Parallelism: Vertices $`v \in V`$ correspond to typed node handles per REQ-0034 and REQ-0035; raw pointers are prohibited. Edges $`e \in E`$ possess unique 32-bit identifiers (`EdgeId`), endpoints $`(\text{src}(e), \text{dst}(e))`$, kind tag $``k \in \mathcal{K}_{\text{edge}}``$, and property payload. Parallel directed edges between identical node pairs $`(u, v)`$ are permitted for distinct relationships (e.g., parallel port connections or flow channels). 2. Canonical Kinds & Bidirectionality: Edges belong to closed set $``\mathcal{K}_{\text{edge}} = \{ \text{Contains}, \text{Specializes}, \text{Types}, \text{ConnectsTo}, \text{FlowsTo}, \text{AllocatesTo}, \text{Constrains}, \text{DependsOn} \}``$. For every edge $`e \in E`$, the engine registers $`e`$ simultaneously in outgoing list $`\text{OutEdges}(\text{src}(e))`$ and incoming list $`\text{InEdges}(\text{dst}(e))`$. Forward and reverse traversals exhibit symmetric algorithmic efficiency. 3. Deterministic Canonical Ordering: Incident edge lists maintain a total order keyed by: (1) category tag, (2) neighbor index, and (3) declaration sequence, ensuring bitwise reproducible compilation (REQ-0003) and invariant RFC 4122 UUIDv5 hashing (REQ-0010). 4. Error Recovery & Diagnostics: Operations enforce a deterministic, non-panicking contract (REQ-0011). Inserting an edge with an invalid or stale handle emits diagnostic `E0200`. Introducing a cycle into containment forest $``G_{\text{cont}} = (V, E_{\text{Contains}})``$ emits diagnostic `E0203`. Diagnostics strictly use synthetic abstract MBSE placeholders (`Package_0`, `Classifier_Alpha`, `Port_1`, `Flow_A`, `param_x : Real`). ---
                      The core abstract syntax tree (AST) graph engine shall provide deterministic topological dependency scheduling, cycle detection, and shortest-path routing across model elements. Vertices represent lowered AST entities (packages, classifier definitions, feature usages, and ports) in the AST addressed by typed node handles (`NodeHandle<T>`). Nodes possess deterministic RFC 4122 UUIDv5 identifiers from namespace $``\text{NS}_{\text{DEAP}}``$ and canonical fully qualified paths. Copying string bytes into the symbol interner pool for scalar `SymbolId` tokens is the sole permitted exception to zero-copy memory management. The graph engine shall enforce four deterministic transformations: 1. Kahn Topological Scheduling: Computes linear schedule $``\mathcal{L} = \langle v_1, \dots, v_n \rangle``$ where $`\text{Index}(u, \mathcal{L}) \lt \text{Index}(v, \mathcal{L})`$ for each dependency edge $`(u, v) \in E`$. Schedulable vertices in ready queue $`Q`$ with zero in-degree are dequeued in ascending lexicographical order of interned qualified names ($`\text{QualifiedName}(v)`$), ensuring bitwise reproducibility per REQ-0003. 2. Tarjan SCC Decomposition: Traverses directed multigraphs via linear-time depth-first search to compute maximal strongly connected components $``\mathcal{C} = \{ C_1, \dots, C_k \}``$ and condensation DAG $`G^{\text{scc}} = (\mathcal{C}, E^{\text{scc}})`$. 3. Cycle Diagnostics & Synchronization Recovery: In acyclic contexts (inheritance, containment, execution flows), non-trivial SCCs ($`|C| \gt 1`$ or self-loops) trigger diagnostic `E0203` with circular traceback $``\mathcal{P}_{\text{cycle}}``$., the engine tags cyclic nodes invalid, accumulates diagnostics, and resumes scheduling over acyclic components. Reaching limit $``C_{\text{max\_errors}}``$ emits `E0199` and terminates. 4. Shortest-Path Interconnect Routing: Executes breadth-first search (BFS) between port handles $``P_{\text{src}}``$ and $``P_{\text{tgt}}``$ across directed connection edges, breaking equidistant ties via intermediate qualified name comparison. ---
                      The core metamodel, node arena, and AST graph engine shall provide a deterministic, depth-bounded semantic AST slicing facility (`query_slice`) to extract self-contained subgraphs surrounding a target element for focused reasoning, code generation, and micro-verification within context-isolated subagent environments. ---
                      The core metamodel and AST graph engine shall serialize extracted abstract syntax tree (AST) slices into standalone packages with reified dependency envelopes. Each serialized package must encapsulate the sliced subgraph alongside all referenced external classifier definitions, port contracts, physical unit systems, and numerical constraint declarations required to evaluate the sliced component in complete semantic isolation, without reference lookups into the parent AST. Every serialized package shall contain: 1. Slice Manifest (`SliceManifest`): Deterministic header storing root UUIDv5, target handle, traversal depth $`k`$, schema version, and payload checksum. 2. Sliced Subgraph ($``G_{\text{slice}}``$): Contiguous AST nodes and edges extracted around the target entity per REQ-0049. 3. Reified Dependency Envelope ($``\text{Deps}(G_{\text{slice}})``$): Minimal structural stubs defining external types, $`\mathbb{Q}^7`$ unit vectors (REQ-0098), operational bounds $``[v_{\min}, v_{\max}]``$ (REQ-0112), and directional ports (REQ-0038) referenced by $``G_{\text{slice}}``$. External classifiers in $``\text{Deps}(G_{\text{slice}})``$ shall contain public feature signatures only, strictly excluding behavioral bodies and internal hierarchies. ---
                      The compiler core metamodel and AST graph engine shall implement a deterministic incremental compilation caching subsystem structured upon an explicit module dependency directed acyclic graph (DAG) $`G = (V, E)`$. For each module $`M \in V`$, the compiler shall compute a 64-bit cryptographic content hash $``H_{\text{source}}(M)``$ upon source ingestion, capturing normalized source tokens and syntax tree nodes. Each directed edge $`(U, V) \in E`$ denotes that downstream module $`V`$ depends on upstream module $`U`$. For each module $`M \in V`$, the incremental engine shall compute composite state hash $``H_{\text{state}}(M)``$ by combining $``H_{\text{source}}(M)``$ with upstream dependency state hashes $`\text{Deps}(M)`$ via bitwise XOR reduction. State hash propagation shall proceed in topological sort order over $`G`$. The compiler shall compare $``H_{\text{state}}(M)``$ against cached state hash $``H_{\text{cached}}(M)``$ from the cache manifest. If $``H_{\text{state}}(M) = H_{\text{cached}}(M)``$, the compiler shall bypass re-analysis and re-emission for module $`M`$, reusing cached AST subgraphs, typed symbol tables, and artifacts directly ($``T_{\text{recompile}}(M) = 0``$). If $``H_{\text{source}}(M) \neq H_{\text{cached\_source}}(M)``$ or any upstream state hash changes, the compiler shall invalidate module $`M`$ and its transitive downstream dependent set $`\text{TransitiveDependents}(M)`$, scheduling strictly these affected modules for recomputation. Modules outside this invalidation closure shall be preserved and reused from cache. All recomputed state hashes, source hashes, and artifact descriptors must be committed atomically to the persistent cache manifest upon pass completion. If a dependency cycle is detected during DAG construction or topological sorting, the compiler shall reject the invalid graph, emit diagnostic error code `E0203` detailing the cyclic path, and terminate gracefully. If the cache manifest is missing or corrupted, the compiler shall emit diagnostic error code `E0200`, discard the cache partition, and execute a full clean build from scratch. ---
                      The persistence engine shall perform read-only memory-mapped diffing of candidate artifact byte buffers against on-disk files prior to writing. It shall bypass file emission when generated content matches on-disk bytes identically, preserving modification timestamps (`mtime`), inodes, and metadata attributes. ---
                      The compilation persistence engine shall maintain a centralized artifact manifest (`CodegenManifest`) and execute automated tombstone pruning (`prune_tombstones`) during each compilation pass. When any AST element (such as `Package_0`, `Classifier_Alpha`, or `Port_1`) is deleted, renamed, or relocated, the engine shall compute the exact set difference between previous manifest paths $``\mathcal{A}_{\text{manifest}}``$ and active output paths $``\mathcal{A}_{\text{active}}``$, producing the tombstone pruning set $``\mathcal{T}_{\text{prune}} = \mathcal{A}_{\text{manifest}} \setminus \mathcal{A}_{\text{active}}``$. The engine shall enforce strict filesystem path confinement for every $``f \in \mathcal{T}_{\text{prune}}``$: paths must resolve within output root $``\mathcal{W}_{\text{out}}``$, contain zero parent traversal segments (`..`), and never escape $``\mathcal{W}_{\text{out}}``$ via symlinks. Unconfined paths shall trigger diagnostic error code `E0200` without unlinking. For each validated path, the engine shall atomically unlink the file. External pre-deletion shall be treated as an idempotent no-op. If filesystem permissions or I/O locks prevent deletion, the engine shall record diagnostic error code `E0200` and continue processing remaining tombstones without panicking. Following file unlinking, the engine shall recursively delete empty parent directories up to $``\mathcal{W}_{\text{out}}``$, terminating upon encountering non-empty directories. ---
                      The compiler metamodel lowering engine shall define and enforce the foundational KerML abstract syntax root hierarchy as a rooted directed multigraph of semantic elements $`\mathcal{E}`$, directed relationships $`\mathcal{R} \subseteq \mathcal{E}`$, metadata annotations $`\mathcal{M} \subseteq \mathcal{E}`$, and containment ownership relations $`\mathcal{O} \subset \mathcal{E} \times \mathcal{E}`$, with `Element` as the universal root entity. A `Relationship` ($`r \in \mathcal{R}`$) specializes `Element`, connecting non-empty source ($`\text{source}(r) \subseteq \mathcal{E}`$) and target ($`\text{target}(r) \subseteq \mathcal{E}`$) endpoints. Directed non-reflexive relationships require $`\text{source}(r) \cap \text{target}(r) = \emptyset`$. Empty, reflexive, or dangling endpoints shall emit diagnostic `E0200` per REQ-0191. Containment $`\mathcal{O}`$ forms a strict directed forest enforcing single ownership ($`\forall v \in \mathcal{E}, |\text{owner}(v)| \le 1`$). Cycles ($`(e, e) \in \mathcal{O}^+`$) are prohibited; detected cycles shall emit diagnostic `E0203` with cycle path $``\mathcal{P}_{\text{cycle}}``$ per REQ-0042. Conflicting multiple ownership shall emit `E0200`. `Annotation` ($`\alpha \in \mathcal{M}`$) specializes `Element`, attaching metadata such that $`⟦ e \oplus \alpha ⟧ \equiv ⟦ e ⟧`$. ---
                      The semantic model lowering engine shall represent lexical scopes, naming environments, and containment hierarchies as formal `Namespace` scopes composed of typed `Membership` relationships, mapping interned member symbols to semantic element node handles in the AST graph. Memberships shall partition into two disjoint subsets: 1. `OwningMembership`: Establishes composite ownership and lifecycle containment. The engine shall enforce single ownership: every owned element in the model shall be bound by exactly one `OwningMembership`. Conflicting owning memberships shall trigger diagnostic error code `E0200`. Ownership relations shall form a directed forest; containment cycles shall trigger diagnostic error code `E0203`. 2. Non-Owning Reference `Membership`: Establishes visible reference bindings between a namespace and an element owned elsewhere without altering lifecycle containment. Within any given `Namespace`, named memberships must satisfy lexical uniqueness. Colliding member names resolving to distinct elements within the same namespace shall trigger diagnostic error code `E0200`. Identical names resolving to identical elements are permitted. Every named element shall possess a deterministic qualified name sequence (`QN`), defined inductively as the owner namespace qualified name concatenated with its interned member name, serialized with `::` delimiters (e.g., `Package_0::Classifier_Alpha::Port_1`). Anonymous elements possess no qualified name. Absolute paths prefixed with `::` resolve from root; relative paths resolve from active local scope. Unresolved path segments shall trigger diagnostic error code `E0200`. ---
                      The KerML scoping engine shall evaluate namespace import declarations as deterministic relational projections over exported membership sets across compilation units. The engine shall parameterize import visibility across a two-point bounded lattice $`\mathcal{V} = \{ \text{Private}, \text{Public} \}`$ where $`\text{Private} \prec \text{Public}`$: 1. Private imports (`private import` or default unqualified imports) shall bind symbols strictly into the target namespace internal scope; they shall not be re-exported. 2. Public imports (`public import`) shall bind symbols into the target public interface, transitively re-exporting them to foreign importing scopes. The scoping engine shall support four import modalities: 1. Single-element import (`import Package_0::Classifier_Alpha;`), projecting a designated public member identified by qualified path. 2. Namespace wildcard import (`import Package_0::*;`), projecting all directly declared public members of the source namespace into the target scope. 3. Recursive wildcard import (`import Package_0::**;`), computing the reflexive-transitive closure of public sub-namespace containment with cycle-detection protection. 4. Filtered and aliased import (`import Package_0::Classifier_Alpha as Classifier_Beta;` or predicate filter $`\phi`$), projecting members satisfying boolean filter predicates and binding explicit symbol aliases. The scoping engine shall enforce deterministic shadow precedence: locally declared members within target namespace $``N_{\text{tgt}}``$ shall strictly shadow imported members sharing an identical unqualified identifier. Shadowed imported symbols shall remain accessible via fully qualified paths. When an unqualified identifier lookup matches two or more distinct imported members in the absence of a shadowing local declaration, the engine shall reject the reference and emit diagnostic error code `E0200`. If an import declaration targets an unresolved namespace or member, the engine shall emit diagnostic error code `E0200`. ---
                      The semantic metamodel lowering engine shall formalize the foundational KerML classifier hierarchy into a bounded subtyping poset $`(\mathcal{K}, \le)`$ rooted at `Type`. Classifiers shall be partitioned into structural value types (`DataType`) and extensional identity-bearing entities (`Class`, `Structure`) under set-theoretic denotational semantics. The compiler shall enforce the specialization chain: `Structure` specializes `Class`, `Class` specializes `Classifier`, `DataType` specializes `Classifier`, and `Classifier` specializes `Type`. The compiler shall enforce semantic disjointness: $`⟦ \text{DataType} ⟧ \cap ⟦ \text{Class} ⟧ = \emptyset`$. Multiple inheritance across both `DataType` and `Class` (or `Structure`), or mutable and behavioral features declared in a `DataType`, shall be rejected with diagnostic `E0200`. The compiler shall evaluate identity duality across all instances: 1. For $`a, b \in ⟦ \text{DataType} ⟧`$, equivalence is structural value congruence ($``a \equiv_{\text{val}} b``$) across all feature projections. 2. For $`u, v \in ⟦ \text{Class} ⟧ \cup ⟦ \text{Structure} ⟧`$, equivalence requires extensional object token identity ($`\text{id}(u) = \text{id}(v)`$), remaining non-identical despite feature value congruence. The subtyping relation $`(\mathcal{K}, \le)`$ shall be reflexive, transitive, and antisymmetric. Circular inheritance cycles ($``(C, C) \in \mathcal{E}_{\text{gen}}^+``$) shall trigger diagnostic `E0203`. Unresolved supertypes shall trigger `E0200`. ---
                      The semantic lowering engine shall formalize multi-ary relations as `Association` and `AssociationStructure` classifiers possessing $`k \ge 2`$ participant end features (`AssociationEnd`), enforcing relational constraints, directional navigability, and fiber cardinality bounds over extensional `Link` tuples. An association declaring $`k \lt 2`$ ends shall be rejected at compile time with diagnostic error code `E0200`. Each participant end $``e_i``$ ($`1 \le i \le k`$) shall specify a classifier type $``C_i = \tau(e_i)``$, a multiplicity interval $``\mu_i = [l_i, u_i]``$ ($``l_i \le u_i``$, $``u_i \ge 1``$), navigability $``\text{nav}_i \in \{ \text{Navigable}, \text{NonNavigable} \}``$, and an interned role name. Instantiated links $``L = (o_1, \dots, o_k) \in \prod_{i=1}^k ⟦ C_i ⟧``$ must satisfy participant type conformance $``\tau(o_i) \le C_i``$. Any type mismatch, un-typed participant, or unbound slot shall deterministically trigger diagnostic error code `E0200`. For every participant instance $``x \in ⟦ C_j ⟧``$, the projected fiber on any target end $`i \ne j`$ shall satisfy $``l_i \le |\{ \pi_i(L) \mid L \in ⟦ A ⟧ \wedge \pi_j(L) = x \}| \le u_i``$; violations shall trigger diagnostic error code `E0200`. Expressions attempting traversal to an end marked `NonNavigable` shall trigger diagnostic error code `E0200`. An `AssociationStructure` shall specialize both `Association` and `Structure`, binding relational semantics to internal structural features, lifecycles, and persistent object identity. Specialization $``A_{\text{sub}} \le A_{\text{base}}``$ shall preserve arity, participant type covariance, multiplicity narrowing, and navigability; non-monotonic specializations shall trigger diagnostic error code `E0200`. ---
                      The semantic lowering engine shall formalize occurrence communications and flow exchanges as `Interaction` classifiers in accordance with KerML. An `Interaction` classifier shall multiply specialize both `Behavior` and `Association`, combining behavioral occurrence execution semantics with relational association semantics across two or more participant occurrences ($`k \ge 2`$). As an `Association`, an `Interaction` shall declare two or more participant end features ($``P_{1}, \dots, P_{k}``$, $`k \ge 2`$) specifying classifier types and multiplicity bounds; declaring fewer than two participants shall emit diagnostic `E0200`. As a `Behavior`, an `Interaction` shall govern an occurrence lifecycle over constituent `Step` features modeling occurrence performances. Constituent steps shall include message transfer steps $``s_{\text{transfer}} = \langle e_{\text{send}}, e_{\text{recv}}, \delta_{\text{payload}}, p_{\text{src}}, p_{\text{tgt}}, \tau_{\text{msg}} \rangle``$ transmitting payload $``\delta_{\text{payload}}``$ from send event $``e_{\text{send}}``$ on $``p_{\text{src}}``$ to receive event $``e_{\text{recv}}``$ on $``p_{\text{tgt}}``$. The engine shall enforce a causal precedence poset $``(\mathcal{S}_{I}, \prec)``$ with temporal non-inversion: $``s_{1} \prec s_{2} \implies \tau_{\text{end}}(s_{1}) \le \tau_{\text{start}}(s_{2})``$. The engine shall validate message transfer constraints and causal acyclicity: 1. Directional Causality: Transmission must precede reception ($``\tau(e_{\text{send}}) \lt \tau(e_{\text{recv}})``$); violations ($``\tau(e_{\text{recv}}) \le \tau(e_{\text{send}})``$) shall emit diagnostic `E0201`. 2. Payload Typing: Payload $``\delta_{\text{payload}}``$ must conform to declared type $``\tau_{\text{msg}}``$ ($``\tau(\delta_{\text{payload}}) \le_{\text{sub}} \tau_{\text{msg}}``$); mismatches shall emit diagnostic `E0202`. 3. Precedence Acyclicity: Precedence graph $``G_{I} = (\mathcal{S}_{I}, \prec_{I})``$ must be a DAG; detected causal cycles ($``s \prec_{I}^{+} s``$) shall emit diagnostic `E0203`. Upon recording any diagnostic (`E0200`, `E0201`, `E0202`, `E0203`), synchronization token recovery shall sever cycle back-edges in an overlay graph and continue evaluation, halting with `E0199` if diagnostic buffer capacity is reached. Lowered entities shall use contiguous typed storage, 32-bit handles, and deterministic RFC 4122 UUIDv5 anchors. Test fixtures shall use synthetic placeholders (`Package_0`, `Interaction_Alpha`, `Participant_0`, `Participant_1`, `Step_1`, `Step_2`, `Step_Transfer`, `Payload_Type_A`, `param_x : Real`). ---
                      The semantic lowering engine and AST graph engine shall formalize properties, behavioral invocations, structural slots, directional parameters, and execution steps as instances of the unified `Feature` abstract syntax metaclass. In the KerML metamodel lowering pipeline, `Feature` shall specialize both `Type` and `Relationship`, unifying structural value projection, behavioral invocation, and relational typing. Every `Feature` must bind to declared classifier types via formal `FeatureTyping` relationships ($`\tau`$). The compiler shall prohibit un-typed features whose types cannot be resolved within lexical scope, emitting diagnostic error code `E0200`. A feature $`f`$ owned by classifier definition $`C`$ shall induce an evaluation projection mapping $``\pi_f : ⟦ C ⟧ \longrightarrow \mathcal{P}(⟦ \tau(f) ⟧)``$, mapping each instance of $`C`$ to a finite subset of values in $`⟦ \tau(f) ⟧`$. Every feature must declare a multiplicity interval $``\mu(f) = [m_{\min}, m_{\max}]``$ ($``m_{\min} \in \mathbb{N}_{0}``$, $``m_{\max} \in \mathbb{N}_{0} \cup \{ \infty \}``$, $``m_{\min} \le m_{\max}``$) constraining instance fiber cardinality: $``\forall x \in ⟦ C ⟧, \; m_{\min} \le |\pi_f(x)| \le m_{\max}``$. Inverted intervals ($``m_{\min} \gt m_{\max}``$) or instance fiber violations shall emit diagnostic error code `E0200`. The metamodel shall provide `Parameter` as a specialized `Feature` declaring directionality $`\text{dir}(p) \in \{ \text{In}, \text{Out}, \text{InOut} \}`$. `In` parameters accept inputs and remain immutable within the behavior body; `Out` parameters yield outputs assigned before termination; `InOut` parameters permit bidirectional transfer. Passing unassignable values to `Out`/`InOut` parameters or writing to `In` parameters shall emit diagnostic error code `E0201`. The metamodel shall provide `Step` as a specialized `Feature` representing contextual execution typed by a classifier specializing `Behavior` ($`\tau(s) \le \text{Behavior}`$). Typing a `Step` with a non-behavioral classifier shall emit diagnostic error code `E0200`. Steps project parameter interfaces of their typing behavior as child features. ---
                      The compiler metamodel lowering engine and semantic type checker shall formalize KerML feature subsetting (`Subsetting`, denoted by operator `:>`) as value-set inclusion within the subtyping meet-semilattice. When a feature subsetting relationship $``f_{\text{sub}} :> f_{\text{sup}}``$ is declared between subsetting feature $``f_{\text{sub}}``$ and subsetted feature $``f_{\text{sup}}``$, the compiler shall enforce that for every semantic instance $`x`$ in the domain of the owning classifier, the value set projected by $``f_{\text{sub}}(x)``$ is a subset of the value set projected by $``f_{\text{sup}}(x)``$ satisfying $``\pi_{f_{\text{sub}}}(x) \subseteq \pi_{f_{\text{sup}}}(x)``$. The lowering pass shall verify the following structural invariants for every subsetting declaration: 1. **Co-variant Type Specialization**: The declared or inferred type $``\tau(f_{\text{sub}})``$ shall specialize or equal $``\tau(f_{\text{sup}})``$ in the subtyping partial order ($``\tau(f_{\text{sub}}) \le \tau(f_{\text{sup}})``$). Incompatible or contravariant types shall be strictly rejected with diagnostic code `E0200`. 2. **Multiplicity Interval Narrowing**: Multiplicity intervals $``\mu(f) = [m_{\min}, m_{\max}]``$ must preserve value-set inclusion: $``\mu(f_{\text{sub}}).m_{\max} \le \mu(f_{\text{sup}}).m_{\max}``$ and $``\mu(f_{\text{sub}}).m_{\min} \le \mu(f_{\text{sup}}).m_{\max}``$. Widened upper bounds or infeasible lower bounds shall be rejected with diagnostic code `E0200`. 3. **Domain Specialization**: The featuring classifier context $``\text{owner}(f_{\text{sub}})``$ shall specialize or equal $``\text{owner}(f_{\text{sup}})``$ ($``\text{owner}(f_{\text{sub}}) \le \text{owner}(f_{\text{sup}})``$). Subsetting across disjoint classifiers without an inheritance path shall be rejected with diagnostic code `E0200`. 4. **Directional Flow Polarity**: Directed features (ports and parameters with directionality $`\delta \in \{ \text{In}, \text{Out}, \text{InOut} \}`$) must preserve identical flow directionality ($``\delta(f_{\text{sub}}) = \delta(f_{\text{sup}})``$). Conflicting directions shall be rejected with diagnostic code `E0200`. 5. **Acyclicity Enforcement**: Circular subsetting chains among features ($``f_1 :> f_2 :> \dots :> f_1``$) shall be prohibited and detected at compile time via topological cycle detection, emitting diagnostic error code `E0203`. Lowered subsetting relationship AST nodes shall bind deterministic RFC 4122 UUIDv5 identifiers derived from the fully qualified paths of $``f_{\text{sub}}``$ and $``f_{\text{sup}}``$. On validation failure, the compiler shall record diagnostic `E0200` or `E0203`, assign error sentinel type $``\bot_{\text{type}}``$ to prevent cascade, and recover token synchronization without panicking. ---
                      The metamodel lowering engine shall formalize the KerML and SysML v2 feature redefinition relationship (`:>>`, `redefines`) as contextual slot replacement over multiple inheritance directed acyclic graphs (DAGs), enforcing monotonic C3 superclass linearization, subtyping conformance, and multiplicity interval tightening within the bounded meet-semilattice $`(\text{Types}, \le)`$. When specializing classifier $`C`$ declares feature $``f_{\text{redef}}``$ redefining inherited feature $``f_{\text{orig}}``$ ($``f_{\text{redef}} :>> f_{\text{orig}}``$), the compiler shall enforce: 1. **Contextual Slot Replacement**: $``f_{\text{redef}}``$ shall shadow and replace $``f_{\text{orig}}``$ in $`C`$ and its specializations. References targeting $``f_{\text{orig}}``$ in scope $`C`$ shall resolve directly to $``f_{\text{redef}}``$. 2. **Monotonic C3 Linearization (NP-3)**: Precedence for $`C`$ with direct parents $``P_1, \dots, P_n``$ shall be computed deterministically via C3 linearization. Conflicting precedence orders shall trigger diagnostic error code `E0200`. 3. **Subtyping Conformance**: Redefining type $``\tau(f_{\text{redef}})``$ must co-vary with $``\tau(f_{\text{orig}})``$ ($``\tau(f_{\text{redef}}) \le \tau(f_{\text{orig}})``$). Incompatible types shall trigger diagnostic error code `E0200`. 4. **Multiplicity Interval Tightening**: Multiplicity $``\mu(f_{\text{redef}})``$ must be a sub-interval of $``\mu(f_{\text{orig}})``$ ($``[l_{\text{redef}}, u_{\text{redef}}] \subseteq [l_{\text{orig}}, u_{\text{orig}}]``$). Interval widening shall trigger diagnostic error code `E0200`. 5. **Structural & Directional Invariance**: Directed features shall preserve directional polarity ($``\delta(f_{\text{redef}}) = \delta(f_{\text{orig}})``$) unless conjugated (`~`) per REQ-0063. Direction inversion shall trigger diagnostic error code `E0200`. Ordering and uniqueness flags must be preserved or strengthened. 6. **Acyclicity Enforcement**: Circular redefinitions ($``f_1 :>> f_2 :>> \dots :>> f_1``$) shall be rejected with diagnostic error code `E0203`. 7. **Disambiguation**: Converging inherited redefinitions without C3 ancestor precedence require explicit redefinition in $`C`$; absence shall trigger diagnostic error code `E0200`. 8. **Recovery & Storage**: Violations shall record diagnostics, bind error sentinel $``\bot_{\text{redef}}``$, and continue compilation without panic. AST nodes shall use typed arena handles with interned symbols and RFC 4122 UUIDv5 identifiers. ---
                      The semantic lowering engine and AST graph engine shall formalize the KerML conjugation relationship (`~`) and port inversion transformation across all port definitions, interface definitions, and port usages. The engine shall evaluate conjugation as an algebraic involution over the directional algebra $`\mathcal{D} = \{ \text{In}, \text{Out}, \text{InOut}, \text{None} \}`$, mapping $`\text{In} \mapsto \text{Out}`$, $`\text{Out} \mapsto \text{In}`$, while keeping $`\text{InOut}`$ and $`\text{None}`$ invariant. For any port or interface definition $`P`$, lowering conjugated classifier $`\widetilde{P} = {\sim}P`$ shall preserve structural feature names, payload types ($`\tau`$), multiplicity intervals ($`\mu`$), and behavioral invariant contracts ($`\Psi`$) without alteration, inverting exclusively the flow and parameter directions of contained features: $`\text{dir}(f') = {\sim}\text{dir}(f)`$. Nested port and interface usages within $`P`$ shall conjugate recursively. Consecutive conjugation operators shall simplify algebraically: $`{\sim}^{2k} P \equiv P`$ and $`{\sim}^{2k+1} P \equiv {\sim}P`$ for $``k \in \mathbb{N}_{0}``$. Conjugation applies strictly to classifiers with interaction or port semantics (`PortDefinition`, `InterfaceDefinition`, `PortUsage`). Applying `~` to non-conjugable types (scalars `Integer`, `Real`, `Boolean`, `String`, enumerations, or records lacking ports) shall be rejected, emitting diagnostic `E0200`. Per Algorithmic Bound NP-3, multiple inheritance hierarchies with conjugated parent types (e.g., `Classifier_Alpha :> ~Classifier_Beta, Classifier_Gamma`) shall form a monotonic meet-semilattice and be linearized via the C3 algorithm without backtracking. Conflicting orderings or cycles shall emit diagnostic `E0203`. Connecting two port instances requires conjugate complementarity: an output flow must bind to an input flow of conforming payload type. Direct connections between identical unidirectional flows shall emit diagnostic `E0201`. ---
                      The semantic type checker and metamodel lowering engine shall implement a formal Boolean algebra over classifier type denotations, providing set-theoretic type operators (`unioning`, `intersecting`, `differencing`, `disjoining`) to construct compound classifiers and enforce static disjointness invariants. The lowering engine shall enforce the following normative provisions: 1. `unioning`: The compound union classifier $``T_1 \cup T_2``$ denotes $``⟦ T_1 ⟧ \cup ⟦ T_2 ⟧``$, satisfying subtyping covariance: $``T_1 \le (T_1 \cup T_2) \wedge T_2 \le (T_1 \cup T_2)``$. 2. `intersecting`: The compound intersection classifier $``T_1 \cap T_2``$ denotes $``⟦ T_1 ⟧ \cap ⟦ T_2 ⟧``$, satisfying subtyping contravariance: $``(T_1 \cap T_2) \le T_1 \wedge (T_1 \cap T_2) \le T_2``$. 3. `differencing`: Relative complement $``T_1 \setminus T_2``$ denotes $``⟦ T_1 ⟧ \setminus ⟦ T_2 ⟧``$, satisfying $``(T_1 \setminus T_2) \le T_1``$ and $``(T_1 \setminus T_2) \perp T_2``$. If $``T_1 \le T_2``$, difference denotes empty type $``\bot_{\text{type}}``$; instantiating an uninhabitable difference type shall trigger diagnostic error code `E0200`. 4. `disjoining`: Asserts mutual exclusion $``T_1 \perp T_2 \iff ⟦ T_1 ⟧ \cap ⟦ T_2 ⟧ = \emptyset``$. Disjointness propagates monotonically down the subtyping semilattice: $``\forall S_1 \le T_1, S_2 \le T_2 \implies S_1 \perp S_2``$. Asserting a joint instance, non-empty intersection, or joint specialization ($``C \le T_1 \wedge C \le T_2``$) shall trigger diagnostic error code `E0200`. 5. Subtyping Consistency: Set operations shall preserve subtyping equivalence: $``T_1 \le T_2 \iff ⟦ T_1 ⟧ \subseteq ⟦ T_2 ⟧ \iff ⟦ T_1 \setminus T_2 ⟧ = \emptyset``$. ---
                      The KerML expression lowering engine and semantic type checker shall transform KerML expressions into an immutable, strongly typed abstract syntax tree (AST) rooted in `Expression`. `Expression` shall specialize `Step`, `Feature`, `Classifier`, and `Type`, formalizing every expression as a computational step producing an authoritative result feature ($``p_{\text{result}}``$). The engine shall validate four expression families: 1. **Literal Expressions (`LiteralExpression`)**: Lower primitive constants to typed nodes (`Boolean`, `Integer`, `Real`, `String`, `UnlimitedNatural`, and $``\bot_{\text{type}}``$ for `null`). String literals shall be interned into the symbol interner pool per REQ-0036 as the sole exception to zero-copy memory management. 2. **Feature References & Navigation**: Resolve bare identifiers within lexical scopes ($`\Gamma`$) and member access ($`E.f`$) against $`\tau(E)`$. Unresolved identifiers or features shall emit diagnostic code `E0200`. 3. **Operator Expressions (`OperatorExpression`)**: Prefix, postfix, and binary operators shall enforce signature matching against $``\text{dom}(\text{op}_{\odot})``$; incompatible types emit `E0200`. Static division by literal zero ($`E / 0`$) in constant expressions shall emit `E0200`. Conditional selection ($``\text{if } E_{\text{cond}} \text{ then } E_{\text{then}} \text{ else } E_{\text{else}}``$) requires $``E_{\text{cond}} : \text{Boolean}``$ and unifies branches to their least common supertype ($``T_{\text{then}} \vee T_{\text{else}}``$); violations emit `E0200`. 4. **Invocation Expressions (`InvocationExpression`)**: Invocations $``F(a_1, \dots, a_k)``$ bind arguments to formal parameters $``(p_1, \dots, p_k)``$. Target or arity errors emit `E0200`. For $`\text{In}`$ parameters, argument types must conform ($``\tau(a_i) \le \tau(p_i)``$); type mismatches emit `E0200`. For $`\text{Out}`$ and $`\text{InOut}`$ parameters, arguments must be assignable lvalues ($``\tau(p_i) \le \tau(a_i)``$ for $`\text{Out}`$; $``\tau(a_i) \equiv \tau(p_i)``$ for $`\text{InOut}`$); binding immutable literals or rvalues emits `E0201`. Pure expressions shall be referentially transparent and side-effect free ($``\sigma_{\text{post}} \equiv \sigma_{\text{pre}}``$). Constant expressions shall be evaluated at compile time; cyclic dependencies ($``E_1 \to^+ E_1``$) emit `E0203`. Lowered nodes receive deterministic RFC 4122 UUIDv5 identifiers (REQ-0010). On faults, the engine records diagnostics in sink $``\mathcal{D}_{\text{sink}}``$, binds sentinel $``\bot_{\text{expr}}``$, and resynchronizes at delimiters; reaching limit $``C_{\text{max\_errors}}``$ emits `E0199` and halts. All models and diagnostics shall employ synthetic MBSE placeholders (e.g., `Package_0`, `Classifier_Alpha`, `Function_Alpha`, `param_x : Real`). ---
                      The functional lowering engine of Subsystem 4 shall formalize KerML `Function` classifiers as pure mathematical morphisms from input parameter domains to output result codomains. A `Function` specializes `Behavior` (and transitively `Class`, `Classifier`, `Type`) under referential transparency, total determinism, and side-effect freedom. The lowering engine shall enforce the following normative rules: 1. **Parameter Directionality and Immutability**: Formal parameters must declare direction $`\text{dir}(p) \in \{ \text{In}, \text{Out}, \text{Return} \}`$. Input parameters must declare $`\text{In}`$ and remain immutable. The function must declare exactly one result parameter with direction $`\text{Return}`$ or $`\text{Out}`$ typing return codomain $``T_{\text{ret}}``$. Declaring $`\text{InOut}`$ on a `Function` shall trigger diagnostic `E0201`. 2. **Referential Transparency and Purity**: Evaluation must satisfy $`\mathbf{a} = \mathbf{b} \implies ⟦ F ⟧(\mathbf{a}) = ⟦ F ⟧(\mathbf{b})`$. The body expression shall read strictly from inputs or constants, execute zero state writes, and preserve store equivalence ($``\sigma_{\text{post}} \equiv \sigma_{\text{pre}}``$). State mutation or impure behavior calls shall trigger diagnostic `E0200`. 3. **Return Typing and Body Conformance**: The body expression must evaluate to a type conforming to declared return type $``T_{\text{ret}}``$ ($``\tau(E_{\text{body}}) \le T_{\text{ret}}``$). Incompatible or unresolvable types shall trigger diagnostic `E0200`. 4. **Call-Site Invocation Conformance**: Invocations $``F(a_1, \dots, a_m)``$ must match arity ($`m = k`$) and argument subtyping ($``\tau(a_i) \le T_i``$). Violations shall trigger diagnostic `E0200`. 5. **Call Graph Cycle Detection**: Unbounded recursive cycles lacking a well-founded terminating measure and base condition shall trigger diagnostic `E0203`. Pure non-recursive functions evaluate with $`O(1)`$ stack overhead. ---
                      The KerML lowering engine SHALL formalize spatio-temporal entities as `OccurrenceDefinition` (specializing `Class`) and `OccurrenceUsage` (specializing `Feature` and `Occurrence`). Every `OccurrenceUsage` MUST be typed by one or more `OccurrenceDefinition` classifiers via `FeatureTyping`; typing with non-occurrence classifiers (e.g., `DataType`) SHALL be rejected with diagnostic `E0200`. Each occurrence individual $`o`$ maps to a four-dimensional world-line manifold $`\mathcal{W}(o) \subseteq \mathbb{R}^3 \times \mathbb{R}`$ whose temporal projection yields bounded interval $``\text{temporal\_extent}(o) = [t_{\text{start}}(o), t_{\text{end}}(o)] \subset \mathbb{R}``$ with monotonic ordering $``t_{\text{start}}(o) \le t_{\text{end}}(o)``$. Inverted intervals ($``t_{\text{start}} \gt t_{\text{end}}``$) SHALL emit diagnostic `E0200`. Degenerate intervals ($``t_{\text{start}} = t_{\text{end}}``$) are valid instantaneous snapshot events. Multiplicity intervals $``\mu = [m_{\min}, m_{\max}]``$ MUST satisfy $``0 \le m_{\min} \le m_{\max}``$, or emit diagnostic `E0200`. For composite occurrences ($``o_{\text{sub}} \subseteq_{\text{occ}} o_{\text{super}}``$), the compiler SHALL enforce manifold containment $``\mathcal{W}(o_{\text{sub}}) \subseteq \mathcal{W}(o_{\text{super}})``$, requiring temporal containment $``[t_{\text{start}}(o_{\text{sub}}), t_{\text{end}}(o_{\text{sub}})] \subseteq [t_{\text{start}}(o_{\text{super}}), t_{\text{end}}(o_{\text{super}})]``$. Parent extent violations SHALL emit diagnostic `E0200`. Containment graphs MUST be acyclic; cyclic chains SHALL emit diagnostic `E0203`. ---
                      The KerML lowering engine SHALL formalize occurrence decomposition operators, lowering `snapshot`, `time slice`, and `event occurrence` constructs into rigorous geometric intersections over 4-dimensional occurrence world-lines and world-volumes ($``\mathcal{W} \subseteq \mathbb{R}^3 \times \mathbb{R}``$). An occurrence $O$ instantiated from `OccurrenceDefinition` or `OccurrenceUsage` defines a spatio-temporal extent $\mathcal{W}(O)$ bounded by lifetime interval $``\mathcal{T}(O) = [t_{\text{start}}(O), t_{\text{end}}(O)]``$ with $``t_{\text{start}}(O) \le t_{\text{end}}(O)``$. The lowering engine MUST enforce the following formal semantic rules: 1. **Snapshot Lowering**: A snapshot declaration `Snapshot(O, t_0)` SHALL project the state and active feature values of occurrence $O$ at temporal coordinate $``t_0 \in \mathbb{R}``$. A snapshot has zero Lebesgue measure in time ($``\Delta t = 0``$, $``\lambda_t = 0``$) and MUST satisfy temporal inclusion $``t_{\text{start}}(O) \le t_0 \le t_{\text{end}}(O)``$. Any instant outside parent bounds ($``t_0 \lt t_{\text{start}}(O)``$ or $``t_0 \gt t_{\text{end}}(O)``$) SHALL emit diagnostic `E0200`. Two snapshots at distinct instants ($``t_a \ne t_b``$) are strictly disjoint ($``\text{Snapshot}(O, t_a) \cap \text{Snapshot}(O, t_b) = \emptyset``$). 2. **TimeSlice Lowering**: A time slice declaration `TimeSlice(O, t_1, t_2)` SHALL project occurrence behavior over closed interval $``[t_1, t_2]``$. The engine MUST enforce non-negative duration ($``t_1 \le t_2``$, $``\Delta t = t_2 - t_1 \ge 0``$) and parent lifetime containment ($``[t_1, t_2] \subseteq [t_{\text{start}}(O), t_{\text{end}}(O)]``$). Inverted intervals ($``t_1 \gt t_2``$) or boundary breaches SHALL emit diagnostic `E0200`. 3. **EventOccurrence Lowering**: An event occurrence `EventOccurrence(O, t_e, \Phi)` SHALL formalize an instantaneous trigger satisfying predicate $\Phi$ at coordinate $``t_e``$. The engine MUST verify temporal inclusion ($``t_e \in \mathcal{T}(O)``$) and boolean typing ($``\tau(\Phi) = \text{Boolean}``$). Ill-typed triggers or temporal breaches SHALL emit diagnostic `E0200`. ---
                      The behavioral lowering engine of Subsystem 4 SHALL formalize behaviors, actions, invocations, and temporal performance occurrences in strict accordance with the OMG Kernel Modeling Language (KerML) and Systems Modeling Language (SysML v2) specifications. `Behavior` SHALL specialize `Class` (and transitively `Classifier`, `Type`), formalizing behavioral definitions. Invocations of behaviors within enclosing scopes SHALL be formalized as `Step` features specializing `Feature` and typed by a `Behavior` classifier ($``\tau(s) \le \text{Behavior}``$). Typing a `Step` with a non-behavioral classifier SHALL emit diagnostic `E0200`. Every execution of a behavior over physical or simulated time SHALL be formalized as a `Performance` occurrence specializing `Occurrence`. The lowering engine MUST enforce the following formal semantic rules: 1. **Parameter Conformance and Directionality**: A behavior declares an ordered list of parameters with declared types, multiplicities $``\mu(p) = [m_{\min}, m_{\max}]``$, and directions $``\text{dir}(p) \in \{ \text{In}, \text{Out}, \text{InOut}, \text{Return} \}``$. Arguments bound to parameters at a call site MUST conform to declared parameter types ($``\tau(a) \le \tau(p)``$); subtyping violations SHALL emit diagnostic `E0202`. Directionality violations (assigning to immutable `In` parameters or reading unassigned `Out` parameters) SHALL emit diagnostic `E0201`. 2. **Performance Lifecycle State Automaton**: Each performance occurrence executes over interval $``[t_{\text{start}}, t_{\text{end}}]``$ with $``t_{\text{start}} \le t_{\text{end}}``$. Inverted bounds SHALL emit diagnostic `E0200`. The performance tracks discrete state $``\sigma_{\text{perf}} \in \{ \text{Unstarted}, \text{Executing}, \text{Suspended}, \text{Completed}, \text{Terminated} \}``$. Starting validates pre-conditions $``\mathcal{C}_{\text{pre}}``$, and completing validates post-conditions $``\mathcal{C}_{\text{post}}``$. Contract violations transition to `Terminated` and emit diagnostic `E0202`. Illegal transitions outside the automaton emit diagnostic `E0201`. 3. **Sub-Step Temporal Containment**: For composite behaviors with constituent sub-steps $``\mathcal{S}_B``$, the temporal extent of each sub-step MUST be contained within the parent performance bounds: $``[t_{\text{start}}(s_i), t_{\text{end}}(s_i)] \subseteq [t_{\text{start}}(P), t_{\text{end}}(P)]``$. Out-of-bounds execution SHALL emit diagnostic `E0200`. ---
                      The SysML v2 model organization engine SHALL structure models into modular `package` and subsystem hierarchies, formalizing visibility boundaries, package imports, and encapsulation boundaries as an acyclic package dependency graph. A package declaration (`package <name> {... }`) defines a sovereign namespace boundary specializing KerML `Namespace`. The lowering engine MUST enforce the following formal semantic rules: 1. **Visibility and Encapsulation**: Element memberships within a package declare visibility $``v \in \{ \text{Private}, \text{Public} \}``$, defaulting to `public`. Public elements belong to $``\text{ExportedSymbols}(P)``$ and are accessible via qualified path resolution or package import declarations. Private elements are strictly encapsulated within the declaring package and its lexical children. Any unauthorized access from an external package SHALL emit diagnostic `E0200`. 2. **Package Import Semantics**: The compiler SHALL support single-element (`import P::C;`), namespace wildcard (`import P::*;`), recursive wildcard (`import P::**;`), and alias (`import P::C as A;`) imports. Private imports bind symbols locally; public imports re-export symbols. Every import declaration adds a directed dependency edge $``(P_{\text{src}}, P_{\text{tgt}}) \in \mathcal{D}_{\text{imp}}``$. 3. **Acyclic Package Dependency Graph**: The combined package dependency graph $``G_{\text{pkg}} = (\mathcal{P}, \mathcal{D}_{\text{imp}} \cup \mathcal{D}_{\text{ref}})``$ MUST be a directed acyclic graph (DAG). Any circular import or cross-package dependency cycle SHALL be detected via topological cycle detection and rejected with diagnostic `E0203`. 4. **Nesting Depth Upper Bound**: Package nesting depth SHALL NOT exceed $``D_{\max} = 16``$. Nesting beyond $``D_{\max}``$ SHALL emit diagnostic `E0200`. ---
                      The structural compiler SHALL formalize SysML v2 part definitions (`part def`, `PartDefinition`) and part usages (`part`, `PartUsage`) into strongly typed, compositely owned structural elements anchored within the core KerML classifier subtyping lattice $`(\mathcal{K}, \le)`$. `PartDefinition` SHALL specialize KerML `Structure`, which transitively specializes `Class`, `Classifier`, and `Type` ($`\text{PartDef} \le \text{Structure} \le \text{Class}`$). `PartDefinition` represents an identity-bearing classifier strictly disjoint from identity-free value types ($`⟦ \text{PartDef} ⟧ \cap ⟦ \text{DataType} ⟧ = \emptyset`$); any declaration specializing a `DataType` SHALL emit diagnostic `E0200`. Every `part` usage declaration SHALL lower into a `PartUsage` AST node specializing KerML `Feature` and SysML v2 `ItemUsage`, with the composite ownership flag set strictly to true ($``\text{is\_composite}(u) \equiv \text{true}``$). Composite ownership establishes an existential lifetime dependency: deallocation of containing parent instance $x$ SHALL cause the destruction of all constituent part instances $``y \in \pi_u(x)``$. Every composite part instance $y$ SHALL belong to at most one parent instance ($``|\text{owning\_composite}(y)| \le 1``$); shared composite ownership SHALL emit diagnostic `E0200`. Omitted multiplicity intervals SHALL default to exact singleton $`\mu(u) = [1, 1]`$. Explicit multiplicity intervals $``[m_{\min}, m_{\max}]``$ MUST satisfy $``0 \le m_{\min} \le m_{\max}``$, or emit diagnostic `E0200`. The sub-assembly containment graph $``G_{\text{contain}} = (\mathcal{D}_{\text{part}}, \mathcal{E}_{\text{contain}})``$ MUST be cycle-free for non-zero lower multiplicities ($``m_{\min} \ge 1``$); circular containment cycles SHALL emit diagnostic `E0203`. ---
                      The structural compiler SHALL formalize SysML v2 port definitions (`port def`, `PortDefinition`) and port usages (`port`, `PortUsage`) as interaction point classifiers specializing KerML `Structure`. A port definition $P$ defines an interface protocol specifying typed directed features. Every port usage $p$ declared on an enclosing component or part classifier $C$ SHALL possess an explicit or inferred directionality $`\text{dir}(p) \in \{ \text{In}, \text{Out}, \text{InOut} \}`$ and a valid classifier type $\tau(p) \le \text{PortDefinition}$. The compiler MUST enforce conjugate port instantiation: declaring a port usage with conjugation operator $`\sim`$ ($p : {\sim}P$) SHALL bind the port usage to the conjugated interface where feature directions are inverted according to involution mapping: $`{\sim}\text{In} = \text{Out}`$, $`{\sim}\text{Out} = \text{In}`$, and $`{\sim}\text{InOut} = \text{InOut}`$. Conjugation of non-port classifiers SHALL emit diagnostic `E0200`. Boundary encapsulation MUST be strictly preserved: external connections to component $C$ SHALL terminate exclusively at declared port usages $p \in \text{ports}(C)$, forbidding direct internal feature bypass. Any connection breaching boundary encapsulation SHALL be rejected with diagnostic `E0200`. ---
                      The data and flow modeling engine SHALL formalize SysML v2 item definitions (`item def`, `ItemDefinition`) and item usages (`item`, `ItemUsage`) as structural classifiers specializing KerML `Structure`. Item usages represent physical, energetic, or informational payloads flowing across interconnection topologies with value or token identity semantics. The lowering engine MUST enforce classification duality across all item definitions: 1. **Value Item Payloads**: Item definitions specializing `DataType` represent immutable, identity-free payloads ($`\text{ItemDef} \le \text{DataType}`$). Equality evaluates strictly over structural attribute values. 2. **Discrete Token Payloads**: Item definitions specializing `Class` represent discrete physical or token instances possessing unique extensional identities ($`\text{ItemDef} \le \text{Class}`$, tracking $\text{id}(e)$). For continuous conservative flow topologies, the compiler MUST verify Kirchhoff mass/energy conservation: the sum of input flow rates SHALL equal the sum of output flow rates at each conservative routing node ($`\sum \text{inflow} = \sum \text{outflow}`$). Flow rate mismatches on conservative items SHALL emit diagnostic `E0200`. ---
                      The interconnect engine SHALL formalize SysML v2 connection definitions (`connection def`, `ConnectionDefinition`) and connection usages (`connection`, `connect`, `Connector`) as relational association structures binding two or more port endpoints. `ConnectionDefinition` SHALL specialize KerML `AssociationStructure` and `Structure`. The lowering engine MUST enforce endpoint type compatibility and directional flow legality across all connection usages: 1. **Endpoint Type Conformance**: For a binary connection $``C = (p_1, p_2)``$ between port endpoints $``p_1``$ and $``p_2``$, the source port type MUST conform to the conjugate of the target port type: $``\tau(p_1) \le {\sim}\tau(p_2)``$. Type mismatches across connected endpoints SHALL emit diagnostic `E0200`. 2. **Directional Flow Legality**: Connected port directions MUST be compatible: an `Out` port SHALL connect exclusively to an `In` or `InOut` port ($``\text{dir}(p_1) = \text{Out} \implies \text{dir}(p_2) \in \{ \text{In}, \text{InOut} \}``$). Conflicting directions (e.g., `Out` to `Out` without mediation) SHALL emit diagnostic `E0200`. 3. **Topological Scope Visibility**: Both connection endpoints $``p_1``$ and $``p_2``$ MUST resolve to accessible port usages within the common enclosing component or across immediate peer component boundaries. Out-of-scope or dangling endpoint paths SHALL emit diagnostic `E0200`. ---
                      The protocol engine SHALL formalize SysML v2 interface definitions (`interface def`) as contractual association structures specifying complementary end-roles, and interface usages (`interface`) as communication protocol bindings between component ports. `InterfaceDefinition` SHALL specialize KerML `ConnectionDefinition`; `InterfaceUsage` SHALL specialize KerML `ConnectionUsage`. The lowering engine MUST enforce conjugate duality and port binding: 1. **End-Role Duality**: A binary interface definition $I$ SHALL declare two end-roles $``\text{ends}(I) = (e_1, e_2)``$ satisfying conjugate duality $``\tau(e_2) \equiv {\sim}\tau(e_1)``$. Arity $\ne 2$ SHALL emit diagnostic `E0200`; non-conjugate types SHALL emit `E0201`. 2. **Port Binding**: Interface usage $u$ MUST bind two endpoints $``(p_1, p_2)``$ conforming to end-roles $``(e_1, e_2)``$ of interface $`I = \tau(u)`$: $``\text{type}(p_1) \le \tau(e_1) \wedge \text{type}(p_2) \le \tau(e_2)``$, ensuring $``\text{type}(p_1) \le {\sim}\text{type}(p_2)``$. Non-conforming port types SHALL emit `E0201`; dangling ends SHALL emit `E0220`. 3. **Owned Flows**: Declared item flows MUST preserve payload compatibility ($`\tau(\text{payload}) \le \tau(\text{flow})`$). Incompatible payloads SHALL emit `E0202`. 4. **Interface Inheritance**: Specialization hierarchies MUST form a bounded monotonic meet-semilattice resolved via C3 linearization in $O(V + E)$ time. Cyclic inheritance SHALL emit `E0200`. ---
                      The metamodel lowering engine SHALL formalize SysML v2 `flow` usages (`ItemFlow`) as directed transfers traversing connectors between port endpoints, specializing KerML `Step` and `OccurrenceUsage` in arena storage. The engine MUST enforce four static invariants: 1. **Directional Compatibility**: Source port $``p_{\text{src}}``$ MUST emit ($``\text{dir}(p_{\text{src}}) \in \{ \text{Out}, \text{InOut} \}``$) and target port $``p_{\text{tgt}}``$ MUST ingest ($``\text{dir}(p_{\text{tgt}}) \in \{ \text{In}, \text{InOut} \}``$). Incompatible endpoints SHALL emit diagnostic `E0201`. 2. **Payload Covariance**: Flow payload $``I_{\text{payload}}``$ MUST specialize both endpoint payload types ($``I_{\text{payload}} \le \text{payload\_type}(p_{\text{src}})``$ and $``I_{\text{payload}} \le \text{payload\_type}(p_{\text{tgt}})``$) in meet-semilattice $(\mathcal{T}, \le, \wedge)$. Type violations SHALL emit diagnostic `E0202`. 3. **Rate and Capacity**: Rate interval $``R_{\text{flow}} = [r_{\min}, r_{\max}]``$ MUST satisfy $``0 \le r_{\min} \le r_{\max}``$; invalid bounds SHALL emit diagnostic `E0202`. Peak throughput $``r_{\max} \cdot \text{size}(I_{\text{payload}})``$ SHALL NOT exceed connector capacity $\text{Capacity}(C)$; overflow SHALL emit diagnostic `E0202`. 4. **Endpoint Scoping**: Ports $``p_{\text{src}}``$ and $``p_{\text{tgt}}``$ MUST resolve to accessible ports within scope; unresolvable endpoints SHALL emit diagnostic `E0200`. ---
                      The SysML v2 lowering engine SHALL formalize allocation definitions (`allocation def`) and usages (`allocate... to...`, `AllocationUsage`) as a typed bipartite relation from behavioral source elements to structural target elements. `AllocationDefinition` SHALL specialize KerML `ConnectionDefinition`, and `AllocationUsage` SHALL specialize `ConnectionUsage`. The lowering engine MUST enforce bipartite domain disjointness, structural port consistency, and dependency acyclicity: 1. **Bipartite Disjointness**: Allocations $``U_{\text{alloc}}``$ MUST bind actions $``u_{\text{src}} \in V_S``$ to parts $``u_{\text{tgt}} \in V_T``$ ($``V_S \cap V_T = \emptyset``$). Inverted or reflexive allocations ($``u_{\text{src}} = u_{\text{tgt}}``$) SHALL emit diagnostic `E0200`. 2. **Port Consistency**: Allocating $``u_{\text{src}}``$ to $``u_{\text{tgt}}``$ requires each port $``p_s \in \text{Ports}(u_{\text{src}})``$ to map to port $``p_t \in \text{Ports}(u_{\text{tgt}})``$ with identical direction ($``\text{dir}(p_t) = \text{dir}(p_s)``$) and covariant payload ($``\tau(p_s) \le \tau(p_t)``$). Mismatches SHALL emit diagnostic `E0200`. 3. **Multiplicity Bounds**: Multiplicity intervals $``\mu(U) = [m_{\min}, m_{\max}]``$ MUST satisfy $``0 \le m_{\min} \le m_{\max}``$. Inverted intervals SHALL emit `E0200`. 4. **Dependency Acyclicity**: Circular allocation chains in $``E_{\text{alloc}}^+``$ SHALL emit diagnostic `E0203`. ---
                      The compiler SHALL lower SysML v2 action definitions (`action def`, `ActionDefinition`) as process classifiers specializing KerML `Behavior` and `OccurrenceDefinition`, and action usages (`action`, `ActionUsage`) as discrete steps specializing KerML `Step` and `OccurrenceUsage`. The lowering engine MUST enforce five core invariants: 1. **Parameter Directionality**: Parameters declare $\delta(p) \in \{ \text{In}, \text{Out}, \text{InOut} \}$. Flow edges $``e_{\text{data}}``$ MUST connect `Out`/`InOut` to `In`/`InOut` pins; invalid polarities emit `E0201`. 2. **Payload Subtyping & Multiplicity**: Source payload MUST specialize target type ($``\tau(p_{\text{src}}) \le \tau(p_{\text{tgt}})``$) and source multiplicity MUST NOT exceed target bound ($``\mu(p_{\text{src}}).m_{\max} \le \mu(p_{\text{tgt}}).m_{\max}``$); violations emit `E0202`. 3. **Control Topology**: Control nodes $``V_{\text{ctrl}}``$ in $``G_{\text{flow}}``$ MUST satisfy degree bounds: initial ($0, 1$), final ($\ge 1, 0$), fork/decision ($1, \ge 2$), and join/merge ($\ge 2, 1$); violations emit `E0200`. 4. **Step Lifecycle**: Steps satisfy $\text{State}(s) \in \{ \text{Waiting}, \text{Ready}, \text{Executing}, \text{Completed} \}$, transitioning to `Ready` when incoming control tokens and data inputs arrive. 5. **Dependency Acyclicity**: Step dependency graph $``G_{\text{dep}}``$ MUST be a DAG; cycles emit `E0203`. ---
                      The statechart lowering engine SHALL formalize SysML v2 state machine definitions (`state def`, `StateDefinition`) and state usages (`state`, `StateUsage`) as behavioral classifiers specializing KerML `ActionDefinition` and `ActionUsage`. The lowering engine MUST enforce hierarchical containment and concurrency invariants: 1. **Hierarchical State Tree**: States form a rooted tree $(S, \sqsubseteq)$ where $``s_1 \sqsubset s_2``$ denotes ownership of sub-state $``s_1``$ by composite state $``s_2``$. Containment MUST be acyclic; cyclic chains ($``s_1 \sqsubset^+ s_1``$) emit diagnostic `E0203`. In non-parallel composite states, at most one sub-state is active simultaneously ($|\text{active}(s)| \le 1$). Sibling state names within identical scope MUST be unique; duplicates emit `E0200`. 2. **Orthogonal Parallel Concurrency**: Parallel composite states SHALL contain $k \ge 2$ orthogonal regions $``R_1, \dots, R_k``$. Degenerate states ($k \lt 2$) emit `E0200`. 3. **Cartesian State Configuration**: Active state configurations SHALL satisfy Cartesian product vector $``\mathbf{s} \in \prod_{i=1}^k \text{States}(R_i)``$, enforcing $``|\text{active}(R_i)| = 1``$ for each region. 4. **Transition Synchronization**: Direct transitions between distinct orthogonal regions ($``s_a \in R_i \to s_b \in R_j, i \ne j``$) without fork/join mediation emit `E0200`. Non-state typing emits `E0200`. ---
                      The compiler SHALL lower SysML v2 `transition` usages (`TransitionUsage`) as directed behavioral edges between state configurations, specializing KerML `ActionUsage` and `Step`. The lowering engine MUST enforce five core invariants: 1. **Endpoint Resolution & Orthogonality**: Transitions SHALL connect valid source $``S_{\text{src}}``$ and target $``S_{\text{tgt}}``$ states; unresolved vertices emit `E0200`. Forks ($``|S_{\text{tgt}}| \ge 2``$) and joins ($``|S_{\text{src}}| \ge 2``$) MUST partition across distinct orthogonal regions of a common parallel parent; violations emit `E0200`. 2. **Trigger & Guard Typing**: Triggers $``e_{\text{trigger}}``$ MUST specialize KerML `EventOccurrence` (omitted triggers denote completion events $\epsilon$); invalid trigger types emit `E0201`. Guards $``g_{\text{guard}}``$ MUST evaluate to `Boolean` ($``\tau(g_{\text{guard}}) \equiv \text{Boolean}``$); non-boolean guards emit `E0202`. Sibling transitions with identical source and trigger MUST have disjoint guards; overlapping guards emit `E0200`. 3. **Inner-First Conflict Precedence**: When enabled transitions conflict on exit states, priority SHALL be decided by source tree depth. Deeper source states take precedence ($``\text{Depth}(t_1.s_{\text{src}}) > \text{Depth}(t_2.s_{\text{src}})``$). 4. **Triggerless Cycle Elimination**: Closed cycles of triggerless, guardless transitions emit `E0203`. 5. **Three-Phase Step Ordering**: Firing transition $t$ with $``s_{\text{LCA}} = \text{LCA}(S_{\text{src}}, S_{\text{tgt}})``$ SHALL: (1) exit states from $``S_{\text{src}}``$ to $``s_{\text{LCA}}``$ innermost-first, (2) execute effect $``a_{\text{effect}}``$ atomically, and (3) enter states to $``S_{\text{tgt}}``$ outermost-first. ---
                      The state machine engine SHALL formalize SysML v2 state lifecycle hooks (`entry`, `do`, `exit`) as temporal occurrences bound to state activation, residence, and deactivation intervals. `StateDefinition` and `StateUsage` specialize KerML `Behavior`; `EntryActionUsage`, `DoActionUsage`, and `ExitActionUsage` specialize KerML `ActionUsage`. The lowering engine MUST enforce the following lifecycle invariants: 1. **Multiplicity Bounding**: States declare at most one hook per category ($[0..1]$ multiplicity). Duplicate un-sequenced hooks emit diagnostic `E0200`. 2. **Behavioral Typing**: Each hook $A$ MUST specialize KerML `Behavior` ($`\tau(A) \le \text{Behavior}`$). Non-behavioral types emit `E0201`. 3. **Temporal Ordering**: Residence interval $``[t_{\text{entry}}(S), t_{\text{exit}}(S)]``$ must be non-inverted ($``t_{\text{entry}} \le t_{\text{exit}}``$; inverted emits `E0200`). Lifecycle phases execute sequentially: - *Entry ($``A_{\text{entry}}``$)*: Atomic, run-to-completion step at $``t_{\text{entry}}``$ ($\Delta t = 0$). External events are queued without preemption. - *Do ($``A_{\text{do}}``$)*: Initiated post-entry ($``t_{\text{start}} \ge t_{\text{end}}(A_{\text{entry}})``$). Preemptible; autonomous completion posts $``\varepsilon_{\text{complete}}(S)``$. Outgoing transition firing aborts $``A_{\text{do}}``$ immediately, terminating sub-occurrences before exit invocation. - *Exit ($``A_{\text{exit}}``$)*: Atomic, run-to-completion step upon deactivation after do completion or abort ($\Delta t = 0$), preceding transition effects. 4. **Ladder Dispatch**: Transitions across states with Least Common Ancestor $\text{LCA}$ execute an ascending exit ladder to LCA, transition effects, and a descending entry ladder from LCA to target. Internal transitions execute effects in-place without invoking hooks or aborting $``A_{\text{do}}``$. ---
                      The lowering engine SHALL formalize SysML v2 calculation definitions (`calc def`, `CalculationDefinition`) as functional classifiers specializing KerML `Function`, and calculation usages (`calc`, `CalculationUsage`) as steps specializing KerML `Step`. The compiler MUST enforce five core invariants: 1. **Referential Transparency**: Calculations evaluate as pure functions ($y = f(\mathbf{x})$) without state mutation ($\Delta \text{State} \equiv \emptyset$). Any mutating syntax--including feature assignments or impure calls--emits diagnostic `E0200`. 2. **Parameter Directionality**: Input parameters declare $\text{dir}(p) = \text{In}$. Mutating modes (`InOut`, mutable `Out`) emit `E0201`. Exactly one return parameter ($``p_D^{\text{ret}}``$) of type $``T_{\text{out}}``$ SHALL be declared. 3. **Usage Typing**: Usages MUST type to functional classifiers ($\tau(u) \le \text{Function}$); non-functional types emit `E0200`. Bound arguments MUST satisfy covariant subtyping ($``\tau(a_i) \le \tau(p_i)``$); mismatches emit `E0200`. Missing mandatory parameters emit `E0200`. 4. **Multiplicity Bounds**: Multiplicity intervals $``\mu(u) = [m_{\min}, m_{\max}]``$ MUST satisfy $``0 \le m_{\min} \le m_{\max}``$; inverted intervals emit `E0200`. 5. **Dependency Acyclicity**: Calculation dependency graph $``G_{\text{calc}} = (V_{\text{calc}}, E_{\text{calc}})``$ MUST be a DAG; cycles ($``u \to_{\text{calc}}^+ u``$) emit `E0203`. ---
                      The metamodel lowering engine SHALL formalize SysML v2 `constraint def` (`ConstraintDefinition`) and `constraint` (`ConstraintUsage`) as Boolean predicate functions specializing KerML `Predicate` and `Function`. Every `ConstraintDefinition` SHALL define a pure invariant proposition over formal parameters $``\mathbf{P}_{CD} = (p_1, \dots, p_k)``$` asserting body $``e_{CD}``$` evaluating to `true` across admissible states. The engine MUST enforce five static invariants during lowering: 1. **Boolean Codomain**: `ConstraintDefinition` specializes `Function` ($`\text{ConstraintDefinition} \le \text{Function} \longrightarrow \mathbb{B}`$`). Body $``e_{CD}``$` MUST unify with `Boolean`; non-Boolean types emit `E0200`. 2. **Parameter Directionality**: Parameters MUST declare or default to `In` ($``\text{dir}(p_i) = \text{In}``$). `Out` or `InOut` parameters emit `E0201`. Body evaluation produces zero state mutation ($`\Delta \text{State} \equiv \emptyset`$); side effects emit `E0200`. 3. **Usage Binding**: `ConstraintUsage` $CU$ MUST bind arguments $``\mathbf{A}_{CU}``$` conforming to $``\mathbf{P}_{CD}``$. Arity mismatch ($m \ne k$) or subtyping failure ($``\tau(a_i) \not\le \tau(p_i)``$) emits `E0200`. Unreadable arguments emit `E0201`. 4. **Call Graph Acyclicity**: Definitions MUST NOT form recursive cycles in call graph $``\mathcal{G}_{\text{c\_dep}}``$; cycles emit `E0203`. 5. **Anonymous Lowering**: Blocks (`constraint { <expr> }`) synthesize an arena `ConstraintDefinition`, project free variables as synthetic `In` parameters, and emit a bound `ConstraintUsage`. ---
                      The KerML/SysML v2 lowering engine SHALL lower assert constraint declarations (`assert constraint`, `AssertConstraintUsage`) into invariant assertions specializing KerML `ConstraintUsage` and `Invariant`. Every `AssertConstraintUsage` binds Boolean predicate $\Phi$ to a classifier context (`part def`, `item def`, `action def`, or `state def`) or package, asserting temporal invariance $\square \Phi$ across reachable execution traces. The lowering engine MUST enforce four static invariants: 1. **Specialization & Codomain**: `AssertConstraintUsage` specializes KerML `ConstraintUsage` with codomain `Boolean` and `is_asserted` true. Predicate $\Phi$ MUST unify with `Boolean`; non-Boolean expressions SHALL emit diagnostic `E0200`. 2. **Directionality & Purity**: Parameters MUST declare directional `in` semantics (`E0201` on violation). Evaluation MUST be functionally pure ($``\Delta\text{State} \equiv \emptyset``$; `E0200` on state mutation). 3. **Binding & Acyclicity**: Argument vector $``\mathbf{A}_{ACU}``$ MUST match parameter vector $``\mathbf{P}_{CD}``$ in arity and subtyping ($``\tau(a_i) \le \tau(p_i)``$; `E0200` on mismatch). Anonymous blocks synthesize arena definitions. The constraint call graph MUST be a DAG (`E0203` on cycles). 4. **Dual Synthesis Obligations**: Synthesis SHALL emit SMT-LIB2 proof obligations ($``\text{Reachable}(\sigma) \wedge \neg \Phi \implies \text{UNSAT}``$, emitting `E0200` on refutation) and zero-allocation runtime monitors $``\mathcal{M}_{\text{monitor}}(\sigma_t)``$ evaluating $``\Phi(\sigma_t)``$ in $O(1)$ time with failsafe containment. ---
                      The compiler SHALL lower SysML v2 requirement definitions (`requirement def`, `RequirementDefinition`) as contractual classifiers specializing KerML `ConstraintDefinition`, and requirement usages (`requirement`, `RequirementUsage`) as contextual features specializing KerML `ConstraintUsage`. The lowering engine MUST enforce six core invariants: 1. **Specialization**: `RequirementDefinition` specializes KerML `ConstraintDefinition` with Boolean codomain; `RequirementUsage` specializes `ConstraintUsage`. 2. **Identifier Uniqueness**: Requirements SHALL declare an alphanumeric identifier ($``\text{req\_id}``$); duplicates across compilation units MUST emit diagnostic `E0200`. 3. **Normative Prose**: Definitions SHALL specify non-empty normative text; empty text emits `E0200`. 4. **Subject Binding & Direction**: Definitions declare subject parameter ($``p_{\text{subject}}``$). Parameters MUST declare `In` directionality ($\text{dir}(p) \equiv \text{In}$); non-`In` directions emit `E0201`. Usages MUST bind the subject to conforming types ($``\tau(a_{\text{subject}}) \le \tau(p_{\text{subject}})``$); mismatches emit `E0200`. 5. **Assume-Guarantee Contract**: Requirements formalize contract $``\mathcal{C}_R = (\mathcal{A}_{\text{assume}}, \mathcal{G}_{\text{require}})``$ ($``\mathcal{A}_{\text{assume}}``$ defaults to $\top$). Predicates MUST evaluate to `Boolean` and be functionally pure ($\Delta \text{State} \equiv \emptyset$); violations emit `E0200`. 6. **Acyclicity**: Dependency multigraph $``G_{\text{dep}}``$ MUST be a DAG; cycles emit `E0203`. ---
                      The compiler SHALL lower SysML v2 satisfy requirement usages (`SatisfyRequirementUsage`, declared via `satisfy requirement` or `satisfy... by...`) as directed realization dependencies linking structural parts or actions to requirements, specializing KerML `Feature`, `Step`, and `Relationship`. The lowering engine MUST enforce six invariants: 1. **Specialization**: `SatisfyRequirementUsage` specializes `RequirementUsage` and `AssertConstraintUsage`. 2. **Bipartite Domain**: Disjoint sets $``V_E``$ and $``V_R``$ satisfy $``V_E \cap V_R = \emptyset``$. Usages MUST link $``e \in V_E``$ to $``r \in V_R``$; domain violations emit `E0200`. 3. **Irreflexivity**: Self-satisfaction ($e = r$) and inverted satisfaction ($r \xrightarrow{\text{satisfies}} e$) MUST emit `E0200`. 4. **Subject Conformance**: Realization element $e$ MUST type-conform to the requirement subject parameter ($``\tau(e) \le_{\text{sub}} \tau(p_{\text{subject}})``$); violations emit `E0200`. 5. **Contextual Scoping**: Explicit syntax and contextual shorthand inside part blocks SHALL resolve targets and owners. Unresolved identifiers emit `E0100`. 6. **Coverage & Acyclicity**: Bipartite graph $``G_{\text{trace}} = (V_E \cup V_R, E_{\text{sat}})``$ tracks satisfaction. Zero in-degree requirements emit `E0200` under completeness enforcement. Extended cycles in $``G_{\text{sat\_all}}``$ emit `E0203`. ---
                      The compiler SHALL lower SysML v2 verification case definitions (`verification def`, `VerificationCaseDefinition`) as behavioral procedures specializing KerML `Behavior` and SysML v2 `CaseDefinition`, and verification usages (`verification`, `VerificationCaseUsage`) as discrete occurrences specializing KerML `Step` and `OccurrenceUsage`. The lowering engine MUST enforce five core invariants: 1. **Specialization**: Definitions specialize KerML `Behavior` and `CalculationDefinition` (via `CaseDefinition`); usages specialize KerML `Step` and `OccurrenceUsage`. 2. **Subject Parameter**: Definitions MUST declare subject parameter $``s \in \mathbf{P}_{\text{subj}}``$ with direction `In` or `InOut` ($``\text{dir}(s) \in \{ \text{In}, \text{InOut} \}``$); `Out` direction emits `E0201`. Usages MUST bind conforming arguments ($``\tau(a_s) \le \tau(s)``$); mismatches emit `E0202`, omissions emit `E0200`. 3. **Verdict Codomain**: Definitions MUST declare result parameter of type `VerdictKind` with codomain $``\mathcal{V} = \{ \text{Pass}, \text{Fail}, \text{Inconclusive} \}``$; invalid return types emit `E0200`. 4. **Verification Binding**: The compiler SHALL formalize `verify` relationships ($V \xrightarrow{\text{verifies}} R$), certifying requirement $R$ verified iff evaluation yields `Pass`; `Fail` refutes, `Inconclusive` halts certification. Dangling references emit `E0200`. 5. **Acyclicity**: Invocation multigraph $``\mathcal{G}_{\text{v\_dep}}``$ MUST be a DAG; cycles emit `E0203`. ---
                      The compiler SHALL lower SysML v2 view definitions (`view def`) and usages (`view`) into structural projection elements, and viewpoint definitions (`viewpoint def`) and usages (`viewpoint`) into requirement elements. The lowering engine MUST enforce six invariants: 1. **Specialization**: `ViewDefinition` specializes `PartDefinition` and `Structure`; `ViewUsage` specializes `PartUsage`. `ViewpointDefinition` specializes `RequirementDefinition`; `ViewpointUsage` specializes `RequirementUsage`. 2. **Disjointness**: `ViewDefinition` MUST NOT specialize `DataType`, `ActionDefinition`, or interfaces; `ViewpointDefinition` MUST NOT specialize non-requirement classifiers (`E0200`). 3. **Framing**: Viewpoints frame concerns $``\mathbf{C}_{VP}``$ and query filter predicates $``\Phi_{\text{filter}} : \mathcal{V}_{\text{model}} \to \mathbb{B}``$. 4. **Conformance**: Views declare conformance via `satisfy viewpoint` (`SatisfyRequirementUsage`). Invalid targets or unsatisfied concerns emit `E0200`. 5. **Projection**: Model projection $``\pi_V``$ extracts induced subgraph $``\mathcal{M}_{\text{view}}``$ where $``\forall n \in \mathcal{V}_{\text{model}}, n \in \mathcal{V}_{\text{view}} \iff \Phi_{\text{filter}}(n) \equiv \text{true}``$, preserving edges between exposed vertices. 6. **Acyclicity**: Dependency graph $``G_{\text{vp\_dep}}``$ MUST be a DAG; cycles emit `E0203`. ---
                      The compiler SHALL lower SysML v2 `expose` statements in `ViewDefinition` and `ViewUsage` as declarative selection expressions, projecting conformant induced subgraphs and validating viewpoint obligations. The lowering engine MUST enforce six core invariants: 1. **Modality**: `expose` statements SHALL support explicit paths (`expose <path>;`), shallow wildcards (`expose <path>::*;`), recursive wildcards (`expose <path>::**;`), and predicate filtering (`expose filter <expr>;`) over types, metadata tags (`@Tag_Alpha`), and boolean expressions. 2. **Path Resolution**: Target paths MUST resolve in scope; unresolvable paths emit `E0200`. 3. **Predicate Typing**: Filter expressions MUST evaluate to `Boolean` ($``\tau(\Phi) \equiv \mathbb{B}``$); non-boolean expressions or unbound attributes emit `E0202`. 4. **Induced Subgraph**: View $V$ SHALL project graph $``G_{\text{view}}(V) = (V_{\text{exp}}, E_{\text{exp}})``$ preserving exposed vertices $``V_{\text{exp}}``$ and induced edges $``E_{\text{exp}} = \{ (u, v) \in \mathcal{E}_{\text{model}} \mid u, v \in V_{\text{exp}} \}``$, guaranteeing soundness and completeness. 5. **Viewpoint Conformance**: Conformance (`satisfy viewpoint <ViewpointDef>;`) MUST target valid viewpoints, enforcing coverage ($``\mathbf{M}_{\text{vp}} \subseteq V_{\text{exp}}``$), filter consistency ($``\forall u \in V_{\text{exp}}, \Phi_{\text{vp}}(u) \equiv \text{true}``$), and exclusion ($``V_{\text{exp}} \cap \mathbf{X}_{\text{vp}} = \emptyset``$); violations emit `E0200`. 6. **Acyclicity**: Cross-view expose references $``\mathcal{G}_{\text{exp\_dep}}``$ MUST form a DAG; cycles emit `E0203`. ---
                      The compiler SHALL lower SysML v2 metadata definitions (`metadata def`, `MetadataDefinition`) as structural classifiers specializing KerML `Structure` and `Class`, and semantic annotation usages (`@`, `MetadataUsage`) as extrinsic metadata attachments linking attribute dictionaries to AST nodes without altering host execution semantics. The lowering engine MUST enforce five core invariants: 1. **Specialization**: `MetadataDefinition` specializes KerML `Structure`, `Class`, and `Classifier` ($``\text{MetadataDef} \le \text{Structure} \le \text{Class} \le \text{Classifier}``$); action/state specialization emits `E0200`. `MetadataUsage` specializes KerML `ItemUsage` and `Feature` ($``\text{MetadataUsage} \le \text{ItemUsage} \le \text{Feature}``$). 2. **Metamodel Neutrality**: Annotations are non-intrusive. Attaching or detaching an annotation preserves host semantics ($``⟦ e ⟧ \equiv ⟦ e \mathbin{\Vert} @M ⟧``$), maintaining invariant typing and control flow. 3. **Target Conformance**: Constraint $``\tau_{\text{target}}``$ (`about`) requires $``\text{kind}(e) \le \tau_{\text{target}}``$; violations emit `E0200`. 4. **Attribute Typing & Uniqueness**: Attributes $``\mathbf{A} = (a_1 : T_1, \dots, a_p : T_p)``$ enforce typed arguments ($``\tau(v_i) \le \tau(a_i)``$); mismatches, unknown keys, or missing attributes emit `E0200`. Cycles emit `E0203`. Duplicate non-repeatable annotations emit `E0200`. 5. **Extrinsic Indexing**: Annotations populate dictionary $\alpha(h, a)$. Forward ($``\mathcal{I}_{\text{fwd}}``$) and reverse ($``\mathcal{I}_{\text{rev}}``$) indices query in amortized $O(1)$ time. ---
                      The compiler SHALL bootstrap KerML `Base` (`Package_Base`) into root scope at initialization, providing `Anything`, classifiers `Element` and `Relationship`, `Nothing`, and operators `Op_Equal` and `Op_NotEqual`. Lowering MUST enforce: 1. **Top-Type**: `Anything` ($\top$) is maximal; classifiers `Type_Alpha` specialize `Anything` ($``\text{Type\_Alpha} \le \text{Anything}``$). 2. **Hierarchy**: `Element` specializes `Anything`; `Relationship` specializes `Element`. 3. **Bottom-Type**: `Nothing` ($\bot$) is minimal, satisfying $`\forall T \in \mathcal{T}, \text{Nothing} \le T`$ ($⟦ \text{Nothing} ⟧ = \emptyset$). 4. **Equivalence**: `Op_Equal` evaluates data types by congruence ($``\equiv_{\text{val}}``$) and classes by identity ($`\text{id}(u) = \text{id}(v)`$); cross-domain comparisons yield `false`. `Op_NotEqual` negates equality. 5. **Visibility**: Symbols are injected into root scope without explicit imports. 6. **Reserved Names**: Redefinition emits `E0200`; cycles above `Anything` emit `E0203`. ---
                      The compiler SHALL lower KerML `ScalarValues` types (`Boolean`, `Integer`, `Real`, `String`) and numeric subtypes (`Natural`, `Positive`) into canonical machine representations, preserving semantic value precision, exact integer boundaries, and IEEE 754-2019 binary64 semantics. ---
                      The compiler SHALL bootstrap KerML `Collections` (`Package_Collections`) into root scope at initialization, providing `Collection<T>`, `Set<T>`, `Sequence<T>`, `OrderedSet<T>`, and `Bag<T>`. Lowering MUST enforce: 1. **Taxonomy**: Types classify along flags $`\text{isUnique}`$ and $`\text{isOrdered}`$: `Set` ($1, 0$), `Sequence` ($0, 1$), `OrderedSet` ($1, 1$), and `Bag` ($0, 0$). 2. **Hierarchy**: Collections specialize `Collection<T>`. `OrderedSet<T>` specializes `Set<T>` and `Sequence<T>`; `Set<T>` specializes `Bag<T>`. 3. **Covariance**: Collections enforce covariant subtyping ($``T_1 \le T_2 \implies \mathcal{C}\langle T_1 \rangle \le \mathcal{C}\langle T_2 \rangle``$); violations emit `E0200`. 4. **Typing & Bounds**: Literals require $``\tau(e_i) \le T``$; mismatches emit `E0200`. Out-of-bounds indexing emits `E0200`. 5. **Functions**: Operations require `In` parameters (`InOut`/`Out` emits `E0201`) and Boolean predicates (non-Boolean emits `E0200`). 6. **Acyclicity**: Recursive collection aliases lacking base stratification emit `E0203`. ---
                      The compiler SHALL bootstrap KerML `ControlFunctions` (`Package_ControlFunctions`) into root scope at initialization, providing `ControlNode` (specializing `Feature` and `Step`) and primitive functions `Control_Fork`, `Control_Join`, `Control_Decision`, and `Control_Merge` (specializing `ControlNode` and `Function`). Lowering MUST enforce: 1. **Topology Degrees**: Exact degree constraints: `Control_Fork` ($``\text{deg}_{\text{in}}=1, \text{deg}_{\text{out}}\ge 2``$), `Control_Join` ($``\text{deg}_{\text{in}}\ge 2, \text{deg}_{\text{out}}=1``$), `Control_Decision` ($``\text{deg}_{\text{in}}=1, \text{deg}_{\text{out}}\ge 2``$), and `Control_Merge` ($``\text{deg}_{\text{in}}\ge 2, \text{deg}_{\text{out}}=1``$); violations emit `E0200`. 2. **Token Passing**: Petri net marking $M$: Fork replicates 1 token to all outputs; Join awaits all input tokens before emitting 1 token; Decision routes 1 token to the true guard branch; Merge forwards arriving tokens immediately. 3. **Decision Guards**: Outgoing guards must type-check to `Boolean` (non-Boolean emits `E0202`), be pairwise disjoint, and be exhaustive; overlapping guards emit `E0200`. 4. **Join Deadlock Freedom**: Join inputs must originate from distinct outputs of a common ancestor fork; conflicting guards or un-forked decision paths emit `E0200`. 5. **Instant Cycles**: Closed cycles formed purely of control nodes emit `E0203`. ---
                      The compiler SHALL bootstrap SysML v2 `Quantities` (`Package_Quantities`) into root scope, formalizing quantities as magnitude-unit pairs and classifying ratio and interval scales. Lowering MUST enforce: 1. **Taxonomy**: `QuantityValue` and `MeasurementScale` specialize `DataType`; `RatioScale` and `IntervalScale` specialize `MeasurementScale` disjointly ($`⟦ \text{RatioScale} ⟧ \cap ⟦ \text{IntervalScale} ⟧ = \emptyset`$). `Unit` binds dimension $`\mathbf{d}(u)`$ and scale $`S(u)`$. Non-data specializations emit `E0200`. 2. **Structure**: Nodes bind magnitude $`v \in \mathbb{R}`$, unit $`u \in \mathcal{U}`$, dimension $`\mathbf{d} \in \mathbb{Q}^7`$, and scale $`S`$; missing units emit `E0200`. 3. **Ratio Scales**: Absolute-zero origin ($``0 \cdot u = \mathbf{0}_{\text{abs}}``$) under $``\mathcal{G}_{\text{ratio}}``$; permits scaling ($`k \cdot Q`$) and homogeneous addition. 4. **Interval Scales**: Origin under $``\mathcal{G}_{\text{interval}}``$; permits difference ($``Q_1 - Q_2 \in \mathcal{Q}_{\text{ratio}}``$) and shift ($``Q_{\text{pos}} + Q_{\Delta} \in \mathcal{Q}_{\text{interval}}``$). Direct addition or scaling emits `E0200`. 5. **Homogeneity**: Operations require matching dimensions ($``\mathbf{d}(Q_1) \equiv \mathbf{d}(Q_2)``$); mismatches emit `E0300`. ---
                      The compiler SHALL bootstrap `Package_ISQBase` and `Package_ISQ` into root scope at initialization. Metamodel lowering MUST enforce: 1. **Base Dimensions**: `Package_ISQBase` defines base dimensions ($M, L, T, I, \Theta, N, J$) spanning $(\mathbb{Z}^7,+,-,\mathbf{0})$. 2. **Canonical Basis**: Base dimensions map bijectively to basis vectors $``\mathbf{e}_1 \dots \mathbf{e}_7 \in \mathbb{Z}^7``$; dimensionless quantities map to $\mathbf{0}$. 3. **Derived Spaces**: `Package_ISQ` defines derived dimensions $``\mathbf{d} = \sum_{i=1}^7 c_i \mathbf{e}_i``$ (Force $``\mathbf{e}_M+\mathbf{e}_L-2\mathbf{e}_T``$). 4. **Algebra**: Operations satisfy $``\mathbf{d}(Q_1 \cdot Q_2) = \mathbf{d}(Q_1) + \mathbf{d}(Q_2)``$, $``\mathbf{d}(Q_1 / Q_2) = \mathbf{d}(Q_1) - \mathbf{d}(Q_2)``$, $\mathbf{d}(Q^k) = k \cdot \mathbf{d}(Q)$. 5. **Homogeneity**: Operations ($A \pm B$, $A == B$) require $\mathbf{d}(A) = \mathbf{d}(B)$; mismatches emit `E0300`. 6. **Integrity**: Scope mutations emit `E0200`; derivation cycles in $``\mathcal{G}_{\text{dim\_dep}}``$ emit `E0203`; exponents outside $[-128, 127]$ emit `E0200`. ---
                      The compiler SHALL bootstrap `Package_SI` and `Package_SIPrefixes` into root scope, lowering `UnitDefinition` and `PrefixDefinition` into immutable AST nodes. Lowering MUST enforce: 1. **Specialization**: `UnitDefinition` specializes `MeasurementUnit` ($``\text{UnitDef} \le \text{MeasurementUnit}``$); `PrefixDefinition` specializes `Prefix`. Incompatible specializations emit `E0200`. 2. **Base Units**: Basis $``\mathcal{B} = \{\text{kg},\text{m},\text{s},\text{A},\text{K},\text{mol},\text{cd}\}``$ defines lattice $``\mathbb{Z}^7``$ ($c = 1, o = 0$, $``\text{is\_ratio} = \text{true}``$). 3. **Derived Units**: Coherent units are power products ($c = 1, o = 0$); non-coherent units bind $c \in \mathbb{Q}^+$; affine units define offset $o \in \mathbb{Q}$. 4. **Metric Prefixes**: Prefixes scale $c$ to $10^k \cdot c$ for $k \in \{-24, \dots, 24\}$ in exact arithmetic $\mathbb{Q}$. 5. **Commensurability**: Conversions require identical dimensions ($``\mathbf{d}(U_1) = \mathbf{d}(U_2)``$); mismatches emit `E0201`; cycles emit `E0203`. ---
                      The metrology engine SHALL model physical dimensions as vector space $(\mathbb{Q}^7,+,\cdot)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$. Canonical basis $``\mathcal{B}_{\text{SI}} = \{\mathbf{e}_M, \dots, \mathbf{e}_J\}``$ maps bijectively to the 7 SI base quantities ($M, L, T, I, \Theta, N, J$). Metamodel lowering MUST enforce: 1. **Irreducible Coordinates**: Every dimension $\mathbf{d} \in \mathbb{Q}^7$ is a tuple $(\alpha,\beta,\gamma,\delta,\epsilon,\zeta,\eta)$ with $``d_i = \frac{p_i}{q_i}``$ ($``\gcd(|p_i|,q_i)=1, q_i \in \mathbb{Z}^+``$). Zero vector $\mathbf{0}$ models dimensionless scalars. 2. **Homomorphisms**: $``\mathbf{d}(Q_1 \cdot Q_2) = \mathbf{d}(Q_1) + \mathbf{d}(Q_2)``$, $``\mathbf{d}(Q_1 / Q_2) = \mathbf{d}(Q_1) - \mathbf{d}(Q_2)``$, $\mathbf{d}(Q^k) = k \cdot \mathbf{d}(Q)$ ($k \in \mathbb{Q}$). 3. **Exact Arithmetic**: Operations use checked 64-bit rationals. Divisors $q = 0$ or overflow emit `E0300`. 4. **Homogeneity**: Operations ($A \pm B$, $A == B$, $A \bowtie B$) require $\mathbf{d}(A) = \mathbf{d}(B)$; mismatches emit `E0300`. ---
                      The engine SHALL represent dimensions as irreducible rational 7-tuples over $\mathbb{Q}^7$ spanning ISQ base dimensions ($M, L, T, I, \Theta, N, J$). Lowering MUST enforce: 1. **Irreducible Exponents**: Coordinates MUST be irreducible pairs $(p, q)$ ($p \in \mathbb{Z}, q \in \mathbb{Z}^+, \gcd(|p|, q) = 1$). Denominators $q \le 0$ emit `E0300`. 2. **Dimensionless Zero**: Zero vector $\mathbf{0} \in \mathbb{Q}^7$ acts as additive identity. 3. **Conjugate Pairs**: Conservative ports (`Port_Alpha`, `Interface_Gamma`) MUST bind Across (`Across_Var`, $e$) and Through (`Through_Var`, $f$) features. 4. **Power Invariant**: Conjugate dimensions MUST satisfy $``\mathbf{d}(e) + \mathbf{d}(f) \equiv \mathbf{d}_{\text{Power}} = (1,2,-3,0,0,0,0) \in \mathbb{Q}^7``$. Violations emit `E0301`. 5. **Non-Conservative Exemption**: Signal interfaces (REQ-0106) SHALL NOT enforce the power invariant. 6. **Homogeneity**: Operations ($``Q_1 \pm Q_2``$, $``Q_1 == Q_2``$) require $``\mathbf{d}(Q_1) = \mathbf{d}(Q_2)``$; mismatches emit `E0300`. ---
                      The compiler SHALL execute dimensional algebra over $\mathbb{Q}$ without floating-point arithmetic, synthesizing flow continuity ($\sum f = 0$) and loop conservation ($\sum \Delta e = 0$). Lowering MUST enforce: 1. **Rational Exponents**: Coordinates in $\mathbb{Q}^7$ bind irreducible fractions $a/b$ ($b \gt 0$); operations evaluate $``\mathbf{d}_1 \pm \mathbf{d}_2``$ and $k \cdot \mathbf{d}$; $b = 0$ emits `E0300`. 2. **Flow Continuity**: Multigraph $``\mathcal{G}_{\text{flow}}``$ lowers to incidence matrix $\mathbf{A}$, synthesizing $``\mathbf{A} \mathbf{f} = \mathbf{0}``$ at conservative junctions. 3. **Cycle Conservation**: Matrix $\mathbf{B}$ lowers from cycle basis $\mathcal{C}$, synthesizing $``\mathbf{B} \mathbf{\Delta e} = \mathbf{0}``$ with $\mathbf{A} \mathbf{B}^T = \mathbf{0}$ and $\mathbf{f}^T \mathbf{\Delta e} = 0$. 4. **Homogeneity**: Flows and potentials MUST match in $\mathbb{Q}^7$ (mismatches emit `E0300`); balance faults emit `E0301`. ---
                      The compiler SHALL validate dimensional homogeneity on additive ($A\pm B$), relational ($A\sim B$), and extremum ($\min,\max$) expressions in $\mathbb{Q}^7$. Lowering MUST enforce: 1. **Additive Invariant**: $A\pm B$ requires $``\mathbf{d}_A\equiv\mathbf{d}_B``$; $E$ inherits $``\mathbf{d}_E=\mathbf{d}_A``$. Unary operators preserve dimensions ($``\mathbf{d}_{\pm A}=\mathbf{d}_A``$). 2. **Relational Typing**: Comparisons $A\sim B$ require $``\mathbf{d}_A\equiv\mathbf{d}_B``$, yielding Boolean type with dimensionless $\mathbf{0}\in\mathbb{Q}^7$. 3. **Commensurability**: When $``\mathbf{d}_A\equiv\mathbf{d}_B``$ with $``u_A\ne u_B``$, compiler scales $B$ by $``k=c_B/c_A\in\mathbb{Q}^+``$ in unit $``u_A``$. Mismatches emit `E0300`. 4. **Affine Offsets**: Summing interval quantities ($``o_A,o_B\ne 0``$) emits `E0300`. Difference ($``o_A=o_B``$) yields ratio scale ($``o_E=0``$). Offsets combine as $``o_E=o_A``$. 5. **Cascade Suppression**: Violations emit `E0300`, assign sentinel $``\bot_{\text{dim}}``$, and suppress parent diagnostics. ---
                      The metrology engine SHALL compute and validate dimension vectors for multiplication ($A \cdot B$), division ($A / B$), and reciprocal ($1 / B$) via vector addition, subtraction, and negation in $``\mathbb{Q}^7``$. Lowering MUST enforce: 1. **Multiplication**: $E = A \cdot B$ evaluates to dimension sum $``\mathbf{d}_{A \cdot B} = \mathbf{d}_A + \mathbf{d}_B``$ and scale product $``c_{A \cdot B} = c_A \cdot c_B``$. Identity $``\mathbf{0}``$ satisfies $``\mathbf{d} + \mathbf{0} = \mathbf{d}``$. 2. **Division & Reciprocal**: $E = A / B$ evaluates to dimension difference $``\mathbf{d}_{A / B} = \mathbf{d}_A - \mathbf{d}_B``$ and scale quotient $``c_{A / B} = c_A / c_B``$. Reciprocal $E = 1 / B$ evaluates to $``\mathbf{d}_{1 / B} = -\mathbf{d}_B``$ and $``c_{1 / B} = 1 / c_B``$. If $``\mathbf{d}_A \equiv \mathbf{d}_B``$, division yields identity $\mathbf{0}$. 3. **Affine Prohibition**: Operands MUST belong to ratio scales ($o = 0$). Offsets $o \ne 0$ emit diagnostic `E0300`. 4. **Zero Divisor & Bounds**: Compile-time constant zero divisor ($``v_B = 0``$) emits `E0300` with sentinel $``\bot_{\text{dim}}``$. Exponents $``d_i = p_i / q_i``$ require $``|p_i|, q_i \le 32767``$; overflow emits `E0300`. ---
                      The metrology engine and type checker of Subsystem 5 SHALL enforce that all arguments to transcendental and trigonometric functions evaluate strictly to the dimensionless null vector $\mathbf{0} \in \mathbb{Q}^7$ over the seven ISQ base dimensions. Evaluated results MUST likewise yield $``\mathbf{d}_{\text{result}} = \mathbf{0} \in \mathbb{Q}^7``$. The metrology type checker MUST enforce five core invariants: 1. **Function Family**: Governs $``\mathcal{F}_{\text{trans}}``$ (trigonometric, hyperbolic, exponential, logarithmic) and binary forms ($\operatorname{atan2}$, $``\log_B``$). 2. **Dimensionless Argument**: For $f(E)$ with $``f \in \mathcal{F}_{\text{trans}}``$, argument dimension MUST satisfy $\mathbf{d}(E) \equiv \mathbf{0}$; violations emit `E0300`, setting $\mathbf{d}(f(E)) = \mathbf{0}$. 3. **Multi-Argument**: $``\operatorname{atan2}(E_y, E_x)``$ requires $``\mathbf{d}(E_y) \equiv \mathbf{d}(E_x)``$, yielding $\mathbf{d} = \mathbf{0}$; mismatches emit `E0300`. Logarithms $``\log_B(E)``$ and variable powers require $\mathbf{d} \equiv \mathbf{0}$; violations emit `E0300`. 4. **Angular Units**: Angle units (`rad`, `deg`) define dimensionless ratios ($\mathbf{d} = \mathbf{0}$); trigonometric arguments convert to radians, and inverse functions yield $\mathbf{d} = \mathbf{0}$ with unit `rad`. 5. **Taylor Homogeneity**: Per Buckingham $\pi$, analytic $``f(x) = \sum_{k=0}^{\infty} c_k x^k``$ with scalar $``c_0 \ne 0``$ requires $k \cdot \mathbf{d}(x) = \mathbf{0}$, forcing $\mathbf{d}(x) \equiv \mathbf{0}$ for $k \ge 1$. ---
                      The engine SHALL compute and validate 7D dimension vectors and scale factors for rational power expressions ($A^k$, $\operatorname{pow}(A, k)$, $\operatorname{sqrt}(A)$, $\operatorname{cbrt}(A)$, $\operatorname{root}(A, n)$) with base dimension $``\mathbf{d}_A \in \mathbb{Q}^7``$ and rational exponent $k = p/q \in \mathbb{Q}$ ($p \in \mathbb{Z}, q \in \mathbb{Z}^+, \gcd(|p|, q) = 1$), evaluating $``\mathbf{d}_{A^k} = k \cdot \mathbf{d}_A \in \mathbb{Q}^7``$. ---
                      The compiler SHALL partition flow networks into continuous linear subgraphs solved via sparse LU and hybrid switched junctions formulated as a Linear Complementarity Problem (LCP), solved via Lemke pivoting bounded by iteration cutoff $``\kappa_{\text{pivot}}``$. Lowering MUST enforce: 1. **Network Partitioning**: Partition multigraph $``\mathcal{G}_{\text{flow}}=(\mathcal{V}_{\text{junc}},\mathcal{E}_{\text{flow}})``$ into continuous branches $``\mathcal{E}_{\text{lin}}``$ and switched branches $``\mathcal{E}_{\text{switch}}``$, fixing reference $``J_{\text{ref}}``$ ($``e_{\text{ref}}=0``$). 2. **Sparse LU Factorization**: Assemble conductance $``\mathbf{K}=\mathbf{A}_{\text{lin}}\mathbf{G}\mathbf{A}_{\text{lin}}^T``$ and reduced matrix $``\mathbf{K}_{\text{red}}``$, solving $``\mathbf{K}_{\text{red}}\mathbf{e}=\mathbf{f}_{\text{ext}}``$. Rank deficiency ($\text{rank}\lt n-1$) emits `E0301`. 3. **Canonical LCP Formulation**: Switched branches pair flow $``z_k\ge 0``$ with drop $``w_k\ge 0``$. Schur reduction yields $\operatorname{LCP}(\mathbf{M},\mathbf{q})$: $\mathbf{w}-\mathbf{M}\mathbf{z}=\mathbf{q}$, $\mathbf{w}\ge\mathbf{0}$, $\mathbf{z}\ge\mathbf{0}$, $\mathbf{w}^T\mathbf{z}=0$, with matrix $``\mathbf{M}=\mathbf{A}_{\text{switch}}^T\mathbf{K}_{\text{red}}^{-1}\mathbf{A}_{\text{switch}}``$ and offset $``\mathbf{q}=\mathbf{A}_{\text{switch}}^T\mathbf{K}_{\text{red}}^{-1}\mathbf{f}_{\text{ext}}+\mathbf{q}_0``$. 4. **Lemke Pivot Solver**: Solve $\operatorname{LCP}(\mathbf{M},\mathbf{q})$ with vector $``\mathbf{d}_{\text{aux}}=\mathbf{1}``$ and bound $``N_{\text{pivot}}\le\kappa_{\text{pivot}}``$ (default $4m^2$). Driving $``z_0=0``$ yields solution $(\mathbf{w}^*,\mathbf{z}^*)$. Cutoff or ray termination ($``z_0\gt 0``$) emits `E0399`. 5. **Dimensional Homogeneity**: Drops $``w_k``$ and flows $``z_k``$ MUST conform to $``\mathbf{d}_{\text{across}},\mathbf{d}_{\text{through}}\in\mathbb{Q}^7``$, summing to power $[M]^1[L]^2[T]^{-3}$; mismatches emit `E0300`. ---
                      The flow solver SHALL classify all connections $``f \in \mathcal{F}_{\text{flow}}``$ into Conservative ($``\mathcal{F}_{\text{cons}}``$) or Non-Conservative ($``\mathcal{F}_{\text{noncons}}``$) flows. Lowering MUST enforce: 1. **Conservative Flows ($``\mathcal{F}_{\text{cons}}``$)**: Classified as conservative if both ports are acausal with conjugate Across-Through pairs in $``\mathbb{Q}^7``$ satisfying $``\mathbf{d}_e+\mathbf{d}_f \equiv \mathbf{d}_{\text{power}} = (1,2,-3,0,0,0,0)``$, synthesizing Kirchhoff constraints ($``\mathbf{A}_{\text{cons}}\mathbf{f}=\mathbf{0}``$, $``\mathbf{B}_{\text{cons}}\mathbf{\Delta e}=\mathbf{0}``$). 2. **Non-Conservative Flows ($``\mathcal{F}_{\text{noncons}}``$)**: Flows linking directional ports (`in`, `out`) lacking conjugate pairs evaluate in causal DAG $``\mathcal{G}_{\text{causal}}``$ with broadcast fan-out. 3. **Disjoint Partition & Diagnostics**: Sets must be disjoint ($``\mathcal{F}_{\text{cons}} \cap \mathcal{F}_{\text{noncons}} = \emptyset``$). Incompatible hybrid connections or power invariant violations emit `E0300`. Multiple unarbitrated drivers emit `E0201`. ---
                      The metrology engine SHALL validate conservative interfaces using dual conjugate variable pairs $(e, f)$ whose dimensional product evaluates to universal Power $``\mathbf{d}_{\text{Power}} = (1, 2, -3, 0, 0, 0, 0) \in \mathbb{Q}^7``$. Lowering MUST enforce: 1. **Conjugate Declaration**: Conservative elements declare pairs $(e, f) \in \mathbb{Q}^7 \times \mathbb{Q}^7$ of Across effort $e$ and Through flow $f$. 2. **Power Invariant**: Addition requires $``\mathbf{d}(e) + \mathbf{d}(f) \equiv \mathbf{d}_{\text{Power}}``$. Mismatches emit `E0301`; zero denominators emit `E0300`. 3. **Domain Closure**: Abstract pairs (`Port_Alpha`, `Effort_Var`, `Flow_Var`) verify closure in $\mathbb{Q}^7$: Potential, Dynamic, Rotational, and Volumetric pairs each sum to $``\mathbf{d}_{\text{Power}}``$. 4. **Interconnect Compatibility**: Connecting ports $``P_1, P_2``$ requires $``\mathbf{d}(e_{P_1}) \equiv \mathbf{d}(e_{P_2})``$ and $``\mathbf{d}(f_{P_1}) \equiv \mathbf{d}(f_{P_2})``$, synthesizing $``f_{P_1} + f_{P_2} = 0``$. Mismatches emit `E0300`. 5. **Constitutive Homogeneity**: Parameters satisfy $\mathbf{d}(R) = \mathbf{d}(e) - \mathbf{d}(f)$, $``\mathbf{d}(C) = \mathbf{d}(f) + \mathbf{e}_T - \mathbf{d}(e)``$, and $``\mathbf{d}(I) = \mathbf{d}(e) + \mathbf{e}_T - \mathbf{d}(f)``$. Mismatches emit `E0300`. Non-conservative interfaces bypass checks. ---
                      The network solver SHALL synthesize generalized Kirchhoff Flow Law (KFL) continuity equations at conservative junctions. Lowering MUST enforce: 1. **Flow Continuity**: Ideal junctions $``J_i \in \mathcal{V}_{\text{ideal}}``$ require $``\sum \sigma_{i, e} c_e f_e(t) = 0``$ ($``\sigma_{i, e} \in \{+1, -1\}``$, $``c_e \in \mathbb{Q}^+``$), giving $``\mathbf{A}_{\text{ideal}} \mathbf{C}_{\text{unit}} \mathbf{f}(t) = \mathbf{0}``$. 2. **Dynamic Storage**: Accumulating junctions $``J_i \in \mathcal{V}_{\text{accum}}``$ satisfy $``\sum \sigma_{i, e} c_e f_e(t) = \frac{d S_i}{dt}(t)``$ with $``\mathbf{d}(S_i) \equiv \mathbf{d}_{\text{through}} + [T]^1``$; mismatches emit `E0300`. 3. **Homogeneity**: Incident branches require $``\mathbf{d}(e_a) \equiv \mathbf{d}(e_b)``$ in $\mathbb{Q}^7$ (mismatches emit `E0300`); units scale via $``c_e \in \mathbb{Q}^+``$. 4. **Rank Defect**: Components $``\mathcal{K}_c``$ have rank defect 1 ($``\text{rank}(\mathbf{A}_c) = |\mathcal{V}_c| - 1``$); datum elimination yields full-rank $``\mathbf{A}_{\text{reduced}}``$. 5. **Static Balance**: Imbalance emits `E0301`. Dangling degree-1 junctions with flow emit `E0220` or `E0301`. ---
                      The network solver SHALL synthesize generalized Kirchhoff Potential Law (KPL) equations across conservative loops. Lowering MUST enforce: 1. **Cycle Basis**: Spanning forest $\mathcal{T}$ on $``\mathcal{G}_{\text{flow}}``$ ($|\mathcal{K}|$ components) leaves chords $``e_k \in \mathcal{E}_{\text{chord}}``$ ($``N_C = |\mathcal{E}_{\text{flow}}| - |\mathcal{V}_{\text{junc}}| + |\mathcal{K}|``$), inducing fundamental cycles $``\mathcal{L}_k``$. 2. **Cycle Matrix**: Assembles $``\mathbf{B} = [\mathbf{B}_T \mid \mathbf{I}_{N_C}]``$ ($``B_{k, e} \in \{+1, -1, 0\}``$), enforcing $\mathbf{B} \mathbf{\Delta e}(t) = \mathbf{0}$. Cycles satisfy $\oint \Delta e = 0$. 3. **Datum Potential**: Datum $``J_{\text{ref}, m}``$ sets $``e(J_{\text{ref}, m}) = 0``$; $``\mathbf{\Delta e} = \mathbf{A}_{\text{red}}^T \mathbf{e}_{\text{node}}``$ ensures $\mathbf{B} \mathbf{\Delta e} = \mathbf{0}$ since $\mathbf{B} \mathbf{A}^T = \mathbf{0}$. 4. **Homogeneity**: Loop branches require $``\mathbf{d}_{\text{across}}(e_a) \equiv \mathbf{d}_{\text{across}}(e_b)``$ in $\mathbb{Q}^7$; mismatches emit `E0300`. 5. **Static Balance**: Imbalance $``\sum B_{k, e} \Delta e_e \ne 0``$ emits `E0301`. ---
                      The network solver SHALL construct incidence matrix $\mathbf{A}\in\{-1,0,1\}^{n\times b}$ for network $``\mathcal{G}_{\text{flow}}=(\mathcal{V}_{\text{junc}},\mathcal{E}_{\text{flow}})``$, verify topological rank, and synthesize cut-set and cycle matrices. Lowering MUST enforce: 1. **Incidence Assembly**: Branch $``e_j=(u_j,v_j)``$ sets $``A_{i,j}=+1``$ at source $``u_j``$, $``A_{i,j}=-1``$ at target $``v_j``$, and $0$ elsewhere, with $``\sum_{i=1}^n A_{i,j}=0``$. Self-loops ($``u_j=v_j``$) emit `E0203`. 2. **Rank Solvability**: Components $``\mathcal{K}_c``$ require $\text{rank}(\mathbf{A})=n-p$ where $p=|\mathcal{K}|$. Single components ($p=1$) have defect 1 ($\text{rank}(\mathbf{A})=n-1$). Deficiencies emit `E0301`. 3. **Reduced Incidence**: Designating datum $``J_{\text{ref},m}``$ per component ($``e(J_{\text{ref},m})=0``$) yields full-rank $``\mathbf{A}_{\text{red}}\in\{-1,0,1\}^{(n-p)\times b}``$ with $``\text{rank}(\mathbf{A}_{\text{red}})=n-p``$. 4. **Duality**: Spanning forest $\mathcal{T}$ partitions tree $``\mathcal{E}_{\text{tree}}``$ and chords $``\mathcal{E}_{\text{chord}}``$, giving $``\mathbf{A}_{\text{red}}=[\mathbf{A}_T\mid\mathbf{A}_C]``$ with $``\det(\mathbf{A}_T)\in\{-1,+1\}``$. Cut-set $``\mathbf{Q}=[\mathbf{I}_{n-p}\mid\mathbf{Q}_C]``$ ($``\mathbf{Q}_C=\mathbf{A}_T^{-1}\mathbf{A}_{\text{red}}``$) requires $\mathbf{Q}\mathbf{f}=\mathbf{0}$. Cycle $``\mathbf{B}=[-\mathbf{Q}_C^T\mid\mathbf{I}_{b-n+p}]``$ requires $\mathbf{B}\mathbf{\Delta e}=\mathbf{0}$. 5. **Orthogonality**: Requires $\mathbf{A}\mathbf{B}^T=\mathbf{0}$, $\mathbf{Q}\mathbf{B}^T=\mathbf{0}$, $\mathbf{f}^T\mathbf{\Delta e}=0$, and $``\mathbf{Y}_{\text{node}}=\mathbf{A}_{\text{red}}\mathbf{Y}\mathbf{A}_{\text{red}}^T\succ 0``$. Common junctions require $``\mathbf{d}_{\text{through}}\in\mathbb{Q}^7``$ (mismatches emit `E0300`). Degree $\le 1$ junctions emit `E0220`. ---
                      The network solver SHALL verify power product balance across closed conservative boundaries $\Omega$. Lowering MUST enforce: 1. **Port Power**: Ports $``P_k \in \mathcal{P}_{\text{ext}}``$ bind $``(e_k, f_k)``$ with $``P_k(t) = e_k(t) f_k(t)``$ and $``c_k \in \mathbb{Q}^+``$. Mismatches against $``\mathbf{d}_{\text{Power}}``$ emit `E0300`. External power satisfies $``P_{\text{ext}}(t) = \sum \sigma_k c_k P_k(t) = P_{\text{in}}(t) - P_{\text{out}}(t)``$. 2. **Storage Rate**: States $``S_s \in \mathcal{S}_{\text{storage}}``$ require $``\mathbf{d}(E_{\text{internal}}) \equiv \mathbf{d}_{\text{Energy}}``$ and $``\mathbf{d}(\frac{dE}{dt}) \equiv \mathbf{d}_{\text{Power}}``$; mismatches emit `E0300`. 3. **Dissipation Non-Negativity**: Dissipation satisfies $``P_{\text{dissipated}}(t) \ge 0``$; negative dissipation ($``P_{\text{dissipated}} \lt 0``$) without active sources emits `E0301`. 4. **Power Balance**: Assemblies enforce $``P_{\text{in}}(t) = P_{\text{out}}(t) + \frac{d E_{\text{internal}}}{dt}(t) + P_{\text{dissipated}}(t)``$. Static imbalance emits `E0301`. 5. **Passivity Invariant**: Passive models require $``\int_0^T P_{\text{ext}}(t) \, dt \ge -E_{\text{initial}}``$ for all $T \ge 0$; violations emit `E0301`. ---
                      The metrology engine SHALL validate parameters and signals against declared operational envelopes $``[v_{\min}, v_{\max}] \subset \overline{\mathbb{R}}``$. Lowering MUST enforce: 1. **Closed Intervals**: Envelopes $``\mathcal{E}_x = [v_{\min}, v_{\max}]``$ require $``v_{\min} \le v_{\max}``$; inversions emit `E0300`. Singletons ($``v_{\min} = v_{\max}``$) are valid. 2. **Homogeneity**: Bounds and operating points require $``\mathbf{d} \equiv \mathbf{d}_{\mathcal{E}} \in \mathbb{Q}^7``$ (mismatches emit `E0300`); units scale via $c \in \mathbb{Q}^+$. 3. **Containment**: Values $``v \in \{v_{\text{const}}, v_{\text{nom}}, v_{\text{init}}, v_{\text{default}}\}``$ require $``v_{\min} \le v \le v_{\max}``$; violations emit `E0301`. Endpoints are valid. 4. **Monotonic Hierarchy**: Nested tiers require $``\mathcal{E}_{\text{normal}} \subseteq \mathcal{E}_{\text{extended}} \subseteq \mathcal{E}_{\text{safety}}``$ ($``v_{\min}^{\text{safe}} \le v_{\min}^{\text{norm}} \le v_{\max}^{\text{norm}} \le v_{\max}^{\text{safe}}``$); inversions emit `E0300`. 5. **Interconnects**: Connected ports require $``\mathcal{E}_1 \cap \mathcal{E}_2 \ne \emptyset``$; disjoint envelopes emit `E0301`. Signals synthesize assertions $``v_{\min} \le x(t) \le v_{\max}``$. ---
                      The metrology engine SHALL perform static boundary value analysis (BVA), verifying tolerance envelopes satisfy safety bounds. Lowering MUST enforce: 1. **Tolerance Hyperbox**: Parameters $``x_i``$ declare nominal $``x_{i,0}``$ and tolerances $``\delta_i^-,\delta_i^+ \ge 0``$, defining interval $``\mathcal{I}(x_i) = [x_{i,0}-\delta_i^-, x_{i,0}+\delta_i^+]``$ and box $``\mathcal{B} = \prod \mathcal{I}(x_i)``$. Inverted bounds emit `E0301`. 2. **Response Extrema**: For $y = f(\mathbf{x})$, computes range $``\mathcal{R}_y = [y_{\min}, y_{\max}]``$. Affine forms evaluate in $O(k)$; general expressions compute enclosure $``[y_{\min}^{\text{IA}}, y_{\max}^{\text{IA}}]``$ via interval arithmetic. 3. **Safety Containment**: Verifies $``[y_{\min}, y_{\max}] \subseteq [Y_{\text{lower\_limit}}, Y_{\text{upper\_limit}}]``$. Breaches emit `E0301`; passes record margins $``\mu_{\text{lower}}, \mu_{\text{upper}} \ge 0``$. 4. **Homogeneity**: Requires $``\mathbf{d}(x_i) \equiv \mathbf{d}(\delta_i)``$ and $``\mathbf{d}(y) \equiv \mathbf{d}(f(\mathbf{x})) \equiv \mathbf{d}(Y_{\text{limit}})``$ in $\mathbb{Q}^7$; mismatches emit `E0300`. Units scale via $``c_u \in \mathbb{Q}^+``$. 5. **Symbolic Synthesis**: Lowers verified bounds into IR assertion nodes and SMT-LIB2 clauses. ---
                      The dynamics solver SHALL assign interval bounds $``[t_{\text{start}}, t_{\text{end}}] \subset \mathbb{R} \cup \{-\infty, +\infty\}``$ to lifecycles, actions, and states referenced to epoch $``t_{\text{epoch}} = 0``$. Lowering MUST enforce: 1. **Interval Bounds**: Intervals require $``t_{\text{start}} \le t_{\text{end}}``$ and $``t_{\text{start}} \ge 0``$. Inversions ($``t_{\text{start}} \gt t_{\text{end}}``$) or negative coordinates emit `E0400`. 2. **Lifecycle Dichotomy**: Events require $``t_{\text{start}} = t_{\text{end}}``$ ($\text{duration} = 0$). Durative occurrences require $``t_{\text{start}} \lt t_{\text{end}}``$ ($\text{duration} \gt 0$). Violations emit `E0400`. 3. **Duration Consistency**: Nominal $``\delta_{\text{nom}} \ge 0``$ requires $``|(t_{\text{end}} - t_{\text{start}}) - \delta_{\text{nom}}| \le \epsilon_{\text{tol}}``$ ($``\epsilon_{\text{tol}} = 10^{-9}``$). Envelopes require $``\delta_{\min} \le t_{\text{end}} - t_{\text{start}} \le \delta_{\max}``$. Breaches emit `E0400`. 4. **Hierarchical Containment**: Sub-occurrences ($``o_{\text{sub}} \subseteq_{\text{occ}} o_{\text{super}}``$) require $``[t_{\text{start}}(o_{\text{sub}}), t_{\text{end}}(o_{\text{sub}})] \subseteq [t_{\text{start}}(o_{\text{super}}), t_{\text{end}}(o_{\text{super}})]``$; breaches emit `E0401`. 5. **State Continuity**: Sequential states satisfy $``t_{\text{end}}(S_i) = t(\tau) = t_{\text{start}}(S_{i+1})``$. Exclusive state overlaps emit `E0401`. ---
                      The dynamics solver SHALL implement an axiomatic solver for Allen's 13 qualitative interval relations over occurrences, actions, and states. Lowering MUST enforce: 1. **Well-Formedness**: Interval `Interval_X` $``= [x_s, x_e]``$ on $\mathbb{R}$ SHALL satisfy $``x_s \lt x_e``$. Inverted ($``x_s \gt x_e``$) or degenerate ($``x_s = x_e``$) bounds emit `E0400`. 2. **JEPD Relations**: Classifies pairs into $``\mathcal{B}_{13}``$ in $O(1)$; conflicts with assertions emit `E0400`. 3. **Bitmask Algebra**: Encodes relations as $``\mathbf{m}_R \in [0, 8191]``$; evaluates boolean algebra and converse ($R^\smile$). Empty intersection emits `E0401`. 4. **Symmetry**: Mandates identity $R(X, X) \equiv \{ \mathbf{eq} \}$ (breaches emit `E0400`) and converse symmetry $R(Y, X) \equiv (R(X, Y))^\smile$ (contradictions emit `E0401`). 5. **Difference Lowering**: Lowers relations into difference inequalities $u - v \le c$ ($``u, v \in \{ x_s, x_e, y_s, y_e \}``$) with guard $``\epsilon_{\text{dur}} \gt 0``$. ---
                      The dynamics solver SHALL perform path consistency constraint propagation using Allen's $13 \times 13$ composition table, verifying qualitative temporal constraints. Lowering MUST enforce: 1. **Matrix Model**: Encodes `TemporalNetwork_Alpha` as matrix $``\mathbf{M} \in (2^{\mathcal{B}_{13}})^{N \times N}``$. Diagonals initialize to $\{ \mathbf{eq} \} = 0\text{x}1000$; unconstrained off-diagonals to $\mathbf{U} = 0\text{x}1\text{FFF}$. Assertion $``C(X_i, X_j) = R``$ sets $\mathbf{M}[i, j] \leftarrow R$ and $\mathbf{M}[j, i] \leftarrow R^\smile$. 2. **Composition Table**: Precomputes 169 compositions $``\mathbf{T}_{\text{comp}}[r_1][r_2]``$ as 13-bit masks. Disjunctive composition $``R_1 \circ R_2``$ evaluates in $O(1)$ via bitwise OR over active bits. 3. **Queue-Driven PC-2**: Queue $Q$ tracks revised pairs. For popped $(i, j)$ and vertex $k$, updates $\mathbf{M}[k, j] \leftarrow \mathbf{M}[k, j] \cap (\mathbf{M}[k, i] \circ \mathbf{M}[i, j])$ and converse $\mathbf{M}[j, k] \leftarrow (\mathbf{M}[k, j])^\smile$. 4. **Monotonic Convergence**: Enforces $\mathbf{M}^{(t+1)}[i, j] \subseteq \mathbf{M}^{(t)}[i, j]$, terminating within $13 \cdot N(N - 1)$ insertions since cells prune at most 13 times. 5. **Conflict Rejection**: Emptied cells ($\mathbf{M}[i, j] = \emptyset$) emit `E0400`; reflexivity breaches ($\mathbf{eq} \notin \mathbf{M}[i, i]$) emit `E0401`. ---
                      The temporal solver SHALL enforce consistency over lifecycles and interval constraints. Lowering MUST enforce: 1. **Formulation**: Lifecycles $o \in \mathcal{O}$ define $``I(o) = [t_{\text{start}}, t_{\text{end}}]``$. Constraints $``C_{ij}``$ bind masks $``\mathbf{m}_{R(i, j)} \in [0, 8191]``$ over $``\mathcal{B}_{13}``$ with symmetry $``R(o_j, o_i) \equiv (R(o_i, o_j))^\smile``$. 2. **ORD-Horn Filter**: Membership $``R(o_i, o_j) \in \mathcal{H}_{\text{ORD}}``$ evaluates in $O(1)$ time. Tractable components route to path consistency; others route to difference logic SMT. 3. **Path Consistency**: Solves ORD-Horn networks via $``R(o_i, o_k) \leftarrow R(o_i, o_k) \cap (R(o_i, o_j) \circ R(o_j, o_k))``$. Contradictions ($R = \emptyset$) emit `E0400`. 4. **Difference Logic**: General networks lower to QF_RDL formula $``\Phi_{\text{temporal}}``$ over $``\{t_{i, s}, t_{i, e}\}``$, enforcing duration guards and selector clauses. 5. **Bounded SMT**: General networks (NP-1) solve under budget $``\kappa_{\text{temporal}}``$. Unsatisfiability emits `E0400`; step exhaustion emits `E0406`. ---
                      The dynamics solver SHALL construct directed causal precedence graph $``G_{\text{prec}} = (V, E)``$ across action executions, behavioral steps, and state transitions, asserting acyclicity to guarantee deadlock-free execution. ---
                      The dynamics engine SHALL lower action sequences, fork nodes, and join nodes into execution DAGs, verifying precedence, barrier synchronization, and data-race freedom. Lowering MUST enforce: 1. **Sequential Precedence**: Steps $``\langle s_1, \dots, s_n \rangle``$ with $``(s_i, s_{i+1}) \in E_{\text{ctrl}}``$ require $``t_{\text{end}}(s_i) \le t_{\text{start}}(s_{i+1})``$; immediate chaining requires equality. Inversions emit `E0400`. 2. **Fork Semantics**: $``N_{\text{fork}}``$ requires $\text{in-deg} = 1$ and fan-out $k \ge 2$ (faults emit `E0400`), replicating tokens across $``P_1, \dots, P_k``$ at $``t_{\text{start}}(P_i) = t_{\text{end}}(N_{\text{fork}})``$. 3. **Barrier Synchronization**: $``N_{\text{join}}``$ requires $\text{in-deg} = k \ge 2$ and $\text{out-deg} = 1$ (faults emit `E0400`), synchronizing at $``t_{\text{start}}(N_{\text{join}}) = \max_i t_{\text{end}}(P_i)``$; early dispatch emits `E0404`. 4. **Token Conservation**: $``N_{\text{join}}``$ MUST consume $k$ tokens ($``\Delta\text{Tokens}_{\text{net}} = 0``$). Deficits or unjoined paths emit `E0400`. 5. **Bernstein Independence**: Concurrent branches $``P_i, P_j``$ require pairwise disjoint read/write sets ($``\mathcal{W}_i \cap \mathcal{W}_j = \emptyset``$, $``\mathcal{W}_i \cap \mathcal{R}_j = \emptyset``$); hazards emit `E0404`. $``G_{\text{exec}}``$ must be acyclic; cycles emit `E0400`. ---
                      The state machine solver SHALL validate and lower hierarchical statecharts and orthogonal regions into active configurations. Lowering MUST enforce: 1. **Tree Acyclicity**: States form rooted tree $(S, \sqsubseteq)$. States $``s \ne s_{\text{root}}``$ require unique $\text{parent}(s)$; cycles ($s \sqsubset^+ s$) or multi-parents emit `E0402`. Duplicate sibling names emit `E0402`. 2. **Taxonomic Partitioning**: States partition into atomic leaves $``\mathcal{S}_{\text{atomic}}``$, XOR composites $``\mathcal{S}_{\text{xor}}``$ (activating $\le 1$ child), AND composites $``\mathcal{S}_{\text{orth}}``$ ($m \ge 2$ regions), regions $\mathcal{R}$, and pseudo-states $\mathcal{P}$. 3. **Region Disjointness**: Orthogonal states require $m \ge 2$ regions; degenerate states emit `E0405`. Regions $``R_i \ne R_j``$ partition states into disjoint sets ($``\text{States}(R_i) \cap \text{States}(R_j) = \emptyset``$). Direct cross-region transitions emit `E0405`. 4. **Active Configurations**: Requires $``s_{\text{root}} \in C``$, ancestor closure $\text{ancestors}(s) \subseteq C$ (emits `E0402`), XOR singularity $|C \cap \mathcal{C}| = 1$ (emits `E0402`), and region concurrency $``|C \cap \text{Leaves}(R_i)| = 1``$ (emits `E0405`). 5. **LCA Scope & Synchronization**: Transition scope is $``\text{LCA}(s_{\text{src}}, s_{\text{tgt}})``$. Concurrent leaves $``l_1 \ne l_2 \in \text{Leaves}(C)``$ require $``\text{LCA}(l_1, l_2) \in \mathcal{S}_{\text{orth}}``$ (XOR LCA emits `E0402`). Cross-region transitions synchronize via fork/join nodes. ---
                      The state machine solver SHALL validate and lower discrete event dispatching under Run-to-Completion (RTC) semantics with a bounded FIFO event queue. Lowering MUST enforce: 1. **Queue Semantics**: Events partition into Signal, Call, Time, Change, and Completion. External events enqueue at FIFO tail ($``K_{\text{max\_queue}}=65536``$); completion events precede external stimuli. Overflow ($``|Q|\ge K_{\text{max\_queue}}``$) or non-positive intervals ($``\delta_{\text{timer}}\le 0``$) emit `E0400`. 2. **RTC Non-Interruptibility**: Steps execute atomically from head event $e$. Arriving events buffer at tail without preemption or state mutation. Dequeuing $``e_{i+1}``$ requires quiescence and action completion. 3. **Trigger Matching**: Transition $\tau$ matches $e$ iff trigger, kind, and payload conform ($``\text{type}(\pi_e)\sqsubseteq\text{type}(\text{param}(\tau))``$); faults emit `E0400`. Satisfied guards enable transitions; ambiguous overlapping sibling guards emit `E0400`. 4. **Priority & Deferral**: Deeper states take priority ($``\tau_1\succ\tau_2\iff\text{depth}(\text{source}(\tau_1))\gt\text{depth}(\text{source}(\tau_2))``$). Invalid containment emits `E0402`. States may defer events to $``\mathcal{Q}_{\text{defer}}``$; conflicting trigger/deferral emits `E0400`. Unhandled events discard safely. 5. **Orthogonal Concurrency**: Events dispatch across regions, firing $\le 1$ transition per region without races. ---
                      The compiler SHALL verify that outgoing transitions from any state on identical events have mutually disjoint guards ($``G_1 \wedge G_2 \equiv \text{false}``$), ensuring determinism. Lowering MUST enforce: 1. **Trigger Partitioning**: Outgoing transitions from `State_Alpha` partition by trigger `Event_0` (or $\epsilon$). If $``|\mathcal{T}_{s, e}| \ge 2``$, checks execute across all $``\binom{|\mathcal{T}_{s, e}|}{2}``$ pairs. 2. **Mutual Exclusion**: Transitions `Transition_Alpha`, `Transition_Beta` on `Event_0` require $``\text{UNSAT}(\overline{G}_1 \land \overline{G}_2)``$; overlap or missing guards ($\text{true}$) emit `E0400`. 3. **Theory Admissibility**: Guards MUST evaluate to `Boolean` in decidable fragments (`PROP`, `QF_LRA`, `QF_LIA`). Non-linear terms or invalid types emit `E0402`. 4. **Bounded SMT Solving**: Solvers operate under budget $``\kappa_{\text{smt}} = 100{,}000``$; exhaustion emits `E0400`. Interval checks discharge 1D bounds in $O(1)$. 5. **Hierarchy Precedence**: Differing depths follow inner-first priority; sibling transitions at identical depth sharing `Event_0` MUST be disjoint, emitting `E0400`. ---
                      The solver SHALL analyze state machine reachability, diagnosing dead states, unreachable transitions, and trap states. Lowering MUST enforce: 1. **Initial Singularity**: Scopes require initial state $``s_0 \in \mathcal{S}``$ ($``|\{s \mid \text{is\_initial}(s)\}| = 1``$); faults emit `E0400`. State $``s_0``$ is reachable ($``s_0 \in \mathcal{R}``$). 2. **Fixed-Point Reachability**: Reachable set $\mathcal{R} \subseteq \mathcal{S}$ is least fixed point $``\mathcal{R} = \mu X. (\{s_0\} \cup \text{Post}(X))``$ via BFS/DFS over a visited bitset. $\text{Post}(X)$ evaluates transitions $\tau \in \mathcal{T}$ with satisfiable guards ($``\text{Sat}(g_\tau) \ne \text{false}``$). 3. **Dead States**: States lacking paths from $``s_0``$ ($``s \in \mathcal{D}_{\text{dead}} = \mathcal{S} \setminus \mathcal{R}``$) emit `E0400`, detecting isolated vertices and cyclic islands. 4. **Dead Transitions & Trap Sinks**: Transitions from dead states ($``s_{\text{src}} \in \mathcal{D}_{\text{dead}}``$) or with unsatisfiable guards emit `E0403`. Reachable non-final states lacking outgoing transitions are trap states ($``s \in \mathcal{D}_{\text{trap}}``$), emitting `E0403`. 5. **Hierarchy Propagation**: Unreachable composite state $``S_{\text{comp}} \in \mathcal{D}_{\text{dead}}``$ transitively invalidates nested states. Reachable composite states propagate reachability to internal initial states. ---
                      The solver SHALL verify reachability, deadlock freedom, and livelock absence across $K \ge 2$ orthogonal regions via Bounded Model Checking (BMC). Lowering MUST enforce: 1. **Cartesian Space**: States define $K$ regions ($``\mathcal{C}_{\text{global}}=\prod_{i=1}^K S_i``$) with exact-one active leaf per region ($``|C\cap\text{Leaves}(R_i)|=1``$). Unique root is $``s_0``$. 2. **SAT Unrolling**: Unrolls transitions into $``\Phi_k``$ ($``k\le k_{\text{max}}``$, default $50$), conjoining $``I(s_0)``$, transitions $``\bigwedge_{t=0}^{k-1} T(s_t,s_{t+1})``$, and violation $``\neg\text{Safe}(s_k)``$. 3. **Transition Relations**: Encodes interleavings, synchronized compound fork/join transitions, and stuttering ($``\mathbf{x}_i^{(t+1)}=\mathbf{x}_i^{(t)}``$). 4. **Deadlock & Livelock**: Deadlocks emit `E0400` with trace $\mathbf{w}$. Non-progress cycles emit `E0400`. Unreachable states emit `E0400`. 5. **Step Budget**: CDCL solver enforces budget $``\kappa_{\text{steps}}``$ ($2\times 10^5$); exceeding $``\kappa_{\text{steps}}``$ emits `E0406`. ---
                      The state machine solver SHALL validate failsafe fallback transitions, priority preemptive evacuation, and absorbing safe states across discrete statecharts. Validation MUST enforce: 1. **Fallback Completeness**: States $``s \in \mathcal{S}_{\text{op}}``$ and faults $``e_{\text{fault}} \in \mathcal{E}_{\text{fault}}``$ require transition $``T_{\text{failsafe}}``$ to $``s_{\text{safe}} \in \mathcal{S}_{\text{safe}}``$, defined on $s$ or inherited ($``s_{\text{src}} \in \text{scope}(s)``$); missing coverage emits `E0400`. 2. **Preemptive Priority**: Fallback transitions require priority $``\pi(T_{\text{failsafe}})``$ exceeding nominal transitions in scope ($``\\pi(T_{\text{failsafe}}) \gt \pi(T_{\text{nominal}})``$); inversions emit `E0410`. 3. **Priority Disjointness**: Fallback transitions from state $s$ or ancestors for identical faults require distinct priorities ($``\pi(T_1) \ne \pi(T_2)``$); conflicts emit `E0410`. 4. **Tautological Guard**: Guards must evaluate unconditionally to true ($g \equiv \text{true}$); non-tautological guards emit `E0410`. 5. **Safe State Absorption & Reset**: State $``s_{\text{safe}}``$ must be reachable via $``G_{\text{failsafe}}``$ (unreachable states emit `E0400`). State $``s_{\text{safe}}``$ is absorbing: spontaneous ($\epsilon$) or nominal exits emit `E0400`; exit requires certified event $``e_{\text{reset}} \in \mathcal{E}_{\text{reset}}``$. Transitions bind atomic safing actions $``A_{\text{safing}}``$. ---
                      The state machine solver SHALL validate and execute Shallow History (`[H]`) and Deep History (`[H*]`) restoration semantics. Lowering MUST enforce: 1. **Taxonomy**: Pseudostates partition into Shallow (`History_Shallow`) and Deep (`History_Deep`) within composite (`CompositeState_Alpha`), orthogonal composite, or region (`Region_1`). Root ($``s_{\text{root}}``$), leaf, or duplicate placement emits `E0400`. 2. **Default Transition**: Pseudostates MUST declare one unconditional transition $``T_{\text{default}}``$ ($``e_{\text{trig}} = \epsilon, g \equiv \text{true}``$) to child state ($``s_{\text{tgt}} \in \mathcal{C}_{\text{parent}}``$); violations emit `E0400`, external targets emit `E0411`. 3. **Non-Occupational**: History pseudostates cannot be in active configuration $C$ ($``C \cap \mathcal{P}_{\text{history}} = \emptyset``$); actions emit `E0400`. 4. **Snapshot & Reset**: Exiting $``S_{\text{comp}}``$ records active descendants: $``\mathcal{H}(S_{\text{comp}}) \leftarrow C \cap \text{descendants}(S_{\text{comp}})``$. Final state or reset clears history ($\mathcal{H} \leftarrow \emptyset$). 5. **Restoration**: Shallow (`[H]`) restores child $s^* \in \mathcal{H} \cap \mathcal{C}$ (or $``T_{\text{default}}``$ if $\mathcal{H} = \emptyset$), resolving initial transitions deeper. Deep (`[H*]`) restores descendants $``\mathcal{H}(S_{\text{comp}})``$ (or $``T_{\text{default}}``$ if $\mathcal{H} = \emptyset$) without initial transitions. Corrupted states emit `E0411`. 6. **Order**: Transition effect $\to$ container entry $\to$ default action or restored entry actions. ---
                      The dynamics engine SHALL provide a deterministic stepper (`SimulationStepper_Alpha`) and trace logger (`TraceLog_1`) stepping statecharts against event traces. Stepping MUST enforce: 1. **Configuration**: Tracks $``C = \langle \mathcal{S}_{\text{active}}, \mathcal{V}_{\text{env}}, \mathcal{Q}_{\text{events}}, t_{\text{sim}}, \kappa_{\text{step}} \rangle``$ from root $``s_0``$. Ancestor closure or XOR breaches emit `E0402`. 2. **Transition Selection**: Dequeued $e$ evaluates guards $``g_T``$. Conflicts resolve by depth, priority $\pi(T)$, and FQN order. Guard faults emit `E0400`. 3. **LCA Traversal**: Firing $T^*$ executes bottom-up exits to $``\text{LCA}(s_{\text{src}}, s_{\text{tgt}})``$, effect $``A_{\text{trans}}``$, and top-down entries. Spontaneous $\epsilon$-steps loop to quiescence; exceeding $``\kappa_{\text{micro\_max}}``$ emits `E0400`. 4. **Trace Logging**: Emits JSON trace (`TraceLog_1`) recording steps, timestamps, configurations, events, guards, firings, actions, and status, guaranteeing bitwise determinism. 5. **Halting**: Unmatched events record `Status::Quiescent`, preserving $C$. Final states with empty queues halt simulation (`Status::Terminal`). ---
                      The safety compiler SHALL build, validate, and query a deterministic 7-tier bipartite DAG (`TraceabilityGraph_Alpha`) $``G_{\text{trace}} = (V_{\text{trace}}, E_{\text{trace}})``$ linking requirements, design elements, interfaces, constraints, code, and witnesses. Validation MUST enforce: 1. **Disjoint Partitioning**: Vertices $``V_{\text{trace}}``$ partition into seven disjoint tiers: `Tier_1` ($``T_1``$, $``\mathcal{R}_{\text{mission}}``$), `Tier_2` ($``T_2``$, $``\mathcal{R}_{\text{system}}``$), `Tier_3` ($``T_3``$, $``\mathcal{C}_{\text{arch}}``$), `Tier_4` ($``T_4``$, $``\mathcal{P}_{\text{port}}``$), `Tier_5` ($``T_5``$, $``\mathcal{I}_{\text{safety}}``$), `Tier_6` ($``T_6``$, $``\mathcal{M}_{\text{code}}``$), and `Tier_7` ($``T_7``$, $``\mathcal{W}_{\text{verify}}``$). Unpartitioned or multi-tier entities emit `E0402`. 2. **Strict Adjacent Edges**: Edges $``(u, v) \in E_{\text{trace}}``$ MUST satisfy $``\tau_V(v) = \tau_V(u) + 1``$ within $``E_{\text{trace}} \subseteq \bigcup_{i=1}^6 (T_i \times T_{i+1})``$. Skip-tier, backward, and intra-tier edges emit `E0400`. 3. **Typing & Acyclicity**: Edges bind relations: `Refines`, `Allocates`, `Exposes`, `Guards`, `Enforces`, `Witnesses`. Monotonic tier steps guarantee acyclicity; cycles or conflicts emit `E0400`. 4. **Bidirectional Traversal**: Adjacency $\text{Adj}^+$ and transposed $\text{Adj}^-$ support forward $\text{Reach}^+$ and backward $\text{Reach}^-$ sweeps, indexing verification threads $``\langle v_1, \dots, v_7 \rangle``$. ---
                      The formal safety compiler SHALL enforce an upward allocation completeness gate (`AllocationGate_Alpha`) ensuring every system requirement allocates to architecture or safety invariants. Verification MUST enforce: 1. **Target Admissibility**: Allocation edge $``e_{\text{alloc}} = (r, e)``$ MUST connect $``r \in V_{\text{req}}``$ (`RequirementNode_0`) to $``e \in \mathcal{E}_{\text{target}} = T_3 \cup T_4 \cup T_5``$ (`Component_1`, `Port_1`, `Invariant_Safe_0`); external targets emit `E0400`. 2. **Completeness & Coverage**: Each $``r \in V_{\text{req}}``$ requires $|\text{Alloc}(r)| \ge 1$ (faults emit `E0400`). Global coverage $``\mu_{\text{alloc}}(V_{\text{req}})``$ MUST equal $1.0$; deficits emit `E0404`. 3. **Hierarchical Completeness**: Decomposed requirements require parent allocation ($|\text{Alloc}(r)| \ge 1$) or leaf allocation ($\forall c \in \text{Leaves}(r), |\text{Alloc}(c)| \ge 1$); unallocated leaves emit `E0400`. 4. **Irreflexivity & Acyclicity**: Allocations MUST be irreflexive ($``(r, r) \notin E_{\text{alloc}}``$) and acyclic over $``E_{\text{alloc}} \cup E_{\text{decomp}}``$; cycles emit `E0400`. 5. **Multi-Cardinality**: Supports 1-to-N and N-to-1 allocation mappings deterministically. ---
                      The safety compiler SHALL enforce downward realization completeness (`RealizationGate_Alpha`) across traceability DAG $``G_{\text{trace}}``$. Verification MUST enforce: 1. **Universal Realization**: Elements $``e \in V_{\text{elem}}``$ (classifiers, parts, ports, actions, states) MUST satisfy $``(r, e) \in E_{\text{realize}}``$ for requirement $``r \in V_{\text{req}}``$. Orphans emit `E0405`. 2. **Hierarchical Inheritance**: Direct realization links $r$ to $e$. Nested children ($``e_{\text{child}} \sqsubset^+ e_{\text{parent}}``$) inherit parent realizers. Elements pass when $|\text{Realizers}(e)| \ge 1$. 3. **Mission Grounding**: Realizing requirements $r \in \text{Realizers}(e)$ MUST trace to mission roots $``m \in V_{\text{mission}}``$. Ungrounded requirements emit `E0400`. 4. **Incidence Matrix**: Synthesis emits boolean matrix $``\mathbf{M}_{\text{realize}} \in \{0, 1\}^{|V_{\text{elem}}| \times |V_{\text{req}}|}``$ with row completeness ($``\sum_j M_{\text{realize}, i, j} \ge 1``$). ---
                      The verification engine SHALL enforce a Verification Witness Completeness Gate (`WitnessGate_Alpha`) across the traceability graph, asserting that all requirements are witnessed. The compiler MUST enforce: 1. **Witness Coverage**: Every $``r \in \mathcal{R}_{\text{all}}``$ MUST link to at least one witness $``w \in \mathcal{W}_{\text{verification}}``$ via $``(r, w) \in E_{\text{witness}}``$. Unwitnessed requirements ($``\text{deg}_{E_{\text{witness}}}(r) = 0``$) emit `E0407`. 2. **Method Rigor**: Witnesses declare $``\kappa_{\text{method}}(w) \in \{ \text{Test}, \text{Analysis}, \text{Inspection}, \text{Demonstration} \}``$. Safety invariant requirements in Tier 5 require `Test` or `Analysis`; other methods emit `E0400`. 3. **Reference Integrity**: Edges $(r, w)$ MUST resolve to defined entities. Dangling targets emit `E0400`. 4. **Verdict Certification**: Certification requires $\ge 1$ `Pass` and zero `Fail` verdicts; `Fail` verdicts emit `E0400`. 5. **Hierarchical Rollup**: Composite requirements satisfy completeness directly or via conjunction across all leaf descendants. ---
                      The safety compiler SHALL eliminate extraneous AST nodes and unreachable behaviors lacking reachability to root requirements. The analyzer (`DeadEliminator_1`) MUST evaluate reachability over traceability DAG (`SafetyGraph_Alpha`) from roots $``R_{\text{root}}``$. ---
                      The verification engine SHALL compute and verify Merkle root digest $``H_{\text{root}} \in \{0, 1\}^{256}``$ over 7-tier traceability graph `TraceGraph_Alpha`, emitting manifest `HashAttestation_0` (`MerkleTree_1`) to guarantee bitwise determinism. Attestation MUST enforce: 1. **Serialization**: $``V_{\text{trace}}``$ partitions into tiers $``T_1 \dots T_7``$. Nodes $u$ serialize to canonical payload $\text{Data}(u)$ ($``\tau_V``$, $``\Delta_V``$, FQN, digest). Unpartitioned nodes emit `E0400`. 2. **Child Sorting**: Children sort into canonical order $``\text{Children}_{\text{canon}}(u)``$ by tier, relation, FQN, and UUIDv5. Disordered iterations emit `E0400`. 3. **Bottom-Up Hashing**: Post-order hashing uses hash $H$ (BLAKE3/SHA-256). Leaves evaluate $``H(w) = H(\text{TAG}_{\text{leaf}} \mathbin{\Vert} \text{Data}(w))``$; internal nodes evaluate $``H(u) = H(\text{TAG}_{\text{node}} \mathbin{\Vert} \text{Data}(u) \mathbin{\Vert} k \mathbin{\Vert} H(v_1) \dots H(v_k))``$, memoizing diamond DAGs. 4. **Root Synthesis**: Root $``H_{\text{root}}``$ hashes graph metrics and sorted roots $``r_1 \prec \dots \prec r_m``$. Sub-hashes $``H(T_i)``$ isolate deltas. Mismatches emit `E0400`. 5. **Inclusion Proofs**: Proofs $\Pi(u)$ verify membership in $``O(\text{depth} \cdot d_{\max})``$ time. Forged proofs emit `E0409`. ---
                      The safety compiler SHALL extract and validate a Hierarchical Control Structure (HCS) topology from the AST, partitioning entities into disjoint sets: controllers ($C$), actuators ($E$), processes ($P$), and sensors ($O$). Lowering MUST enforce five topological invariants: 1. **Role Disjointness**: Controllers and processes SHALL be distinct per loop ($c \ne p$); interfaces disjoint ($E \cap O = \emptyset$). Conflicts emit `E0400`. 2. **Directed Flows**: Control actions bind $u=(c,e,p)\in\mathcal{U}$; feedbacks bind $y=(p,o,c)\in\mathcal{Y}$. Ports MUST follow directionality (`out` $\to$ `in` $\to$ `out` $\to$ `in`). Inversions or dangling interfaces emit `E0412`. 3. **Supervisory Stratification**: Levels $``\ell : C \cup P \to \mathbb{N}_0``$ assign base plants $\ell(p) = 0$ and supervisory flows $\ell(c) \gt \ell(x)$. Graphs MUST be acyclic DAGs; cycles emit `E0400`. 4. **Closed-Loop Observability**: Flows $(c, e, p) \in \mathcal{U}$ MUST pair with feedback $(p, o, c) \in \mathcal{Y}$ unless annotated `@open_loop`; omissions emit `E0400`. 5. **Process Model**: Controllers issuing actions MUST bind a process model ($``\mathcal{M}_{\text{proc}}(c)`` \in \mathcal{V}_{\text{AST}}``$); missing models emit `E0400`. ---
                      The safety compiler SHALL compute the minimal hitting set of constraints covering all declared hazards, ingesting hazards $\mathcal{H}$ and constraints $\mathcal{C}$ from the AST arena as an abstract hypergraph. ---
                      The safety engine SHALL execute combinatorial tensor expansion and context pruning across control actions, universal STPA guide words, and operational context states. Expansion and pruning MUST enforce: 1. **Control Actions & Guide Words**: Extracts actions $``A = \{ a_1, \dots, a_m \}``$ (`ControlAction_Alpha`) and binds 4-word alphabet $G$. Empty $A$ or malformed words emit `E0400`. 2. **Context States ($``S_{\text{context}}``$)**: Binds valuations $``s \in \prod_{j=1}^d D_j``$ ($``d \le d_{\max}``$). Inconsistent predicates emit `E0400`; overflow ($``d > d_{\max}``$, $``|U| > K_{\max}``$) emits `E0414`. 3. **Tensor Expansion ($U$)**: Constructs candidate tensor $``U = A \times G \times S_{\text{context}}``$ (`ContextTensor_0`) with $``|U| = 4 \cdot |A| \cdot |S_{\text{context}}|``$. 4. **Context Pruning**: Evaluates $``\Phi_{\text{reach}}``$, $``\Phi_{\text{active}}``$, and $``\Phi_{\text{hazard}}``$ (`Pruner_1`), pruning invalid tuples and retaining hazardous $``\mathcal{U}_{\text{pruned}} \subseteq U``$. 5. **Deterministic Reduction**: Evaluates tuples on work-stealing threads ($``P_{\text{workers}} \le N_{\text{max\_workers}}``$); canonical sorting guarantees bitwise parity; divergence emits `E0400`. Directives: UUIDv5 anchors (Directive 1); work-stealing ($``N_{\text{max\_workers}}``$) (Directive 2); symbol interning (Directive 3); recovery on `;` with sentinels ($``\bot_{\text{uca}}``$, $``\bot_{\text{tensor}}``$), halting at $``C_{\text{max\_errors}}``$ with `E0199` (Directive 4); Release budgets (Directive 5). Placeholders (`Package_0`, `ControlAction_Alpha`, `ContextTensor_0`, `Pruner_1`, `param_x : Real`) used. ---
                      The safety compiler SHALL synthesize Boolean safety invariants from hazard scenarios by generating the logical negation of hazardous state predicates over the state vector. ---
                      The safety compiler SHALL construct invariants as typed `ConstraintExpr` AST nodes and lower them to canonical CNF via De Morgan normalization and bounded Tseitin transformation. Pipeline rules: 1. **AST Nodes**: Allocates `ConstraintExpr` nodes (`ConstraintExpr_Alpha`) on terms (`param_x : Real`). Type errors emit `E0400`. 2. **De Morgan**: Rewrites $\implies, \iff, \oplus$ to $\neg, \land, \lor$. Pushes negations to leaves ($\neg(A \land B) \rightsquigarrow \neg A \lor \neg B$), drops double negations ($\neg\neg A \rightsquigarrow A$), and inverts duals ($``\neg(t_1 \lt t_2) \rightsquigarrow t_1 \ge t_2``$). 3. **CNF Lowering**: Distributes into clauses (`Clause_0`). Overflowing $``K_{\text{dist\_max}} = 256``$ triggers Tseitin transformations, enforcing linear $``O(|N_{\text{expr}}|)``$ clauses. 4. **Simplification**: Prunes tautologies ($l \lor \neg l$). Contradictions ($l \land \neg l$) emit `E0400`. Subsumes clauses ($``C_1 \subseteq C_2 \implies C_1``$). 5. **Sorting**: Sorts literals (`Literal_0`, `Literal_1`) and clauses lexicographically for thread parity. ---
                      The safety compiler SHALL synthesize FMECA records across four universal failure dimensions (Interface, State, Action, Resource) for every architectural component in the system AST. The synthesis engine MUST enforce: 1. **Component Decomposition**: Partitions $``C \in \mathcal{C}_{\text{arch}}``$ (`Component_Alpha`) elements into disjoint sets $``\text{Elements}_d(C)``$ (Interface `Port_1`, State `State_0`, Action `Action_0`, Resource `Resource_0`). Empty elements emit `E0400`. 2. **Failure Kinds Alphabets**: Binds 21 canonical failure kinds across Interface (6), State (5), Action (5), and Resource (5); malformed kinds emit `E0400`. 3. **Cartesian Synthesis**: Generates $``\mathcal{F}(C) = \bigcup_{d} \{ (c, d, m) \mid c \in \text{Elements}_d(C), m \in \text{FailureKinds}(d) \}``$ (`FailureMode_0`) with $|\mathcal{F}(C)| \le 21 \cdot |\text{Elements}(C)|$. 4. **Record Formulation**: Allocates arena records (`FMECA_Table_1`) binding effects ($``\mathcal{E}_{\text{local}}, \mathcal{E}_{\text{next}}, \mathcal{E}_{\text{end}}``$ to `Hazard_0`), $``\mathcal{D}_{\text{mech}}``$, $``\mathcal{M}_{\text{prov}}``$, and $``\Delta_R``$. Unmapped propagation or unmitigated critical failures emit `E0400`. 5. **Deterministic Reduction**: Evaluates and sorts records via $``\prec_{\text{fmeca}}``$ across work-stealing threads; guarantees bitwise parity. ---
                      The safety compiler SHALL compute Risk Priority Numbers ($RPN$), evaluating integer scores and mitigation gates. `RPN_Engine_0` MUST enforce: 1. **Ratings**: Ingests modes $``\mathcal{F} = \{ f_1, \dots, f_N \}``$ (`FailureMode_Alpha`) in `Package_0`. Modes MUST declare $\langle S(f), O(f), D(f) \rangle \in [1, 10]^3 \cap \mathbb{Z}^+$. Invalid ratings emit `E0400`. 2. **Scoring**: Evaluates $RPN(f) = S(f) \times O(f) \times D(f) \in [1, 1000]$ via exact integer arithmetic. 3. **Criticality**: Evaluates $\text{IsCritical}(f) \iff (S(f) \ge 9 \lor RPN(f) \ge 200)$, enforcing severity primacy ($S \ge 9$) and product thresholding ($RPN \ge 200$). Sets $\text{AP}(f) \in \{ \text{High}, \text{Medium}, \text{Low} \}$. 4. **Mitigation**: Critical modes ($\text{IsCritical}(f) \equiv \text{true}$) MUST bind constraint $``\mathbf{C}_{\text{mitig}}(f) \ne \emptyset``$ (`Constraint_0`). Unmitigated modes emit `E0400`. 5. **Ordering**: Sorts $\mathcal{F}$ under total order $``\succ_{\text{RPN}}``$ by $RPN \downarrow, S \downarrow, O \downarrow, D \downarrow$, and $\text{FQN}(f) \uparrow$, guaranteeing bitwise parity. ---
                      The safety compiler SHALL synthesize Run-Time Assurance (RTA) Simplex and Duplex patterns into verified control structures. ---
                      The safety compiler SHALL synthesize smooth transition interpolation for Run-Time Assurance (RTA) switching logic, interpolating `Signal_0` between `Classifier_Alpha` and `Classifier_Beta` via blender `BlendFunction_Alpha` across duration `TransTime_1` ($``T_{\text{switch}}``$). ---
                      The safety compiler SHALL formulate Control Barrier Function (CBF) forward invariance contracts for critical state constraints, ensuring synthesized and filtered control laws maintain safe set forward invariance. ---
                      The compiler SHALL implement a declarative pluggable regulatory safety profiles engine defining severity scales, required attributes, checklists, and rules without mutating core AST schemas. The pipeline MUST enforce five rules: 1. **Pluggable Architecture**: The compiler SHALL ingest profile $\mathcal{P}$ (`SafetyProfile_Alpha`) with scale $``\mathcal{S}_{\text{levels}}``$ (`SeverityScale_0`), attributes $``\mathcal{A}_{\text{required}}``$, checklists $``\mathcal{C}_{\text{checklists}}``$ (`Checklist_1`), and rules $``\mathcal{R}_{\text{rules}}``$. Unregistered profiles emit `E0400`. 2. **Metamodel Invariance**: Profile binding SHALL preserve core AST structures ($\text{Metamodel}(\mathcal{A} \mid \mathcal{P}) = \text{Metamodel}(\mathcal{A})$). Schema mutations emit `E0400`. 3. **Severity Ordering**: Profiles SHALL enforce strict total order $``s_i \prec_{\mathcal{S}} s_{i+1}``$ with rank $``\text{rank}(s_i) = i``$. Cyclic orders emit `E0400`. 4. **Monotonic Attributes**: Attributes SHALL be level-monotonic ($``s_a \prec_{\mathcal{S}} s_b \implies \mathcal{A}_{\text{required}}(\kappa, s_a) \subseteq \mathcal{A}_{\text{required}}(\kappa, s_b)``$). Missing attributes emit `E0400`. 5. **Checklists & Composition**: Verification gates $``\mathcal{C}_{\text{checklists}}``$ at threshold $``s_{\text{thresh}}``$ require evidence (`Witness_0`). Inconsistent compositions emit `E0400`. ---
                      The ICD engine of Subsystem 8 SHALL construct the $N^2$ System Interface Matrix representing component interactions, placing internal identities on diagonal cells and directed contracts in off-diagonal cells. ---
                      The compiler SHALL verify topological consistency across the $N^2$ System Interface Matrix $\mathbf{M}$ (`InterfaceMatrix_Alpha`), ensuring bidirectional channels exhibit symmetry and directed flows exhibit antisymmetry. ---
                      The compiler SHALL allocate logical signal flows into shared interconnect channels, minimizing matrix cut bandwidth while enforcing multidimensional capacity bounds. ---
                      The ICD engine of Subsystem 8 SHALL extract the canonical Master Signal Flow Dictionary `FlowDictionary_0` from AST item flows without ungrounded tokens or fallbacks. Every record in `FlowDictionary_0` MUST be an authoritative 10-tuple $``\sigma = \langle \text{ID}, S_{\text{src}}, P_{\text{src}}, S_{\text{tgt}}, P_{\text{tgt}}, \tau_{\text{payload}}, u_{\text{unit}}, f_{\text{rate}}, v_{\text{failsafe}}, \pi_{\text{protocol}} \rangle``$: interned `ID` (`Signal_Alpha`), subsystems $``S_{\text{src}}, S_{\text{tgt}}``$, ports $``P_{\text{src}}, P_{\text{tgt}}``$, payload $``\tau_{\text{payload}}``$, SI dimension $``u_{\text{unit}} \in \mathbb{Q}^7``$, rate $``f_{\text{rate}} \gt 0``$, failsafe $``v_{\text{failsafe}}``$, and protocol $``\pi_{\text{protocol}}``$. Records with $|\sigma| \ne 10$ or null tokens ($\bot$) SHALL emit `E0200`. Interface contracts MUST be valid: $``P_{\text{src}}``$ owned by $``S_{\text{src}}``$ emitting ($``\text{dir}(P_{\text{src}}) \in \{ \text{Out}, \text{InOut} \}``$); $``P_{\text{tgt}}``$ owned by $``S_{\text{tgt}}``$ ingesting ($``\text{dir}(P_{\text{tgt}}) \in \{ \text{In}, \text{InOut} \}``$); payload matching $``\tau_{\text{payload}}``$; and $``v_{\text{failsafe}} \in \text{Domain}(\tau_{\text{payload}})``$. Contract violations or $``f_{\text{rate}} \le 0``$ SHALL emit `E0204`. ---
                      The compiler SHALL synthesize Port Definition Rosters and bind port types for Level 1C Interface Control Documents (ICD), indexing declarations across hierarchies. ---
                      The ICD engine of Subsystem 8 SHALL synthesize Connection Binding Rosters mapping connections to endpoints, channels, and stream IDs, computing exact binary wire layouts. ---
                      The compiler SHALL enforce compile-time dangling port gate `DanglingGate_Alpha` over boundary ports during Level 1C ICD generation. ---
                      The compiler SHALL verify that engineering units of signal flows match connected port dimensions in $\mathbb{Q}^7$. ---
                      The compiler SHALL enforce failsafe domain validity and boundary assertion gate `FailsafeGate_Alpha` across signals in the Master Signal Flow Dictionary. ---
                      The ICD engine of Subsystem 8 SHALL verify channel bandwidth budgets, asserting aggregate traffic remains within headroom limits. ---
                      The ICD engine of Subsystem 8 SHALL verify Rate Monotonic Scheduling (RMS) schedulability for periodic task sets on interconnect buses. ---
                      The compiler SHALL verify dynamic schedulability for real-time tasks under scheduler `EDF_Scheduler_0` during Level 1C ICD synthesis. ---
                      The ICD engine of Subsystem 8 SHALL calculate framing overheads and serialization penalties for all signal flows. ---
                      The ICD engine of Subsystem 8 SHALL evaluate static timing and propagate Worst-Case Execution Times (WCET) across interconnect latency paths using analyzer `WCET_Engine_0`. ---
                      The projection engine `UUIDv5_Engine_0` of Subsystem 9 SHALL inject deterministic RFC 4122 UUIDv5 anchors into frontmatter headers of emitted specification artifacts (`Artifact_Alpha`). The pipeline MUST enforce: 1. **Canonical Topological Path**: For node $v$ (`Node_0`), the engine SHALL construct canonical path $``\mathcal{N}_{\text{topological}}(v) = p_0 \mathbin{::} \dots \mathbin{::} \text{Name}(v)``$ in `Package_0`. Paths MUST be environmental-invariant, omitting host paths and timestamps. Malformed paths emit `E0300`, bind sentinel $``\bot_{\text{anchor}}``$, and halt. 2. **RFC 4122 Hashing and Masking**: The engine SHALL compute SHA-1 over namespace `Namespace_1` ($``\text{NS}_{\text{DEAP}}``$) and UTF-8 path bytes, masking digest bytes to enforce Version 5 ($``u_6 \operatorname{AND} 0\text{x0F} \mathbin{|} 0\text{x50}``$) and Variant ($``u_8 \operatorname{AND} 0\text{x3F} \mathbin{|} 0\text{x80}``$). 3. **Frontmatter Schema**: Artifacts SHALL declare fields `id` (36-character hyphenated UUIDv5), `fqn`, `artifact_type`, `ast_handle`, and `digest`. Time-based (v1/v6/v7) and pseudo-random (v4) UUIDs are strictly prohibited; non-deterministic UUIDs emit `E0301`. 4. **Bijective Invariance**: Canonical path to UUIDv5 mapping MUST be bijective, ensuring 0-byte diff churn across regenerations. 5. **Directives**: UUIDv5 anchors (Directive 1); work-stealing ceiling $``N_{\text{max\_workers}}``$ (Directive 2); symbol interning for tokens and frontmatter keys (`id`, `fqn`, `digest`) (Directive 3); recovery on `;` and `|` halting at $``C_{\text{max\_errors}}``$ with `E0199` (Directive 4); Release budget ($< 25\text{ ms}$ for $10^4$ artifacts, $< 100\text{ MB}$) (Directive 5). Placeholders (`Package_0`, `Classifier_Alpha`, `UUIDv5_Engine_0`, `Namespace_1`, `Artifact_Alpha`, `Node_0`, `param_x : Real`) used. ---
                      The downstream projection engine of Subsystem 9 SHALL schedule features in strict bottom-up topological order via `Scheduler_1` over dependency DAG `DependencyDAG_0` ($``\mathcal{G}_{\text{dep}} = (\mathcal{F}, \mathcal{E}_{\text{dep}})``$), synthesizing leaf features before dependent composite features to eliminate forward reference gaps. ---
                      The projection engine of Subsystem 9 SHALL synthesize Epic specifications by partitioning models along top-level subsystem boundaries and projecting capability allocations. ---
                      The downstream engine of Subsystem 9 SHALL synthesize UML class and component architecture diagrams within Epic specifications using synthesizer `Diagram_Alpha`, streaming artifacts directly through `ArtifactSink_0`. ---
                      Subsystem 9 projection engine SHALL synthesize macro statecharts and operational scenarios within Epic specifications. ---
                      The projection engine of Subsystem 9 SHALL synthesize Feature specifications from the AST and enforce the 3-Layer Definition of Done (3-Layer DoD) via `DoD_Validator_0`. ---
                      The projection engine of Subsystem 9 SHALL project Feature Layer 1 domain state and primitive structural typing specifications. ---
                      Subsystem 9 SHALL project Feature Layer 2 specifications for every classifier `Feature_0`. Lowering MUST enforce: 1. **Dynamic Operations**: Operations `Operation_Alpha` lowered from actions, calcs, or functions SHALL define signatures $``op = \langle \text{Name}, \mathbf{P}_{op}, \tau_{\text{return}} \rangle``$. Parameters $``\mathbf{P}_{op} = \langle (p_i, \text{dir}_i, \tau_i) \rangle``$ MUST declare directions $``\text{dir}_i \in \{\text{In}, \text{Out}, \text{InOut}\}``$ and types $``\tau_i \in \mathcal{V}_{\text{AST}}``$. Missing directions or duplicate names emit `E0300`; untyped parameters or return mismatches emit `E0308`. 2. **State Machines**: Machine `StateMachine_0` SHALL formalize states $s \in \mathcal{S}(F)$ and transitions $``t = \langle s_{\text{source}}, e_{\text{trigger}}, g_{\text{guard}}, s_{\text{target}} \rangle \in \mathcal{T}(F)``$. Initial pseudostates MUST have one outgoing transition with trigger $\epsilon$. Unresolved states (`State_Missing`) emit `E0300`. 3. **Guards and Actions**: Guards $``g_{\text{guard}}``$ MUST evaluate side-effect free to `Boolean` (violations emit `E0308`). Overlapping guards on identical triggers emit `E0300`. Action hooks `Action_1` MUST bind operations in $\mathcal{O}(F)$. 4. **Sentinels**: Violations record diagnostics in sink $``\mathcal{D}_{\text{sink}}``$, bind sentinels $``\bot_{\text{op}}``$ or $``\bot_{\text{trans}}``$, and continue lowering. 5. **Directives**: UUIDv5 anchors (Directive 1); work-stealing ceiling $``N_{\text{max\_workers}}``$ (Directive 2); symbol interning (Directive 3); recovery on `;`, `|`, `}` halting at $``C_{\text{max\_errors}}``$ with `E0199` (Directive 4); Release budget ($< 25\text{ ms}$ for $10^4$ nodes, $< 100\text{ MB}$) (Directive 5). Placeholders (`Package_0`, `Feature_0`, `StateMachine_0`, `Operation_Alpha`, `Action_1`, `State_0`, `State_Missing`, `param_x : Real`) used. ---
                      Subsystem 9 SHALL project Feature Layer 3 physical dynamics, Kirchhoff network laws, and conservative equations for every classifier `Feature_0`. ---
                      Subsystem 9 SHALL project User Story specifications for feature `Feature_0`. ---
                      The downstream projection engine of Subsystem 9 SHALL project formal Use Case specifications from the compilation unit abstract syntax tree. ---
                      Subsystem 9 SHALL project Engineering Tasks from AST definitions into a Work Breakdown Structure (WBS) rooted at `WBS_0`. ---
                      Subsystem 9 SHALL perform bidirectional incremental AST patching and synchronization via `SyncEngine_Alpha` across upstream AST models and downstream projections against base AST $``T_{\text{base}}``$. ---
                      Subsystem 9 SHALL maintain bidirectional traceability across AST entities and projected artifacts, executing cascade `Cascade_1` over `TraceGraph_Alpha` ($``\mathcal{G}_{\text{trace}} = (V, E_{\text{trace}})``$) upon AST mutation. ---
                      The projection engine of Subsystem 9 SHALL reconcile divergence between upstream AST models and downstream projections via `ConflictResolver_Alpha`. Reconciliations MUST resolve base $B$, upstream $U$, and downstream $D$: 1. **Three-Way Extraction**: For $``e \in C_{\text{diff}}``$ in `Package_0`, computes $``\Delta_U(e) = (U(e) \ne B(e))``$ and $``\Delta_D(e) = (D(e) \ne B(e))``$. Malformed schema records emit `E0300`. 2. **Automated Policies**: Disjoint mutations ($``\Delta_U \land \neg \Delta_D``$ or $``\neg \Delta_U \land \Delta_D``$) accept edits under `Policy_1`. Convergent edits ($``\Delta_U \land \Delta_D \land U = D``$) merge into $``M_{\text{resolved}}``$ without conflict. 3. **Contradictory Divergence**: Incompatible concurrent edits ($``\Delta_U \land \Delta_D \land U \ne D``$) under `Policy_Alpha` MUST fail closed, emitting `E0315` (`DivergenceConflictViolation`) and binding sentinel $``\bot_{\text{resolve}}``$. 4. **Sentinels and Recovery**: Faults record in $``\mathcal{D}_{\text{sink}}``$, bind $``\bot_{\text{resolve}}``$, and recover on delimiters (`;`, `###`, `---`), halting at $``C_{\text{max\_errors}}``$ with `E0199`. 5. **Directives**: UUIDv5 anchors (Directive 1); work-stealing pool $``N_{\text{max\_workers}}``$ (Directive 2); symbol interning in $``\mathcal{S}_{\text{intern}}``$ (Directive 3); delimiter recovery halts at $``C_{\text{max\_errors}}``$ with `E0199` (Directive 4); release performance isolation (Directive 5). Placeholders (`Package_0`, `ConflictResolver_Alpha`, `Divergence_0`, `Policy_1`, `param_x : Real`) used. ---
                      The downstream projection engine of Subsystem 9 SHALL synthesize a specification manifest (`Manifest_Alpha`) and verification ledger (`HashLedger_0`) covering all emitted artifacts ($\mathcal{A}$). ---
                      The backend of Subsystem 10 SHALL lower actions, statecharts, and constraints into SSA representation `LumiIR_Alpha`. ---
                      Subsystem 10 SHALL enforce value semantics, typed slots, immutable SSA bindings, and state transformers for `MemoryModel_Alpha`. ---
                      The emission engine of Subsystem 10 SHALL stream code artifacts ($\mathcal{A}$) through writer sinks (`WriterSink_Alpha`) via `StreamEmitter_1`. Monolithic file accumulation is strictly prohibited. ---
                      The persistence engine of Subsystem 10 SHALL persist artifacts ($\mathcal{A}$) through manifest `CodegenManifest_Alpha` via fingerprint `ArtifactFingerprint_0` using XXH3 hashing. ---
                      The simulation engine of Subsystem 10 SHALL synthesize discrete fixed-step Forward Euler blocks (`EulerSolver_Alpha`) for continuous dynamical models (`Package_0::Classifier_Alpha`). ---
                      Subsystem 10 SHALL execute register allocation and instruction scheduling over LUMI IR basic blocks (`Block_0`). ---
                      Subsystem 10 SHALL evaluate state-space models and synthesize RK4 solvers via `StateSpaceEngine_Alpha`. ---
                      Subsystem 10 SHALL synthesize idiomatic, zero-allocation ROS2 node architectures (`RosNode_Alpha`) from AST components (`Classifier_Alpha`). ---
                      Subsystem 10 SHALL synthesize OMG DDS IDL schemas (`IDL_0`) and CDR codecs (`CDR_Codec_1`) from AST structures (`Struct_Alpha`) via `DdsGenerator_Alpha`. ---
                      Subsystem 10 SHALL emit freestanding, zero-allocation C++20 header (`.hpp`) and source (`.cpp`) translation units (`TranslationUnit_0`) from classifiers (`Classifier_Alpha`) via `CppEmitter_Alpha`. ---
                      Subsystem 10 SHALL synthesize MISRA C99 source (`.c`) and header (`.h`) files via `MisraEmitter_Alpha` from AST classifiers (`Classifier_Alpha`). ---
                      Subsystem 10 SHALL synthesize freestanding, zero-allocation C99 and C++20 MMIO register headers (`.h`, `.hpp`) from peripheral blocks (`RegBlock_0`) via `RegisterHeaderGen_Alpha`. ---
                      Subsystem 10 SHALL synthesize formal verification scripts (`.m`) targeting verification engines (MATLAB / SLDV) from AST classifiers (`Classifier_Alpha`) via `ProofSynthesizer_Alpha`. ---
                      Subsystem 10 SHALL synthesize SMT-LIB2 (`.smt2`) scripts targeting first-order SMT solvers via `SMTEncoder_Alpha`. ---
                      Subsystem 10 SHALL persist artifacts via `FilePersistence_Alpha`. ---
                      Subsystem 11 SHALL emit structured diagnostic records via `DiagnosticEngine_Alpha`. ---
                      `TaxonomyEngine_Alpha` SHALL partition diagnostics into five disjoint taxonomy ranges: Ingestion/Lexer (`E0100`--`E0199`), Metamodel/Typing (`E0200`--`E0299`), Metrology/Conservation (`E0300`--`E0399`), Spatio-Temporal/Safety (`E0400`--`E0499`), and Backend/Emission (`E0500`--`E0599`). Unclassified codes MUST NOT be emitted. ---
                      Subsystem 11 SHALL execute reverse synchronization via `ProseGate_Alpha` and `Reconciler_0`. ---
                      Subsystem 11 SHALL parse and mutate CommonMark documents non-destructively via `MarkdownParser_Alpha` and `MutationEngine_0`. ---
                      Subsystem 11 SHALL detect drift and enforce zero-divergence bijective synchronization between schemas and artifacts via `DriftDetector_Alpha` and `ModelSync_0`. ---
                      Subsystem 12 SHALL provide a headless CLI and deterministic subcommand interface via `CliEngine_Alpha`. ---
                      Subsystem 12 SHALL enforce dual performance gates bounding latency and RSS via `AssuranceGate_Alpha`, `LatencyMonitor_0`, and `RssTracker_1`. Pipeline MUST enforce: 1. **Dual Gates**: For model `Package_0` ($|\text{Nodes}| \le 10{,}000$), `LatencyMonitor_0` SHALL assert latency $``p_{99}(\Delta t) \lt 25.0\text{ ms}``$; `RssTracker_1` SHALL assert memory $``\text{RSS}_{\text{peak}} \lt 104{,}857{,}600\text{ bytes}``$ (100.0 MB). 2. **Dedicated Isolation**: Gates SHALL evaluate in Release mode (`--release`) under dedicated harnesses isolated from CI tests ($``K_{\text{warmup}} \ge 50``$, $M \ge 1{,}000$ iterations). 3. **Memory Sampling**: `RssTracker_1` SHALL sample OS memory at phase boundaries across arenas, interned strings, tables, and diagnostics without unmanaged bloat. 4. **Termination**: The engine SHALL guarantee non-panicking termination. Breaches MUST exit with code 1 and emit `E0196`. Sampling faults MUST emit `E0300`, bind $``\bot_{\text{gate}}``$, and fail closed. 5. **Directives**: UUIDv5 anchors via $``\text{OID}_{\text{DEAP}}``$ (Directive 1); work-stealing pool $``N_{\text{max\_workers}}``$ (Directive 2); symbol interning (Directive 3); recovery on `;` halting at $``C_{\text{max\_errors}}``$ with `E0199` (Directive 4); Release budget ($< 25.0\text{ ms}$, $< 100.0\text{ MB}$) (Directive 5). Placeholders (`Package_0`, `Classifier_Alpha`, `Port_1`, `param_x : Real`) used. ---
                      Subsystem 12 SHALL discharge formal proof obligations (`ProofObligation_Alpha`) from contracts via `SmtSolver_0`. ---
                      Subsystem 12 SHALL verify panic-free execution and AST invariant preservation via `FuzzerEngine_Alpha` and `InvariantChecker_1`. ---
                      Subsystem 12 SHALL execute 4-pass semantic parity verification via `ParityVerifier_Alpha`. --- */
