                      Calculation lowering, typing, and dependency analysis execute strictly within Complexity Class $\mathbf{P}$. For $``V = |\mathcal{C}_{\text{calc}}| + |\mathcal{U}_{\text{calc}}|``$ nodes and $``E = |E_{\text{calc}}|``$ dependency edges: - Node allocation and symbol interning execute in amortized $O(1)$ time per node ($O(V)$). - Parameter directionality and covariant subtyping evaluate in $O(1)$ checks via precomputed bitsets (tractable fragment of NP-3). - Purity AST inspection traverses expression trees in linear time $O(V)$. - Dependency acyclicity and evaluation ordering evaluate in $O(V + E)$ time using Tarjan's SCC or Kahn's algorithm. - Multiplicity interval validation executes in $O(1)$ scalar checks ($O(V)$). Total sequential complexity is $O(V + E)$. Parallel package lowering scales as $``O((V + E) / N_{\text{max\_workers}} + \log N_{\text{max\_workers}})``$. While equational constraint solving is NP-complete (NP-4 in REQ-0083), functional calculation DAG evaluation remains strictly polynomial. ---
