                      - **Complexity Class:** Class $\mathbf{P}$ (Deterministic Polynomial Time). - **Asymptotic Bound:** $``O(|T_{\text{types}}|)``$ typing projection ($``|T_{\text{types}}| = \sum |\mathbf{A}_F|``$). AST traversal runs in $``O(|T_{\text{types}}|)``$ time. Type, $\mathbb{Q}^7$ unit, and bound checks run in $O(1)$ time. Space: $``O(|T_{\text{types}}|)``$. Pool: $``O(|T_{\text{types}}| / N_{\text{max\_workers}} + \log N_{\text{max\_workers}})``$. - **Tractable Subclass and Frontier:** N/A (Deterministic P). Avoids NP-3 linearization (REQ-0061), NP-6 flow solving (REQ-0105), and NP-8 SMT solving (REQ-0197). ---
                      - **Complexity Class:** Class $\mathbf{P}$ (Deterministic Polynomial Time). - **Asymptotic Bound:** $O(|S| + |T|)$ logic and state machine lowering ($|S| = |\mathcal{O}| + |\mathcal{S}|$, $|T| = |\mathbf{P}| + |\mathcal{T}|$). Work-stealing scales as $``O((|S| + |T|)/N_{\text{max\_workers}} + \log N_{\text{max\_workers}})``$. Arena: $O(|S| + |T|)$. - **Tractable Subclass and Frontier:** N/A (Deterministic P). Linear lowering bypasses NP-5 reachability (REQ-0124) and NP-8 (REQ-0197). ---
                      - **Complexity Class:** Class $\mathbf{P}$ (Deterministic Polynomial Time). - **Asymptotic Bound:** $O(|E|)$ topological Kirchhoff conservation ($|E|$ flows). Incidence and flow sums evaluate in $O(|E|)$ time. Cycle checks run in $O(|E|)$ on planar graphs. Work-stealing scales as $``O(|E|/N_{\text{max\_workers}} + \log N_{\text{max\_workers}})``$. Arena: $O(|J| + |E|)$. - **Tractable Subclass and Frontier:** N/A (Deterministic P). Linear balance avoids continuous LCP solving in NP-6 (REQ-0105). ---
                      - **Complexity Class:** Class $\mathbf{P}$ (Deterministic Polynomial Time). - **Asymptotic Bound:** $O(|U|)$ story cataloging ($|U| = \sum |\mathcal{U}(F)|$). Ingestion and checks take $O(1)$ time via symbol interning. 4-tier MoSCoW distribution sort takes $O(|U|)$ time. Arena storage: $O(|U|)$. Work-stealing: $``O(|U| / N_{\text{max\_workers}} + \log N_{\text{max\_workers}})``$. - **Tractable Subclass and Frontier:** N/A (Deterministic P). Linear story cataloging avoids NP-2 bin packing (REQ-0147) and NP-8 invariant proving (REQ-0197). ---
                      - **Complexity Class:** Class $\mathbf{P}$ (Deterministic Polynomial Time). - **Asymptotic Bound:** $O(|UC| \cdot \text{steps})$ use case scenario trace ($``|UC| = |\mathcal{U}_{\text{proj}}|``$, $``\text{steps} = \max |S_{\text{primary}}|``$). AST traversal executes in $O(|UC|)$ time; linear step validation and branch target resolution execute in $O(\text{steps})$ time. Parallel pool: $``O((|UC| \cdot \text{steps})/N_{\text{max\_workers}} + \log N_{\text{max\_workers}})``$. Arena memory: $O(|UC| \cdot \text{steps})$. - **Tractable Subclass and Frontier:** N/A (Deterministic P). Linear scenario tracing bypasses NP-1 interval solving (REQ-0117), NP-5 state reachability (REQ-0124), and NP-8 SMT solving (REQ-0197). ---
                      - **Complexity Class:** Class $\mathbf{P}$ (Deterministic Polynomial Time). - **Asymptotic Bound:** $O(|T|)$ task decomposition ($``|T| = |\mathcal{T}_{\text{tasks}}|``$). Bottom-up effort aggregation and DoD validation run in $O(1)$ time per node ($O(|T|)$ total). Arena: $O(|T|)$. Work-stealing: $``O(|T| / N_{\text{max\_workers}} + \log N_{\text{max\_workers}})``$. - **Tractable Subclass and Frontier:** N/A (Deterministic P). Linear tree decomposition bypasses NP-2 bin packing (REQ-0147) and NP-4 hitting sets (REQ-0135). ---
                      - **Complexity Class:** Class $\mathbf{P}$. - **Asymptotic Bound:** $O(|V|)$ 3-way AST diff and patch ($``|V| = |V_{\text{base}}| + |V_{\text{upstream}}| + |V_{\text{downstream}}|``$). Traversal and UUIDv5 diffing run in $O(|V|)$ time. Work-stealing scales as $``O(|V| / N_{\text{max\_workers}} + \log N_{\text{max\_workers}})``$. Arena memory scales as $O(|V|)$. - **Tractable Subclass and Frontier:** N/A (Deterministic P). Fixed-anchor alignment avoids NP-hard subtree isomorphism and NP-8 SMT solving (REQ-0197). ---
                      - **Complexity Class:** Class $\mathbf{P}$ (Polynomial Time). - **Asymptotic Bound:** $O(|V| + |E|)$ BFS dirty cascade over $``\mathcal{G}_{\text{trace}}``$. Bitset lookups run in $O(1)$ time. Scaling: $``O((|V| + |E|) / N_{\text{max\_workers}} + \log N_{\text{max\_workers}})``$. Arena: $O(|V| + |E|)$. - **Tractable Subclass and Frontier:** N/A (Deterministic P). Linear BFS avoids NP-hard feedback sets, NP-1 intervals (REQ-0117), NP-2 packing (REQ-0147), and NP-8 SMT (REQ-0197). ---
                      - **Complexity Class:** Class $\mathbf{P}$ (Deterministic Polynomial Time). - **Asymptotic Bound:** $``O(|C_{\text{diff}}|)``$ 3-way conflict resolution ($``|C_{\text{diff}}| = |\text{Dom}(B) \cup \text{Dom}(U) \cup \text{Dom}(D)|``$). Diff evaluation and dispatch run in $O(1)$ time per element. Work-stealing pool scales as $``O(|C_{\text{diff}}| / N_{\text{max\_workers}} + \log N_{\text{max\_workers}})``$. Arena memory: $``O(|C_{\text{diff}}|)``$. - **Tractable Subclass and Frontier:** N/A (Deterministic P). Local 3-way reconciliation avoids NP-complete graph coloring (REQ-0180) and SMT solving (REQ-0197). ---
                      - **Complexity Class:** Class $\mathbf{P}$ (Deterministic Polynomial Time). - **Asymptotic Bound:** $O(|\mathcal{A}| \cdot \text{size})$ for artifacts $\mathcal{A}$ of average byte size $\text{size}$. Streaming evaluation executes in $``O(S_a)``$; sorting takes $O(|\mathcal{A}| \log |\mathcal{A}|)$; root hashing takes $O(|\mathcal{A}| \cdot K)$ ($K = 32$ bytes). Work-stealing scales as $``O((|\mathcal{A}| \cdot \text{size})/N_{\text{max\_workers}} + \log N_{\text{max\_workers}})``$. Arena space is $O(|\mathcal{A}|)$. - **Tractable Subclass and Frontier:** N/A (Deterministic P). Ledger hashing avoids NP-1 intervals (REQ-0117), NP-2 packing (REQ-0147), and NP-8 solving (REQ-0197). ---
                      - **Complexity Class:** Class $\mathbf{P}$ (Deterministic Polynomial Time). - **Asymptotic Bound:** $``O(|B| + |E_{\text{cfg}}|)``$ CFG and dominance traversal ($``|B| = |\mathcal{B}|, |E_{\text{cfg}}| = |\mathcal{E}_{\text{cfg}}|``$). Lowering runs in $``O(|B| + |E_{\text{cfg}}| + |I|)``$ for $|I|$ instructions. Dominator trees take $``O(|B| + |E_{\text{cfg}}|)``$; SSA checks take $O(1)$ per use. Work-stealing scales as $``O((|B| + |E_{\text{cfg}}|)/N_{\text{max\_workers}} + \log N_{\text{max\_workers}})``$. Arena memory is $``O(|B| + |E_{\text{cfg}}| + |I|)``$. - **Tractable Subclass and Frontier:** N/A (Deterministic P). SSA lowering avoids NP-7 coloring (REQ-0180), NP-5 reachability (REQ-0124), and NP-8 solving (REQ-0197). ---
                      - **Complexity Class:** Class $\mathbf{P}$. - **Asymptotic Bound:** $O(|I|)$ alias-free verification over instructions $|I|$ and slots $``|\mathcal{S}_{\text{slot}}|``$. Slot checks take $``O(|\mathcal{S}_{\text{slot}}|)``$; SSA checks take $O(1)$; dominance checks take $``O(|I| + |\mathcal{E}_{\text{cfg}}|)``$. Arena space is $``O(|I| + |\mathcal{S}_{\text{slot}}|)``$; work-stealing is $``O(|I| / N_{\text{max\_workers}} + \log N_{\text{max\_workers}})``$. - **Tractable Subclass and Frontier:** N/A (Deterministic P). Bypasses NP-1 (REQ-0117) and NP-7 (REQ-0180). ---
                      - **Complexity Class:** Class $\mathbf{P}$ (Deterministic Polynomial Time). - **Asymptotic Bound:** $O(|A|)$ streaming I/O with $O(1)$ memory for $a \in \mathcal{A}$ of size $|A|$. Buffering runs in $O(|\beta|)$ with $``\lceil |A| / B_{\text{max\_chunk\_size}} \rceil``$ flushes. Work-stealing scales as $``O((|V| + |E| + |A|)/N_{\text{max\_workers}} + \log N_{\text{max\_workers}})``$. Arena space is $O(|V|)$. - **Tractable Subclass and Frontier:** N/A (Deterministic P). Avoids NP-1 intervals (REQ-0117), NP-2 packing (REQ-0147), NP-7 registers (REQ-0180), and NP-8 solving (REQ-0197). ---
                      - **Complexity Class:** Class $\mathbf{P}$ (Deterministic Polynomial Time). - **Asymptotic Bound:** $O(|B|)$ hashing ($> 10\text{ GB/s}$) per artifact. Manifest emission for $K = |\mathcal{A}|$ artifacts takes $``O(N_{\text{bytes}} + K \log K)``$. Work-stealing scales as $``O(N_{\text{bytes}} / N_{\text{max\_workers}} + K \log K)``$. Arena space is $O(K)$. - **Tractable Subclass and Frontier:** N/A (Deterministic P). Avoids NP-1 intervals (REQ-0117), NP-2 packing (REQ-0147), and NP-8 solving (REQ-0197). ---
                      - **Complexity Class:** Class $\mathbf{P}$ (Deterministic Polynomial Time). - **Asymptotic Bound:** $O(n)$ update per timestep ($n=\dim(\mathbf{x})$); dense updates take $O(n^2+nm)$ ($m=\dim(\mathbf{u})$); horizon over $K$ steps takes $O(K\cdot n)$. Work-stealing takes $``O((M\cdot K\cdot n)/N_{\text{max\_workers}}+\log N_{\text{max\_workers}})``$. Arena space is $O(n)$. - **Tractable Subclass and Frontier:** N/A (Deterministic P). Evaluates arithmetic without NP-1 intervals (REQ-0117) or NP-8 solving (REQ-0197). ---
                      - **Complexity Class:** NP-Hard (NP-7 Register Allocation and DAG Scheduling). - **Asymptotic Bound:** Kempe allocation executes in $O(|V|^2)$ and critical-path list scheduling executes in $``O(|I| + |E_{\text{dep}}|)``$. Liveness analysis takes $O(|\mathcal{B}| \cdot |V|)$. Work-stealing scales as $``O(|V|^2 / N_{\text{max\_workers}})``$. Arena footprint is $``O(|V| + |E| + |I| + |E_{\text{dep}}|)``$. - **Tractable Subclass and Frontier:** NP-7 (Chaitin Graph K-Coloring and Latency-Constrained DAG Instruction Scheduling). Kempe simplification with optimistic spilling and single-pass list traversal guarantee polynomial tractability. ---
                      - **Complexity Class:** Class $\mathbf{P}$. - **Asymptotic Bound:** State evaluation runs in $O(n^2)$ time per step; RK4 update takes $O(n)$ time. Offline ZOH discretization requires $O(n^3)$ operations. Work-stealing scales as $``O(S \cdot n^2 / N_{\text{max\_workers}} + \log N_{\text{max\_workers}})``$. Memory is $O(n^2)$. - **Tractable Subclass and Frontier:** N/A (Deterministic P). Stepping is deterministic without branching, avoiding NP-1 and NP-8. ---
                      - **Complexity Class:** Class $\mathbf{P}$ (Deterministic Polynomial Time). - **Asymptotic Bound:** $O(|P|)$ where $``|P|=\sum_{C\in\mathcal{C}}|\mathcal{P}(C)|``$. Lowering, QoS derivation, and topic checks take $O(1)$ per port ($O(|P|)$ total). Interconnect RxO checks take $O(|\mathcal{K}|)$ ($|\mathcal{K}|\le|P|$). Work-stealing scales as $``O(|P|/N_{\text{max\_workers}}+\log N_{\text{max\_workers}})``$. Arena space is $O(|P|)$. - **Tractable Subclass and Frontier:** N/A (Deterministic P). Bypasses NP-1 intervals (REQ-0117), NP-2 packing (REQ-0147), and NP-8 solving (REQ-0197). ---
                      - **Complexity Class:** Class $\mathbf{P}$ (Deterministic Polynomial Time). - **Asymptotic Bound:** Schema emission runs in $O(|S|)$ for fields $``|S|=\sum|\mathbf{\Phi}_S|``$. Serialization runs in $O(|B|)$ for wire length $|B|$. Work-stealing scales as $``O(|S|/N_{\text{max\_workers}})``$. Space is $O(|S|)$ with $O(1)$ heap. - **Tractable Subclass and Frontier:** N/A (Deterministic P). Bypasses NP-1 intervals (REQ-0117), NP-2 packing (REQ-0147), and NP-8 solving (REQ-0197). ---
                      - **Complexity Class:** Class $\mathbf{P}$. - **Asymptotic Bound:** Emission runs in $``O(|V_{\text{AST}}|)``$ time for nodes $``V_{\text{AST}}``$. Traversal is $``O(|V_{\text{AST}}| + |E_{\text{AST}}|)``$, formatting is $O(|A|)$, and chunk streaming is $O(1)$. Work-stealing scales as $``O((|V_{\text{AST}}| + |A|) / N_{\text{max\_workers}} + \log N_{\text{max\_workers}})``$. Memory is $``O(|V_{\text{AST}}| + |E_{\text{AST}}|)``$. - **Tractable Subclass and Frontier:** N/A (Deterministic P). Lowers syntax directly, avoiding NP-1 and NP-8. ---
                      - **Complexity Class:** Class $\mathbf{P}$. - **Asymptotic Bound:** $``O(|V_{\text{AST}}|)``$ for AST nodes $``V_{\text{AST}}``$. Emission and layout checks run in $``O(|V_{\text{AST}}|)``$ time. Cycle checks take $``O(|\mathcal{F}_{\text{c99}}| + |\mathcal{E}_{\text{call}}|) \subseteq O(|V_{\text{AST}}|)``$. Work-stealing scales as $``O(|V_{\text{AST}}| / N_{\text{max\_workers}} + \log N_{\text{max\_workers}})``$; arena is $``O(|V_{\text{AST}}|)``$. - **Tractable Subclass and Frontier:** N/A (Deterministic P). DAG traversal avoids NP-1 intervals (REQ-0117), NP-2 packing (REQ-0147), and NP-8 solving (REQ-0197). ---
                      - **Complexity Class:** Class $\mathbf{P}$ (Deterministic Polynomial Time). - **Asymptotic Bound:** $``O(|R_{\text{registers}}|)``$ register header emission. Lowering takes $O(1)$ per register ($``O(|R_{\text{registers}}|)``$ total). Offset checks take $``O(|R_{\text{registers}}|)``$. Work-stealing scales as $``O(|R_{\text{registers}}| / N_{\text{max\_workers}} + \log N_{\text{max\_workers}})``$. Arena space is $``O(|R_{\text{registers}}|)``$. - **Tractable Subclass and Frontier:** N/A (Deterministic P). Avoids NP-1 intervals (REQ-0117), NP-2 packing (REQ-0147), NP-7 registers (REQ-0180), and NP-8 solving (REQ-0197). ---
